{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_37","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"rg -n 'WARN|ERROR|\\\\\"'$div|'\"\\\\\"'$mod'\"' cores/bench/generated/timing/gowin_p0/gw.log | head -40; cat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":"89:WARN  (PR1014) : Generic routing resource will be used to clock signal 'clock_d' by the specified constraint. And then it may lead to the excessive delay or skew\n# Implementation notes\n\nImplemented the hypothesis in `rtl/alu.sv` and extended `test/test_alu.py`.\n\n- Replaced the four real division/remainder operators with one combinational\n  unsigned restoring divider. Its 32 generated stages have k-bit trial and\n  remainder signals and one k+1-bit zero-extended subtraction each. The\n  subtraction's borrow bit and a reduction of the divisor's upper bits decide\n  whether to accept the subtraction. The final upper-bit predicate is constant\n  true. Quotient bits and the final remainder come from the same network.\n- Signed DIV/REM convert inputs to unsigned magnitudes and restore quotient\n  and remainder signs separately. Division by zero and INT_MIN/-1 are selected\n  explicitly. The divider is excluded under RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS; every original\n  ALTOPS formula and multiplication expression is unchanged.\n- Added deterministic differential checks around all 32 power-of-two boundaries,\n  high-bit divisors, mixed signs, zero divisors, signed overflow, and random\n  full-width/small-divisor inputs. Fixed operands are checked through successive\n  DIVU/REM/DIV/REMU changes. Nonzero unsigned results also satisfy a=q*b+r and r<b.\n  Existing checks remain intact; stale iterative-divider comments were corrected.\n- Added a guarded core_pkg.sv include to alu.sv so the requested alphabetical\n  glob lint command finds pipeline types before core.sv. The normal package-first\n  source lists skip this include, including cocotb builds without an include path.\n  This is the only deviation from the planned datapath/test changes.\n\nPipeline registers, latency, forwarding, bus handshakes, RVFI, all other RTL,\nsource lists, core.yaml, and evaluation contracts are unchanged. The actual\ncore.yaml declares nret=1, so local checks use its existing single-channel\nwrapper rather than the prompt's generic NRET=2 description.\n\nValidation:\n\n- Requested Verilator glob lint: PASS, no warnings, both real and ALTOPS builds.\n- `pytest -v cores/bench/test/test_alu.py`: PASS, all 27 cocotb tests.\n- `pytest -v cores/bench/test/`: PASS, all five runners (including ALU and pipeline).\n- `RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench JOBS=8 bash formal/run_all.sh`:\n  PASS, 53 passed / 0 failed on the first run, no formal fix attempts.\n  Revalidation after the guarded include also passed 53/53 checks.\n- `make cosim TARGET=bench NRET=1`: PASS for selftest RVFI comparison with and\n  without random bus stalls, and stalled CoreMark canonical CRC validation.\n  Rebuilt and passed again after the guarded include.\n- `make timing TARGET=bench`: running (Gowin placement option 0).\n\nConcerns: the design still has a combinational 32-stage arithmetic path and\nsigned input/output carry logic. Area and timing gains must be measured with\nGowin. The ordinary formal gate uses ALTOPS and does not prove real arithmetic;\nthe actual divider is exercised by the differential ALU tests and cosimulation.\nThe slow formal-deep suite has not been run locally.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
