{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_91", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md'", "aggregated_output": "# Shared AND/OR/XOR result family\n\nImplemented the proposed micro-optimization exactly in `rtl/alu.sv`:\nparallel scalar `xor_en` and `and_en` decodes feed two masked word terms,\nwhich are ORed into `logic_result`. One grouped AND/OR/XOR case arm selects\nthat result. There is no additional bitwise-operation result selector.\nAll other case arms, operation encodings, ports, real inactive M-extension\noutputs and exact operation-specific ALTOPS formulas are unchanged. No\npipeline, forwarding, arithmetic-unit, decoder, predictor or RVFI logic was\nmodified.\n\nExtended `test/test_alu.py` while retaining all existing checks. Added\nzero/all-ones and alternating-pattern cross products, walking-one and\nwalking-zero pairs, and deterministic random pairs. Fixed-operand operation\ntransitions cover AND/OR/XOR in both directions and interleave every other\n5-bit opcode, including shifts, ADD/SUB, comparisons, LUI, M-extension and\nall default-zero encodings. Both normal and ALTOPS builds run these checks.\n\nLocal checks:\n\n- Required Verilator lint command: PASS, no warnings.\n- `pytest -q cores/bench/test/`: PASS, 13 runners / 119 cocotb tests;\n  includes 12 normal ALU tests, 12 ALTOPS ALU tests, the unchanged 35-test\n  pipeline suite, decoder and registered arithmetic suites in both modes.\n- `make cosim TARGET=bench NRET=1`: PASS, selftest full RVFI comparison both\n  with and without random memory stalls, plus stalled CoreMark validation.\n  The existing validator requires all canonical CRCs (e9f5, e714, 1fd7,\n  8e3a, fcaf), the literal `Correct operation validated.`, and no OOB flag.\n- `run_coremark_ipc` using the built bench simulator: PASS, 10 iterations,\n  exactly 4,296,444 start/stop MMIO-bracketed cycles; 2.3275061888389562e-6\n  iterations/cycle. This validator also checked CRCs, the validation literal,\n  EBREAK completion, OOB status and both marker brackets.\n- `RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench JOBS=8 bash formal/run_all.sh`:\n  PASS on the initial implementation, 53 passed / 0 failed on the first\n  invocation. No counterexamples, fixes or retries.\n- Gowin canonical timing across placement options 0, 1 and 2: PASS placement,\n  Fmax 87.424 / 82.342 / 82.342 MHz; median 82.342 MHz. Vendor resources:\n  3,821 logic cells, 1,090 registers, 40 LUT-RAM, 4 BSRAM, 2 DSP; 12 logic\n  levels. This is a regression from the supplied champion's 93.817 MHz\n  median and 3,675 logic cells.\n- Fitness from that measured median and validated CoreMark interval:\n  191.65 iterations/sec. The required >98.133 MHz and >228.405 iterations/sec\n  thresholds are NOT met. The Boolean factoring alone did not improve\n  fitness, despite preserving the exact instruction schedule/cycle count.\n\nThe Education synthesis `.vg` is encrypted, so a separate Gowin build of\nthe initial RTL with the documented `-gen_verilog_sim_netlist 1` reporting\noption produced a readable post-route `.vo`. Its timing/resources exactly\nmatched canonical placement option 0. Netlist inspection found only 11\ncomplete shared-function LUT4s (bits 4, 5, 7, 8, 10, 11, 14, 15, 24, 25,\n26), with `INIT=16'h5CCF`; the inverted truth table was checked against\nall 16 combinations of a, b, xor_en and and_en. Other bits were split or\nabsorbed into surrounding logic. For example, bit 1 had separate XOR and\nAND LUT2s, `cpu/u_ex/n4007_s17` (`INIT=4'h6`) and `n4007_s18`\n(`INIT=4'h8`). The intended uniform single-LUT4 mapping was not retained.\n\nA follow-up measurement is in progress with Gowin's documented\n`syn_keep = 1` attributes on the two scalar enables and shared result word.\nThis preserves synthesis boundaries without changing the Boolean function,\noperation case arms, cycle behavior or any module interface. Final results\nand the selected RTL will be recorded after measurement.\n\nNo architectural deviations. Notes are kept under\n`cores/bench/` to respect the target-only edit scope. No evaluation-contract\nsources or other cores were edited. Real arithmetic was not changed, so\nthe slow `formal-deep` multiplier/divider gate was not rerun.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
