{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_38", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"git diff --check\npython3 -c 'import re, subprocess; from pathlib import Path; paths = subprocess.check_output([\\\"git\\\", \\\"diff\\\", \\\"--name-only\\\"], text=True).splitlines(); extra = subprocess.check_output([\\\"git\\\", \\\"ls-files\\\", \\\"--others\\\", \\\"--exclude-standard\\\"], text=True).splitlines(); allowed = re.compile(r\\\"\"'^cores/bench/(rtl/[''^/]+'\"\\\\.sv|test/test_[\"'^/]+'\"\\\\.py)\"'$\"); invalid = [p for p in paths + extra if not allowed.fullmatch(p)]; assert not invalid, invalid; assert Path(\"cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\").is_file(); print(\"Scope check: PASS;\",len(paths),\"allowed changed files; notes present\")'\"'\ncat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"", "aggregated_output": "Scope check: PASS; 7 allowed changed files; notes present\n# Aligned internal RV32M operation tags\n\nImplemented the proposed encoding exactly: MUL/MULH/MULHSU/MULHU are\n16/17/18/19 and DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU are 20/21/22/23. RV32I operations remain\n0..10 and the operation field remains five bits. EX classifies multiply\nwith alu_op[4:2] == 3'b100 and division/remainder with == 3'b101, so tags\n24..31 are excluded explicitly.\n\nOnly core_pkg.sv and ex_stage.sv changed in RTL. Decoder validation,\narithmetic dispatch, ALTOPS formulas, signedness, pipeline bundles,\nlaunch/response ownership, saved metadata, bypass enables and priorities,\ntrap controls, retirement, nret=1 and top-level ports are unchanged.\nAuditing RTL consumers found no numeric old-tag comparisons outside the\nconstant definitions being replaced.\n\nUpdated M-operation aliases locally in the five specified test modules;\nshared _helpers.py is untouched. Existing arithmetic vectors and legality,\nlatency, backpressure, saved metadata and bypass assertions are retained.\nAdded checks for zero ALU results on unused tags 11..15 and 24..31 in real\nand ALTOPS modes, no EX arithmetic occupancy/launch on those tags, and\nalternating multiply/divide families covering all eight recoded operations\nwith exact results, latency, held responses and completion metadata.\n\nNo architectural deviations. Notes are placed under cores/bench/ to\nrespect the target-only editing boundary.\n\nLocal verification:\n- Required Verilator lint command: PASS, no warnings.\n- NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench: PASS, 2 ELFs. Includes full RVFI selftest\n  comparison with and without instruction/data stalls and stalled\n  CoreMark canonical CRC/validation/bounded-memory checks.\n- make test TARGET=bench: PASS, all 13 pytest runners / 121 cocotb cases\n  (158.34 seconds), including decoder, real and ALTOPS ALU/multiply/divide/\n  EX, ID/EX, immediate generation, register file and 35 pipeline cases.\n- RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench JOBS=8 bash formal/run_all.sh:\n  PASS on the first attempt: 53 passed, 0 failed. Automatically selected\n  the unchanged single retirement wrapper and checks_si.cfg (ALTOPS).\n  Includes illegal-instruction, liveness, unique retirement, register and\n  instruction checks; reg_ch0 completed in 338 seconds. No counterexample\n  or fix attempts. Real arithmetic is covered by the passing real-mode\n  unit and cosimulation gates; optional formal-deep was not run.\n- Gowin placements 0, 1 and 2: PASS (all fit and route) via the unchanged\n  evaluator's python3 -m tools.eval.gowin bench --all-options --paths 5\n  entry point. Used --all-options instead of make timing's default single\n  placement so the complete scored median is measured.\n\nMeasured performance:\n- Placement 0: 85.351 MHz, 12 logic levels.\n- Placement 1: 85.673 MHz, 13 logic levels.\n- Placement 2: 85.673 MHz, 13 logic levels.\n- Median Fmax: 85.673 MHz, 8.68% below champion's 93.817 MHz.\n- Stalled CoreMark: 10 iterations / 4,296,444 marker-bounded cycles,\n  exactly unchanged from the champion; completed with canonical CRCs.\n- Fitness: 199.40 iterations/second, computed using the evaluator's median\n  and exact iterations/cycle (equivalent timing/CoreMark components of\n  make fpga; no extra placement rerun).\n- Placement-0 area: 3,633 logic cells, 1,090 registers, 40 LUT-RAM,\n  4 BSRAM, 2 DSP; logic count fell by 42 from the champion's 3,675.\n\nThis hypothesis DOES NOT meet performance acceptance (>98.133 MHz and\n>228.405 iterations/second). Simpler family classifiers and lower logic\ncount did not improve vendor timing. The worst reported placement-0 paths\nrun from registered rs2_val through EX to predictor counters; placements\n1/2 have rs2_val-through-EX-to-ID operand paths. No unrelated datapath,\nshifter, comparator, crossbar or predictor changes were made to chase the\nregression. The requested implementation is left intact for evaluation.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
