{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_52","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"git diff --check; git status --short; git -C formal/riscv-formal status --short; sed -n '30,115p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":" M cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py\n?? cores/bench/test/test_hazard_unit.py\n?? cores/bench/test/test_predictor.py\n?? cores/bench-w4KBjDuOw/\n?? cores/bench-wIFMkVcOB/\n?? cores/bench-wKuTCZibU/\nalignment and correction priority. A hazard test covers correction with\nsimultaneous younger load-use/imem holds and older dmem/divider holds.\n\nLocal checks:\n\n- Required Verilator lint command: pass, no warnings.\n- `make test TARGET=bench`: pass, all nine pytest runners, including the\n  real and ALTOPS divider suites and expanded pipeline/predictor checks.\n- `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench`: pass on the first implementation;\n  rebuilt final RTL and `python3 -m tools.eval.cosim . bench`: pass for\n  selftest with and without random bus stalls and stalled CoreMark CRCs.\n- Stalled canonical CoreMark: 4,190,183 measured cycles for ten iterations,\n  accepted CRC/validation checks and valid MMIO timing brackets.\n- `RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench JOBS=8 bash formal/run_all.sh`:\n  pass on final RTL, 53 passed and zero failed. The first equivalent form\n  also passed all 53 checks. Neither run required a counterexample fix.\n- `NRET=1 make fpga TARGET=bench`: pass on final RTL, including all three\n  vendor placement options and bracketed, CRC-validated stalled CoreMark.\n\nFinal Gowin measurements:\n\n| Metric | Final RTL |\n| --- | --- |\n| Placement option 0 Fmax | 66.590 MHz |\n| Placement option 1 Fmax | 73.351 MHz |\n| Placement option 2 Fmax | 73.351 MHz |\n| Median Fmax | 73.351 MHz |\n| Logic cells / FFs | 3,453 / 857 |\n| LUT-RAM / BSRAM / DSP | 56 / 4 / 6 |\n| Measured CoreMark cycles / iterations | 4,190,183 / 10 |\n| Fitness | 175.05 iterations/sec |\n| Gain over champion's 162.96 iterations/sec | 7.42% |\n\nThe final median product exceeds the 4.6% acceptance bar. Median Fmax\nimproves 7.11% over 68.482 MHz. The option-0 worst setup path still starts\nat registered rs2_val and ends at the multiplier input: 38 cells, 20.122 ns\narrival. Final area saves 160 logic cells and 128 FFs versus the champion.\nThe exact prototype numbers are not reproduced: the final median is higher\n(73.351 versus 72.566 MHz), and logic count is 15 cells higher (3,453 versus\n3,438); measured CoreMark cycles are identical.\n\nThe initial equivalent form masked the training payload with validity\nbefore saturation. It passed correctness but produced 3,408 logic cells\nand a 69.476 MHz median, below the prototype result. The final implementation\ninstead uses the requested explicit invalid-row first-update override and\nsaturates only valid live payloads. No pipeline RTL was transplanted.\n\nThere are no functional deviations from the hypothesis. Additional unit\ntests live in allowed `test/test_*.py` files. Formal uses the existing fast\nALTOPS contract; real arithmetic is covered by the preserved unit/cosim\nchecks, and arithmetic RTL was not changed.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
