{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_6", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'for p in /AGENTS.md /srv/AGENTS.md /srv/hwebench/AGENTS.md /srv/hwebench/clones/AGENTS.md /srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6_1-sol_xhigh-v2-rep6/AGENTS.md /srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6_1-sol_xhigh-v2-rep6/cores/AGENTS.md /srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6_1-sol_xhigh-v2-rep6/cores/bench/AGENTS.md /srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6_1-sol_xhigh-v2-rep6/cores/bench/worktrees/AGENTS.md; do if test -f \"$p\"; then cat \"$p\"; fi; done; rg --files --hidden -g AGENTS.md -g '\"'\"'!formal/riscv-formal/**'\"'; cat Makefile; cat cores/bench/core.yaml\"", "aggregated_output": ".PHONY: help lint test test-infra cosim formal fpga timing next loop report bench clean\n.DEFAULT_GOAL := help\n\n# Resolve OSS CAD Suite path so commands work even when the user hasn't\n# sourced .toolchain/oss-cad-suite/environment in this shell.\nTOOLCHAIN_DIR := $(CURDIR)/.toolchain\nOSS_BIN       := $(TOOLCHAIN_DIR)/oss-cad-suite/bin\nLOCAL_BIN     := $(TOOLCHAIN_DIR)/bin\nexport PATH := $(OSS_BIN):$(LOCAL_BIN):$(PATH)\n\n# Orchestrator knobs (pass-through to tools.orchestrator):\n#   N        — number of rounds for `make loop` (default 10).\n#   K        — tournament size, slots per round (default 1 = sequential).\n#   AGENT    — codex (default) or claude. Honors a pre-existing\n#              AGENT_PROVIDER env var if AGENT isn't set on the make\n#              command line.\n#   BASE     — when forking a new TARGET, copy from cores/<BASE>/.\n#              Default: baseline (orchestrator-side default).\n#   COREMARK — target CoreMark iterations/sec (e.g. '370').\n#   LUT      — target LUT count (e.g. '3000').\n#   WORKTREE — default ON. `make loop` first creates a dedicated git worktree\n#              at .worktrees/<TARGET>/ on branch core-<TARGET> and re-execs\n#              itself there. Lets two `make loop` invocations for different\n#              TARGETs run in parallel without git index/merge collisions.\n#              To opt out (run directly on the current branch + cwd) pass\n#              an explicit empty value: `make loop TARGET=v1 WORKTREE=`.\nN        ?= 10\nK        ?= 1\nAGENT    ?= $(or $(AGENT_PROVIDER),codex)\nBASE     ?=\nCOREMARK ?=\nLUT      ?=\nWORKTREE ?= 1\n\n# Compose optional CLI flags for the orchestrator. Empty vars produce\n# empty strings so the orchestrator falls back to its defaults.\nORCH_FLAGS  = --iterations $(N) --tournament-size $(K)\nifneq ($(strip $(BASE)),)\n  ORCH_FLAGS += --base $(BASE)\nendif\nifneq ($(strip $(COREMARK)),)\n  ORCH_FLAGS += --coremark-target $(COREMARK)\nendif\nifneq ($(strip $(LUT)),)\n  ORCH_FLAGS += --lut-target $(LUT)\nendif\n\n# Multi-core: TARGET selects the core under cores/<TARGET>\n…[5130 of 8202 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:242b4776bcfa2fb3]…\nH_TARGET_FLAG)\nendif\n\nreport:\n\tpython3 -m tools.orchestrator --report $(ORCH_TARGET_FLAG)\n\nclean:\n\trm -rf test/cosim/sim_build sim_build out\n\trm -rf experiments/worktrees\n\trm -f bench/programs/*.elf\n\trm -f test/*.result.xml\n\tfind test -name __pycache__ -prune -exec rm -rf {} + 2>/dev/null || true\n\tfind tools -name __pycache__ -prune -exec rm -rf {} + 2>/dev/null || true\nifneq ($(strip $(TARGET)),)\n\trm -rf $(OBJ_DIR)\n\trm -rf $(GEN_DIR)\n\trm -rf cores/$(TARGET)/sim_build\nendif\nname: bench\ndescription: Frozen LLM-benchmark fixture core. Identical RTL to baseline at the bench-fixture-v1\n  freeze point. The benchmark matrix clones from the bench-fixture-v1 orphan branch\n  and operates only on this directory.\nisa: rv32im\nnret: 1\ntarget_fpga: tang-nano-20k\ntargets:\n  fmax_mhz: 135\n  lut4: 10000\n  coremark_iter_s: 300\n  coremark_per_mhz: 2.2\ncurrent:\n  fmax_mhz: 93.817\n  lut4: 3675\n  ff: 1090\n  coremark_iter_s: 2.0e-06\n  coremark_per_mhz: 0.0\n  source_id: hyp-20261002-003-r5s2\n  updated: '2026-10-02T19:22:34.323434Z'\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
