{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_46","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'git diff --check; git status --short; cat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md'","aggregated_output":" M cores/bench/rtl/core_pkg.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/id_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/test/test_ex_stage.py\n M cores/bench/test/test_id_stage.py\n M cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py\n# Branch comparison leaf retiming\n\nImplemented the proposed boundary change without an extra stage or bubble.\nID/EX now carries sixteen two-bit-slice equality flags and sixteen unsigned\nless-than flags. ID computes them from the same forwarding-resolved, x0-corrected\nvalues captured into rs1_val/rs2_val, using the existing payload reset and\nadvance/hold enable. Control-only squash remains unchanged. EX reduces the\nregistered leaves with four ordered balanced levels and applies signed correction\nusing the retained operand sign bits. ALU, M-extension units, prediction policy,\nalignment checks, memory interface, top-level ports, nret=1, and RVFI are unchanged.\n\nExtended all affected packed test layouts without removing existing assertions.\nAdded exhaustive two-bit leaf tests in every slice, random and directed EX tests\nfor all six branch conditions and bit significance, hold/reset/squash checks,\nsubword accepted-load branch tests, same-destination writers, x0/source aliases,\nand back-to-back signed/unsigned branches under independent bus stalls. Stalled\nread buses now carry changing poison words in the pipeline tests. A Yosys SAT\nmiter proves the actual ID capture and EX reduction against independently\nregistered native comparisons for arbitrary 32-bit operands and all funct3s.\n\nLocal checks:\n\n- Required Verilator lint command: pass, no warnings.\n- Full cocotb/pytest suite: 14 pytest entries passed, including real RV32M and\n  ALTOPS unit variants; 120 cocotb cases passed. SAT comparison proof: pass.\n- Cosimulation: pass for selftest with and without independent random bus\n  stalls, and canonical CoreMark CRC/UART/OOB checks. The first bare make cosim\n  invocation used the Makefile's NRET=2 harness default and failed to compile;\n  rerunning with NRET=1 passed without any contract-file changes.\n- Canonical CoreMark: 10 iterations, exactly 4,296,444 timed cycles, valid\n  start/stop MMIO markers and canonical CRCs/UART; no OOB access.\n- Unchanged local formal gate: pass, 53 checks passed and 0 failed on the first\n  attempt using RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench JOBS=8 bash\n  formal/run_all.sh (auto-selected wrapper_si.sv and checks_si.cfg).\n  reg_ch0 completed after 410 seconds. No counterexample or RTL fix/retry.\n\nAll three vendor placements completed using tools.eval.gowin --all-options:\n\n| Placement option | Fmax (MHz) | Reported logic levels |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| 0 | 80.444 | 11 |\n| 1 | 78.139 | 10 |\n| 2 | 78.139 | 10 |\n\nMedian Fmax is 78.139 MHz and fitness is 181.869006 iterations/second at the\nunchanged cycle count. This fails the proposed acceptance thresholds of\n98.133 MHz and 228.405 iterations/second. Vendor area is 3,553 logic cells,\n1,122 registers, 40 LUT-RAM cells, 4 BSRAMs, and 2 DSPs. The 32 added registers\nmatch the leaf payload. Critical paths include advancing EX result/control\nthrough forwarding into ID operands and leaf registers; option 0 includes a\n37-cell ALU-to-branch_eq capture path. The predicted timing risk materialized,\ndespite fewer logic cells. No unrelated optimization was substituted for this\nstructural hypothesis.\n\nImplementation notes are kept at the explicitly permitted per-core path rather\nthan the repository/worktree root to respect the target-core sandbox.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
