{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_31", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '/\"'^ *Path1$/,/''^ *Path2$/p'\"' cores/bench/generated/timing/gowin_p0/impl/pnr/core_bench.tr | head -150; tail -3 cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl; cat \\\"\"'$TMPDIR/return-stack-timing.log\"'", "aggregated_output": "{\"id\": \"hyp-20261003-001-r10s0\", \"title\": \"Fuse immediate selection into the ID ALU-B forwarding mux\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The champion's limiting path runs from registered EX ALU operands through\\nthe ALU and forwarding back to the ID/EX ALU inputs. ID currently resolves\\na three-source rs2_value, forces x0, then selects immediate versus that\\nresult for alu_b. This serial selection adds another mux to a timed\\nrecurrence. Previous opcode recoding, predictor updates and the six-source\\ndirect EX result crossbar all regressed; the latter increased LUTs to\\n3,887. A smaller change confined to final ALU-B selection can remove one\\nserial mux while retaining the shared EX bypass and producer qualification.\\nA local experiment fusing both ALU-A and ALU-B selection passed the\\nexisting ID/pipeline suites but reached only 92.375 MHz median, below the\\n93.817 MHz champion. The proposed narrower ALU-B-only circuit avoids the\\nadditional AUIPC/ALU-A crossbar and its routing pressure.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The champion's limiting path runs from registered EX ALU operands through\\nthe ALU and forwarding back to the ID/EX ALU inputs. ID currently resolves\\na three-source rs2_value, forces x0, then selects immediate versus that\\nresult for alu_b. This serial selection adds another mux to a timed\\nrecurrence. Previous opcode recoding, predictor updates and the six-source\\ndirect EX result crossbar all regressed; the latter increased LUTs to\\n3,887. A smaller change confined to final ALU-B selection can remove one\\nserial mux while retaining the shared EX bypass and producer qua