{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20261002-001-r6s0.log').read_text().splitlines():\n    try:\n        item=json.loads(line).get('item',{})\n    except json.JSONDecodeError:\n        continue\n    if item.get('type') == 'agent_message':\n        print(item.get('text',''))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"I’ll check the prior micro-optimization attempts and current timing evidence, then write a hypothesis targeting the ALU-to-ID forwarding path.\nThe current worst path runs from an ID/EX operand through the ALU and back into the next instruction’s ID/EX operand. Earlier reset and squash changes left that path largely intact. I’ll focus on flattening its result-selection and forwarding muxes while preserving instruction latency and forwarding priority.\nThe hypothesis file is written and schema-valid. An isolated prototype passed the existing ID, EX and pipeline tests, but Gowin timing got worse: the critical path shifted to operation-decode control. I’m checking which selection change caused that before refining the proposal.\nThe timing checks show that flattening the muxes increases the load on the encoded ALU-operation bits. I’m testing whether computing multiply/divide class bits in ID, then carrying them with ID/EX controls, shortens EX completion and forwarding control without adding a pipeline stage.\nThe control-predecode variants also missed the current timing result. The baseline report shows the register-file read path within 0.014 ns of the worst ALU path. I’m testing a register-file reset change that clears per-register validity bits and returns zero until the first write, allowing the data array to retain efficient LUT-RAM inference.\nNone of the tested variants has cleared the 4.6% acceptance margin. Several expose long carry chains through EX. I’m now testing four-bit local adders with a balanced carry-prefix network for ADD/SUB, keeping the pipeline and cycle count unchanged.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
