{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_5", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n --hidden -g '\"'!.git/**'\"' -g '\"'!.codex-home/**'\"' -g '\"'!formal/riscv-formal/**'\"' 'hyp-20261002-002-r2s1|108\\\\.75|7\\\\.45|101\\\\.21|4,491,817|4491817' .\"", "aggregated_output": "./cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:3:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261002-002-r1s1\", \"title\": \"Move division out of the single-cycle execute path\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The only recorded bench experiment is the baseline: 5.442 MHz with a\\n199.837 ns worst path spanning forwarding, EX, and the combinational ALU\\nthrough 156 cells. There are no previous structural attempts or recorded\\nlessons. The ALU implements signed and unsigned divide and remainder with\\ncombinational / and % operators. These unrolled arithmetic networks remain\\nin the timed result-selection cone even when an ordinary RV32I instruction\\nexecutes. Moving this rare, deep operation behind registers offers much\\nmore timing headroom than improving an individual forwarding mux.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The only recorded bench experiment is the baseline: 5.442 MHz with a\\n199.837 ns worst path spanning forwarding, EX, and the combinational ALU\\nthrough 156 cells. There are no previous structural attempts or recorded\\nlessons. The ALU implements signed and unsigned divide and remainder with\\ncombinational / and % operators. These unrolled arithmetic networks remain\\nin the timed result-selection cone even when an ordinary RV32I instruction\\nexecutes. Moving this rare, deep operation behind registers offers much\\nmore timing headroom than improving an individual forwarding mux.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace all four combinational DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU paths with one shared,\\nblocking, iterative divider connected to EX. Keep RV32I execution and\\nmultiplication on their existing single-cycle paths. The divider captures\\nthe fully forwarded operands and operation exactly once, converts signed\\noperands to unsigned magnitudes, and performs one radix-2 restoring\\ndivision step per cycle using a registered partial remainder, quotient,\\ndivisor, and a bounded counter. Share the magnitude datapath between signed\\nand unsigned operations and between quotient and remainder; register sign\\ncorrection before presenting the result. A normal division takes a\n…[17166 of 20238 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:eb2edf58f9736f50]…\nted memory writes,\\nno side effects or RVFI retirement from invalid fetched payloads,\\nconsecutive retirement orders, and unchanged retirement PCs/results\\nwith deterministic independent bus stalls. Run existing formal,\\ncosimulation, and CoreMark correctness gates before Gowin timing.\\n\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 110.73, \"delta_pct\": 9.41, \"vs_baseline\": 813.61, \"fmax_mhz\": 49.74, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4491817, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 2521, \"ff\": 681, \"seeds\": [49.051, 49.74, 49.74], \"perturbations\": [[0, 49.051, 13], [1, 49.74, 13], [2, 49.74, 13]], \"lutram\": 8, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s\", \"to\": \"dmem_1_dmem_1_0_0_s\", \"slack_ns\": -15.387, \"arrival_ns\": 25.682, \"logic_cells\": 13, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_id\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\", \"cpu/u_ex\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 13, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-02T17:21:32.793959Z\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 2}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
