{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_6", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n --hidden -g '\"'!.git/**'\"' -g '\"'!formal/riscv-formal/**'\"' -g '\"'!**/obj_dir/**'\"' -g '\"'!**/build/**'\"' 'hyp-20261003-001-r10s0|183\\\\.32|16\\\\.05|alu_b_immediate|98\\\\.133' .\"", "aggregated_output": "./cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:17:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261002-001-r6s0\", \"title\": \"Factor AND OR XOR into one four-input-LUT ALU result family\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The current champion has a 93.817 MHz median Fmax, with the worst timed path crossing the combinational ALU and EX result selection before returning to ID/EX operands. Its ALU treats AND, OR and XOR as three separate full-width output alternatives. Each result bit can instead use one shared four-input Boolean function, reducing the number of wide alternatives in the ALU output mux. Prior payload-reset and predictor-banking attempts left ordinary ALU forwarding as a timing limit; explicit prefix adders and broad forwarding rewrites also failed to improve local vendor timing. This proposal targets only the bitwise ALU family and its result-selection cost.\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current champion has a 93.817 MHz median Fmax, with the worst timed path crossing the combinational ALU and EX result selection before returning to ID/EX operands. Its ALU treats AND, OR and XOR as three separate full-width output alternatives. Each result bit can instead use one shared four-input Boolean function, reducing the number of wide alternatives in the ALU output mux. Prior payload-reset and predictor-banking attempts left ordinary ALU forwarding as a timing limit; explicit prefix adders and broad forwarding rewrites also failed to improve local vendor timing. This proposal targets only the bitwise ALU family and its result-selection cost.\", \"hypothesis\": \"Implement AND, OR and XOR as one shared bitwise result family without changing latency, the ALU port interface, pipeline topology, operation encoding or forwarding behavior. In parallel with data arrival, decode two scalar controls:\\n  xor_en = (op == ALU_OR) || (op == ALU_XOR)\\n  and_en = (op == ALU_OR) || (op == ALU_AND)\\nFor each bit i, compute\\n  logic_result[i] = ((a[i] ^ b[i]) & xor_en)\\n                  | ((a[i] & b[i]) & and_en).\\nThis has exactly four independent inputs per bit\n…[76446 of 79518 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:ecfb8b8c7cecb0e0]…\ndelta_pct\": -12.68, \"vs_baseline\": 1473.18, \"fmax_mhz\": 81.919, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4296444, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 3470, \"ff\": 971, \"seeds\": [81.45, 81.919, 81.919], \"perturbations\": [[0, 81.45, 11], [1, 81.919, 11], [2, 81.919, 11]], \"lutram\": 56, \"bsram\": 4, \"dsp\": 2, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_id/reg_q.ctrl.alu_op_0_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_id/reg_q.rs2_val_17_s0\", \"slack_ns\": -7.277, \"arrival_ns\": 17.572, \"logic_cells\": 11, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_fwd\", \"cpu/u_id\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 11, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-02T22:18:40.749604Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 9, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-10-03 hyp-20261002-003-r9s2 (regression, -12.68%): Registering BHT training with four 32-row validity-reset LUT-RAM banks shifts the timing limit to ID/EX ALU control through EX forwarding into ID operands, so area savings alone cannot prevent Fmax falling from 93.817 to 81.919 MHz at unchanged CoreMark cycles.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
