ary instruction slots with circular head/tail pointers and occupancy in cores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv. Empty ready fetches enter the existing ID/EX register immediately without also entering the queue; blocked empty fetches enqueue once and advance PC. Buffered heads drain independently of imemReady, and a full queue accepts simultaneous pop/refill. Fetch PC and prediction use the accepted raw bus instruction. Accepted EX correction clears all ownership, squashes ID, rejects the old bus transaction and selects the redirect target; the next ready target falls through without a refill cycle. Queue payload enables use ready, capacity and raw issue hold, allowing harmless inactive payload capture on correction.\\n\\nSeparated raw ID dependency/EX-busy/dmem holds from instruction\n…[2932 of 6004 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:00458540c942b3af]…\nfix changed to a vector array sized by $bits(if_id_t), but that frontend rejects $bits(type) with a syntax error. Second fix uses the preserved bundle's explicit 98-bit width; a direct Yosys frontend/proc/check run now recognizes the slots as memory and reports zero problems. The final full run passed, including pc_fwd_ch0 and reg_ch0. No wrapper, config or check has been edited.\\n\"}\n{\"id\": \"hyp-20261003-003-r14s2\", \"title\": \"Static backward-taken prediction removes dynamic predictor timing and fanout\", \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 183.29, \"delta_pct\": -16.06, \"fmax_mhz\": 79.787, \"cycles\": 4353135, \"lut4\": 3074, \"ff\": 834, \"seeds\": [81.089, 79.787, 79.787], \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_id/reg_q.ctrl.alu_op_4_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_id/reg_q.rs1_val_20_s0\", \"slack_ns\": -7.332, \"arrival_ns\": 17.626, \"logic_cells\": 10, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_mul\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_fwd\", \"cpu/u_id\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 10, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "comple