joined in a balanced tree, with no change to operand capture or instruction latency.\n\nThe comparator probes also lost timing. I’m testing a different micro-optimization: forward an accepted load result directly to a following store’s data input, removing that dependency bubble. Store-address dependencies will keep their existing interlock.\n\nLoad-to-store forwarding saved only 398 CoreMark cycles and regressed timing, so I’m excluding it. I’m refining the original forwarding hypothesis by registering candidate eligibility in ID, which may remove the remaining write-control logic from the selection path.\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
