276 MHz to clear 217.0973 iter/sec. Preserve nret=1, core IO, decoder\ndefault-illegal behavior, trap suppression, arithmetic and all invariants.\n''',\n 'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':6,'confidence':'low'},\n 'changes':[\n {'file':'rtl/id_stage.sv','description':'''Split ID/EX sequential updates into payload and control/valid banks.\nCapture payload solely on \"'!stall with no reset, flush or fetch-valid\ncondition. Keep full ctrl_t/valid reset, flush and invalid-bubble clearing\nwith original priority, and hold the complete accepted instruction during\nstalls. Preserve all existing decode, operand forwarding and ALU-input\nselection expressions; add no pipeline stage or new interlock.\n'\"'''},\n {'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Retain all existing assertions. Add focused reset-during-hold, arithmetic\nwait, stalled-memory and wrong-path sequences with loads, stores, M ops,\nillegal instructions, branches and JALR. Verify that invalid/uninitialized\nID payload cannot create memory or arithmetic requests, forwarding writes,\nbranch training or RVFI retirements. Require exact accepted operands,\nconsecutive retirement order and unchanged zero-wait instruction latency.\nRun unchanged formal and stalled CoreMark gates; include a symbolic\ninitial-payload audit before relying on removal of payload reset.\n'''}]}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(h,sort_keys=False,width=85))\njsonschema.validate(h,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Revised single-angle hypothesis validates:',p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "Revised single-angle hypothesis validates: cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-001-r5s0.yaml\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
