{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_64","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom concurrent.futures import ThreadPoolExecutor,as_completed\nimport json\nfrom tools.eval.gowin import build\nprobe=Path('/srv/hwebench/tmp/6b356b5e/fcee66c5/r6s0_probe')\nwith ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=3) as pool:\n futures={pool.submit(build,Path.cwd(),probe/name/'rtl','fpga/core_bench_si.sv',option,probe/name/f'p{option}'):(name,option) for name in ('lut_logic','reverse_shift') for option in (0,1)}\n for f in as_completed(futures):\n  name,option=futures[f];r=f.result();(probe/name/f'result{option}.json').write_text(json.dumps(r,indent=2));print(name,json.dumps(r),flush=True)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_65", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json, yaml, jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-001-r6s0.yaml')\nd={\n'id':'hyp-20261002-001-r6s0',\n'title':'Factor AND OR XOR into one four-input-LUT ALU result family',\n'category':'micro_opt',\n'motivation':'''The current champion has a 93.817 MHz median Fmax, with the worst timed path crossing the combinational ALU and EX result selection before returning to ID/EX operands. Its ALU treats AND, OR and XOR as three separate full-width output alternatives. Each result bit can instead use one shared four-input Boolean function, reducing the number of wide alternatives in the ALU output mux. Prior payload-reset and predictor-banking attempts left ordinary ALU forwarding as a timing limit; explicit prefix adders and broad forwarding rewrites also failed to improve local vendor timing. This proposal targets only the bitwise ALU family and its result-selection cost.''',\n'hypothesis':'''Implement AND, OR and XOR as one shared bitwise result family without changing latency, the ALU port interface, pipeline topology, operation encoding or forwarding behavior. In parallel with data arrival, decode two scalar controls:\n  xor_en = (op == ALU_OR) || (op == ALU_XOR)\n  and_en = (op == ALU_OR) || (op == ALU_AND)\nFor each bit i, compute\n  logic_result[i] = ((a[i] \"'^ b[i]) & xor_en)\n                  | ((a[i] & b[i]) & and_en).\nThis has exactly four independent inputs per bit: a[i], b[i], xor_en and and_en. AND enables only the second term, XOR only the first, and OR enables both, since (a XOR b) OR (a AND b) equals a OR b. For every other operation both enables are zero. Express this as two masked word terms ORed together, allowing Gowin to map each result bit into one LUT4.\n\nReplace the three separate ALU case arms with one grouped ALU_AND, ALU_OR, ALU_XOR arm returning logic_result. Preserve the existing ADD/SUB, signed/unsigned comparisons, three shifts, LUI, default-zero behavior and real inactive M-extension outputs exactly. Keep every RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS operation-specific formula unchanged and use the same bitwise family in both build modes. Do not introduce another full-width bitwise-op selector after the shared result: the grouped arm is the sole insertion point into the existing ALU output selection.\n\nThe single micro-optimization is factoring a three-choice 32-bit ALU sub-mux into a LUT4-sized truth table. It should reduce logic/routing pressure and shorten ALU result selection, including selection traversed by non-bitwise results, while preserving the champion'\"'s exact instruction schedule and marker-bounded CoreMark cycle count. Decoder validation, x0, trap discipline, bus acceptance, arithmetic ownership, payload stall/squash/reset policy, predictor recovery, nret=1 IO and all RVFI fields/order remain unchanged. No don't-care inputs or relaxed checks are permitted.\n\nWith unchanged 4,296,444 measured CoreMark cycles, acceptance requires median Fmax above approximately 98.133 MHz and fitness above 228.405 iter/sec. Validate actual LUT mapping and median timing with Gowin; a Boolean simplification alone is not evidence of a fitness gain. Run the existing normal/ALTOPS ALU suites and unchanged pipeline/formal/stalled cosimulation/CoreMark gates, including canonical CRCs, the validation literal, OOB checks and existing start/stop MMIO brackets.''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':8,'confidence':'low'},\n'changes':[\n {'file':'rtl/alu.sv','description':'''Add the two parallel scalar logic-family enables and the shared masked-XOR/AND result word. Group ALU_AND, ALU_OR and ALU_XOR into a single case arm selecting that word. Preserve all other ALU branches, operation constants, interfaces, arithmetic semantics and exact ALTOPS substitutions. Avoid pipelining, broad mux rewrites or changes to producer enables.'''} ,\n {'file':'test/test_alu.py','description':'''Retain all existing real and ALTOPS checks. Add exact AND/OR/XOR vectors using zero/all-ones, alternating masks, walking-one/walking-zero operands and deterministic random pairs. Alternate these operations on fixed operands and interleave shifts/add/sub/M-extension opcodes to catch stale or overlapping family enables. Check opcodes outside the family retain their existing results.'''}\n]}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,default_flow_style=False,width=84))\njsonschema.validate(d,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Refined schema-valid micro_opt hypothesis:',p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
