{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_7", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n d=json.loads(line)\n print(d['id'], d.get('category'), d.get('title'), 'fitness',d.get('fitness'),'fmax',d.get('fmax_mhz'),'cycles',d.get('cycles'))\n if d.get('category')=='micro_opt' and d['id']\"'!='\"'baseline-bench-2e8305b':\n  h=d.get('hypothesis',{})\n  print('PROPOSAL:',h.get('hypothesis','') if isinstance(h,dict) else h)\n  print('NOTES:',d.get('implementation_notes',''))\n if d['id']=='hyp-20261002-003-r5s2': print('PATH:',d.get('critical_path'))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "baseline-bench-2e8305b micro_opt Baseline retest for cores/bench fitness 12.12 fmax 5.442 cycles 4491485\nhyp-20261002-001-r1s0 micro_opt Share a width-tapered combinational divider across RV32M operations fitness 8.95 fmax 4.021 cycles 4491485\nPROPOSAL: Replace only the real DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU datapath with one combinational\nunsigned restoring divider that produces quotient and remainder together.\nKeep the existing pipeline, forwarding and bus-handshake behavior, with\nno extra cycles for any instruction. For signed operations, convert both\noperands to unsigned 32-bit magnitudes before the divider, then negate the\nquotient when operand signs differ and negate the remainder only when the\ndividend is negative. Unsigned operations use the original operand bits.\n\nMake the 32 unrolled restoring stages explicitly width-tapered. At stage\nk=1..32, append dividend bit 32-k to the previous remainder to form a\nk-bit trial remainder. Subtract divisor[k-1:0] once using a k+1-bit\nzero-extended subtraction. Accept its low k bits and set quotient bit\n32-k only when the subtraction has no borrow and every divisor bit above\nk-1 is zero; otherwise retain the trial remainder and emit quotient zero.\nAt k=32 the upper-divisor predicate is constant true. Use the subtraction's\nborrow bit instead of a separate magnitude comparator, and use static\ngenerate widths so early stages contain only the necessary carry logic.\nThe final stage supplies both results; do not infer another '%' circuit.\n\nPreserve division-by-zero results explicitly (quotient 0xffffffff,\nremainder original dividend) and signed INT_MIN/-1 results (quotient\n0x80000000, remainder zero). Keep the RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS substitutions\nexactly as they are and exclude the real divider from that build. Keep\nmultiply and all RV32I datapaths unchanged. The expected gain comes from\nsharing arithmetic, reducing carry-chain width and avoiding duplicate\ncomparator/subtractor logic, with unchanged iterations per cycle.\n\nNOTES: \nhyp-20261002-002-r1s1 structural Move division out of the singl\n…[19298 of 22370 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:523f26bdddd3338c]…\nrk cycle count. Decoder validation, x0, trap discipline, bus acceptance, arithmetic ownership, payload stall/squash/reset policy, predictor recovery, nret=1 IO and all RVFI fields/order remain unchanged. No don't-care inputs or relaxed checks are permitted.\n\nWith unchanged 4,296,444 measured CoreMark cycles, acceptance requires median Fmax above approximately 98.133 MHz and fitness above 228.405 iter/sec. Validate actual LUT mapping and median timing with Gowin; a Boolean simplification alone is not evidence of a fitness gain. Run the existing normal/ALTOPS ALU suites and unchanged pipeline/formal/stalled cosimulation/CoreMark gates, including canonical CRCs, the validation literal, OOB checks and existing start/stop MMIO brackets.\nNOTES: \nhyp-20261002-002-r6s1 structural Replace the shared EX bypass bus with direct operand forwarding fitness 204.38 fmax 87.809 cycles 4296444\nhyp-20261002-003-r6s2 predictor One-bit agree prediction removes the counter training lookup fitness 205.18 fmax 88.547 cycles 4315581\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
