{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_71", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-001-r7s0.yaml')\nd={\n'id':'hyp-20261002-001-r7s0',\n'title':'Align M operation codes to shorten EX class selection',\n'category':'micro_opt',\n'motivation':'''The champion scores 218.36 iter/sec at 93.817 MHz and 4,296,444 marker-bounded CoreMark cycles. Its ALU/EX-to-ID recurrence remains the timing limit. Other placements and local prototypes expose paths from registered alu_op bits through EX completion, forwarding eligibility and younger operands. The current MUL codes 11..14 and DIV/REM codes 15..18 straddle binary boundaries, so EX recognizes each family with four full five-bit equality checks. Prior bitwise factoring, a broad operand crossbar and predictor simplification regressed timing. Local decoded-shifter, comparator and added-class-register experiments also failed to clear the required margin. A compact internal encoding attacks the repeated class decisions without a wider crossbar or extra state.''',\n'hypothesis':'''Recode only the eight internal M-extension ALU tags into a naturally aligned block, retaining all RV32I tags 0..10 and the five-bit tag width:\n  MUL=16, MULH=17, MULHSU=18, MULHU=19,\n  DIV=20, DIVU=21, REM=22, REMU=23.\nThese values are {2'b10, instruction_funct3} for the eight validated RV32M instructions. Multiply is exactly alu_op[4:2]==3'b100 and division/remainder is exactly alu_op[4:2]==3'b101. Replace the two EX four-way full-tag classifiers with those bounded three-bit comparisons. Preserve explicit whole-family matching: bit 4 alone must not classify undefined tags 24..31 as M operations.\n\nKeep decoder opcode/funct validation and default-illegal behavior unchanged; its existing symbolic ALU constants now produce the new tags. Keep every other consumer symbolic, including ordinary ALU dispatch, exact ALTOPS formulas, multiplier signedness/high-half selection and divider operation selection. The natural low bits also expose DIV/REM signedness and remainder selection to synthesis through the existing constant comparisons, without changing their arithmetic or request/response protocols. Do not introduce new class registers, alter instruction encodings, widen ctrl_t, change pipeline boundaries, or combine this with result-crossbar, shifter, comparator or prediction changes.\n\nThe intended gain is fewer inputs and less decoding/routing on multiply/divide occupancy, request launch, completion selection and bypass control. Operand data, trap-adjusted enables, launch-once ownership, response holds, saved destinations, x0 exclusion and EX-over-MEM-over-RF forwarding priority retain their current behavior. Numeric tag values are internal; all actual RV32IM results, instruction latencies, stalled bus acceptance and RVFI records must remain identical.\n\nWith unchanged canonical CoreMark cycles, acceptance requires median Gowin Fmax above approximately 98.133 MHz and fitness above 228.405 iter/sec. This is a low-confidence timing hypothesis: smaller Boolean classifiers can still lose through placement, and ordinary shift, load-forwarding or branch paths can remain limiting. Measure all three vendor placement options rather than inferring a gain from source simplification. Run all existing decoder, arithmetic, ID/EX and pipeline checks, unchanged formal and stalled RVFI cosimulation/CoreMark gates. Preserve nret=1, all top-level ports, illegal and alignment traps, strict retirement order, canonical CRCs, the validation literal, bounded memory accesses and MMIO timing brackets. Only update unit-test expectations for the internal tags; retain their exact architectural result and legality assertions. Shared test helpers are outside the allowed test/test_*.py set, so override M tag aliases locally in the listed test modules rather than editing _helpers.py.''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':8,'confidence':'low'},\n'changes':[\n{'file':'rtl/core_pkg.sv','description':'Assign MUL/MULH/MULHSU/MULHU tags 16/17/18/19 and DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU tags 20/21/22/23. Preserve every RV32I tag, five-bit operation width, control/bundle layouts and other declarations. Audit all consumers for literal old tag values.'},\n{'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':\\\"Replace is_multiply and is_divide full-tag equality unions with exact alu_op[4:2] comparisons against 3'b100 and 3'b101. Preserve all operand, launch/transfer, busy, bypass, trap, redirect, predictor-training and pipeline-register logic.\\\"},\n{'file':'test/test_decoder.py','description':'Update local expected M operation aliases to the new internal tags, preserving all instruction encoding, legality, reserved-function and default-illegal assertions. Check the same eight validated RV32M instruction functions map to the corresponding new tags.'},\n{'file':'test/test_alu.py','description':'Update local M tag aliases for inactive-real-operation and exact ALTOPS checks. Retain all RV32I and ALTOPS result assertions; ensure obsolete unused tags 11..15 and unsupported tags 24..31 keep the ALU default-zero result.'},\n{'file':'test/test_mul_unit.py','description':'Update local multiply tag aliases while retaining every exact RV32M arithmetic vector, signed/high-half expectation, request acceptance and response-stability check in real and ALTOPS modes.'},\n{'file':'test/test_div_unit.py','description':'Update local DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU aliases while retaining exact quotient/remainder and ALTOPS checks, divide-by-zero and overflow cases, signedness, launch ownership and held-response checks.'},\n{'file':'test/test_ex_stage.py','description':'Update local M tag aliases used to pack EX inputs. Keep the existing packed layouts and every stall, launch, saved-metadata, bypass and completion assertion. Check family transitions with the recoded tags and verify all existing pipeline/formal/cosimulation gates pass without changing their contracts.'}\n]}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=86))\njsonschema.validate(d,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nassert type(d['expected_impact']['fitness_delta_pct']) is int and -50<=d['expected_impact']['fitness_delta_pct']<=50\nprint('Wrote schema-valid final encoding hypothesis:',p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
