=0..14 combines\n  low child 2*n+1 and high child 2*n+2. Node zero is the whole-word root.\n  Preserve the high-child ordering exactly. Express these as continuous\n  assignments or static generate logic so no full-width ripple subtractor\n  or priority loop is introduced. Start w\n…[3771 of 6843 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:816971597e4cad4c]…\nmes, opposite signs, both directions\n      of a first difference at every bit, and pairs with a more-significant\n      decision opposing all lower bits. Exercise all two-bit leaf input\n      combinations at each slice plus seeded random full-width pairs in\n      both normal and ALTOPS builds. Require exact Python signed/unsigned\n      comparison results and zero in all upper output bits.\n  - file: test/test_ex_stage.py\n    description: |\n      Retain existing arithmetic, saved-metadata and response-hold checks.\n      Add exact outcome checks for all six legal branch predicates over\n      equal values, sign extremes, first differences at every bit and\n      seeded random pairs. Check both saved prediction directions, aligned\n      and misaligned targets, taken-only branch alignment traps, unsupported\n      branch-op default false, and suppression of redirect/training while\n      reset, invalid or older-memory hold applies. Verify accepted EX/MEM\n      next PC, trap controls and architectural operand metadata.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
