{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_7", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nwanted={'hyp-20261002-001-r4s0','hyp-20261002-001-r5s0','hyp-20261002-001-r6s0','hyp-20261002-003-r7s2','hyp-20261002-001-r8s0'}\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d['id'] not in wanted: continue\n print(d['id'],d['category'],d['title'])\n h=d.get('hypothesis',{})\n print(h.get('hypothesis',h) if isinstance(h,dict) else h)\n print('NOTES:',d.get('implementation_notes'))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261002-001-r4s0 micro_opt Balance branch comparison logic to shorten EX recovery\nReplace the EX branch unit's wide relational operators with an explicitly\nbalanced comparison tree suited to four-input FPGA LUTs. Preserve the\npipeline boundaries, predictor, exact branch outcomes and all instruction\nlatencies. This is a local Boolean implementation change to comparison,\nintended to raise Fmax while preserving CoreMark iterations per cycle.\n\nCompute equality and unsigned less-than for sixteen independent two-bit\nslices of the registered rs1/rs2 operands. Each leaf has four operand\ninputs. Combine adjacent low/high groups in four balanced levels using\neq = eq_high & eq_low and\nlt = lt_high | (eq_high & lt_low).\nReproduce the measured prototype with packed 31-bit eq/lt node vectors:\nleaves occupy indices 15+i for operand slice [2*i +: 2], i=0..15;\ninternal node n=0..14 combines high child 2*n+2 and low child 2*n+1.\nNode zero is the root. This layout keeps the most significant operand\nslices on each group's high child.\nThe root supplies whole-word equality and unsigned less-than. Derive\nsigned less-than as (rs1[31] ^ rs2[31]) ? rs1[31] : unsigned_less.\nUse these shared facts for BEQ/BNE, BLT/BGE and BLTU/BGEU, complementing\nonly the matching legal predicate; retain false for unsupported branch\nfunct3 values. Express the tree with static generate indices or explicit\nlevels so synthesis sees bounded local comparisons rather than a new\n32-bit ripple comparator. Do not replace comparison with a full-width\nsubtractor whose carry propagation recreates the long path.\n\nKeep target alignment faults, branch training on actual acceptance,\ndirection-XOR correction, EX/MEM and ID/EX hold/flush priorities,\nbypass producer validity, divider protocol and RVFI metadata intact.\nPreserve nret=1, decoder default-illegal behavior and all correctness\nchecks. Validate all six branch conditions with equality, differing\nsigns and differences at every bit position, including misaligned\ntaken targets and independent instruction/data bus st\n…[20662 of 23734 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:9b493d358d601fa8]…\n comparisons and timed saved-destination selection;\nthis refinement remains unmeasured and requires full evaluation.\nRequire unchanged 4,296,444 canonical measured cycles; acceptance\nneeds more than 228.40456 iter/sec, or approximately 98.133 MHz median\nFmax at that cycle count. Measure all three canonical Gowin placement\noptions and inspect the destination-match path. Local comparator,\nshifter, metadata-sharing and wider one-hot selection probes did not\nestablish a gain on this champion; do not include those changes.\n\nKeep exact real RV32M and ALTOPS arithmetic, launch-once ownership,\nheld responses, registered architectural operands, memory handshakes,\ndecoder default-illegal validation, branch/memory alignment traps,\npredictor training, reset/flush/hold priorities, RVFI fields and strict\nretirement order. Retain every existing test assertion. Run unchanged\nformal, stalled RVFI cosimulation and canonical CoreMark CRC, validation\nliteral, bounded-memory and MMIO-bracket gates before vendor scoring.\n\nNOTES: \n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
