{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_11", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n d=json.loads(line)\n print(json.dumps({k:d.get(k) for k in ('id','title','category','outcome','fitness','fmax_mhz','cycles','lut4','dsp','critical_path')}))\n if d.get('category')=='structural':\n  h=d.get('hypothesis')\n  print(h.get('hypothesis','') if isinstance(h,dict) else h)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "{\"id\": \"baseline-bench-2e8305b\", \"title\": \"Baseline retest for cores/bench\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"outcome\": \"improvement\", \"fitness\": 12.12, \"fmax_mhz\": 5.442, \"cycles\": 4491485, \"lut4\": 12312, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_mem/reg_q.rd_3_s0\", \"to\": \"dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s\", \"slack_ns\": -189.542, \"arrival_ns\": 199.837, \"logic_cells\": 156, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_fwd\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\", \"cpu/u_ex\"]}}\n{\"id\": \"hyp-20261002-001-r1s0\", \"title\": \"Share a width-tapered combinational divider across RV32M operations\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 8.95, \"fmax_mhz\": 4.021, \"cycles\": 4491485, \"lut4\": 4611, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_id/reg_q.rs2_addr_0_s0\", \"to\": \"dmem_1_dmem_1_0_0_s\", \"slack_ns\": -248.428, \"arrival_ns\": 258.722, \"logic_cells\": 375, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_fwd\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\", \"cpu/u_ex\"]}}\n{\"id\": \"hyp-20261002-002-r1s1\", \"title\": \"Move division out of the single-cycle execute path\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"outcome\": \"improvement\", \"fitness\": 101.21, \"fmax_mhz\": 45.46, \"cycles\": 4491817, \"lut4\": 2577, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_id/id_ex_w.rs2_val_9_s1\", \"slack_ns\": -17.306, \"arrival_ns\": 27.6, \"logic_cells\": 47, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_id\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_if\", \"cpu/u_hazard\", \"cpu/u_id\"]}}\nReplace all four combinational DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU paths with one shared,\nblocking, iterative divider connected to EX. Keep RV32I execution and\nmultiplication on their existing single-cycle paths. The divider captures\nthe fully forwarded operands and operation exactly once, converts signed\noperands to unsigned magnitudes, and performs one radix-2 restoring\ndivision step per cycle using a registered partial remainder, quotient,\ndivisor, and a bounded counter. Share the magnitude datapath between signed\nand unsigned operations and between quotient and remainder; register sign\ncorrection before presenting the result. A normal division takes about\n34-35 cyc\n…[6639 of 9711 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:1d16207666c909d9]…\nnsfers acquire one additional refill cycle relative to the\ncurrent combinational IF/ID design; this is the main performance cost.\nA plausible 60-65 MHz median Fmax with a 5-10 percent CoreMark cycle\nincrease would yield about 20-35 percent greater fitness, exceeding the\n4.6 percent acceptance threshold. These are predictions, not measured\nresults. Validate the tradeoff using canonical CRCs, the existing MMIO\nbrackets, independent approximately 22 percent bus stalls, unchanged\nformal/cosimulation gates, and the evaluator's median Gowin timing.\n\n{\"id\": \"hyp-20261002-003-r2s2\", \"title\": \"Instruction-qualified direction prediction with short recovery control\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"outcome\": \"improvement\", \"fitness\": 115.0, \"fmax_mhz\": 48.328, \"cycles\": 4202272, \"lut4\": 3358, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s\", \"to\": \"dmem_1_dmem_1_0_0_s\", \"slack_ns\": -16.928, \"arrival_ns\": 27.223, \"logic_cells\": 14, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_id\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\", \"cpu/u_ex\"]}}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
