{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_69", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-003-r3s2.yaml'", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20261002-003-r3s2\ntitle: \"Cached direct targets shorten the predictor next-PC path\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The current champion scores 115.00 at 48.328 MHz and 4,202,272\n  marker-bounded CoreMark cycles. Its instruction-qualified 128-entry\n  bimodal predictor already removes most direct-control bubbles. A\n  reference run of the canonical ELF contains 2,922,016 bracketed\n  instructions, 529,588 conditional branches, and only 13,735 JALRs;\n  replaying its conditional branches through the current 128x2 table\n  produces 54,452 direction misses. Thus a return predictor or direction\n  accuracy alone has little remaining cycle headroom against the 4.6%\n  acceptance threshold. The promising predictor angle is timing: IF\n  currently decodes a fetched B/J immediate and performs a full PC-plus-\n  immediate addition before choosing the next fetch address. The earlier\n  tagged predictor was evaluated with the old combinational divider, so\n  its timing result does not test this change on the divider champion.\nhypothesis: |\n  Replace instruction-derived direct-target prediction in IF with a\n  128-entry direct-mapped cache of resolved direct branch/JAL targets,\n  while retaining the current separate 128x2 direction counters. This is\n  one predictor timing experiment, not an arithmetic or pipeline rewrite.\n  Index the target cache with PC[8:2], store the full PC[31:9] tag, a\n  word-aligned 30-bit target, and validity. Read tag and target in parallel\n  with the direction counter. Predict only when the current raw instruction\n  is a legal BRANCH encoding or JAL, the tag matches, and the cached entry\n  is valid; a conditional branch also requires the counter MSB. On a cache\n  miss fetch sequentially and let EX resolve and fill it. Keep JALR on its\n  existing unpredicted EX path. Select completed cached-target and PC+4\n  addresses, removing B/J immediate extraction and target addition from\n  the IF next-PC feedback cone rather than keeping an adder as a cold-miss\n  prediction fallback. Preserve the combinational \n…[4249 of 7321 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:1d82094c4d7877ad]…\none aligned legal direct-target fill event per EX acceptance.\n      Preserve JALR, misalignment, link, divider and RVFI behavior.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: |\n      Wire EX target-fill PC/index/target/enable signals to IF alongside\n      existing direction training. Preserve the nret=1 top-level contract,\n      hazard controls, forwarding, and retirement-order generation.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Extend predictor tests with cold/warm direct targets, alternating\n      outcomes, full-PC tag collisions, cache conflicts, reset, and changed\n      B/J immediates at a trained PC. Verify exact retired PCs/next-PCs,\n      link values, traps, consecutive order and no wrong-path stores.\n      Force target mismatch and direction mismatch during imem backpressure,\n      older dmem holds and divider occupancy; assert one fill per advancing\n      legal instruction. Retain existing direction-prediction checks and\n      add a warmed-loop check proving cache hits add no fetch stage.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
