{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_7", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n d=json.loads(line)\n print({k:d.get(k) for k in ('id','category','title','outcome','fitness','fmax_mhz','cycles','lut4','ff')})\n if d.get('category')=='predictor' and 'r3s2' not in d['id']:\n  h=d['hypothesis']\n  print(h['hypothesis'] if isinstance(h,dict) else h)\n  print('NOTES:',d.get('implementation_notes'))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "{'id': 'baseline-bench-2e8305b', 'category': 'micro_opt', 'title': 'Baseline retest for cores/bench', 'outcome': 'improvement', 'fitness': 12.12, 'fmax_mhz': 5.442, 'cycles': 4491485, 'lut4': 12312, 'ff': 460}\n{'id': 'hyp-20261002-001-r1s0', 'category': 'micro_opt', 'title': 'Share a width-tapered combinational divider across RV32M operations', 'outcome': 'regression', 'fitness': 8.95, 'fmax_mhz': 4.021, 'cycles': 4491485, 'lut4': 4611, 'ff': 460}\n{'id': 'hyp-20261002-002-r1s1', 'category': 'structural', 'title': 'Move division out of the single-cycle execute path', 'outcome': 'improvement', 'fitness': 101.21, 'fmax_mhz': 45.46, 'cycles': 4491817, 'lut4': 2577, 'ff': 681}\n{'id': 'hyp-20261002-003-r1s2', 'category': 'predictor', 'title': 'Small tagged target predictor eliminates recurrent control-flow bubbles', 'outcome': 'regression', 'fitness': 13.02, 'fmax_mhz': 5.467, 'cycles': 4197517, 'lut4': 12795, 'ff': 685}\nAdd a 64-entry direct-mapped branch target buffer with an integrated\ntwo-bit saturating direction counter. Index with fetch PC[7:2]; retain\nthe full PC[31:8] tag, a word-aligned 30-bit target, a conditional versus\nunconditional type bit, and a valid bit. A matching unconditional entry\npredicts its cached target; a conditional entry predicts that target\nwhen the counter MSB is set. A miss or not-taken prediction chooses pc+4.\nInclude JAL and JALR in the same predictor, using the last resolved\ntarget for JALR, without adding a return stack or global history.\n\nCarry the exact predicted next PC alongside each accepted instruction\nthrough IF/ID and ID/EX. In EX compute the architectural next PC using\nthe existing forwarded operands, branch comparison, JALR bit-zero\nclearing, and misalignment/trap rules. Redirect and flush only when a\nvalid instruction advances out of EX and its actual next PC differs\nfrom its saved prediction. Check this equality for every instruction,\nincluding non-control and trapped instructions, so stale entries cannot\nsilently skip architectural instructions. RVFI pc_wdata always repor\n…[6876 of 9948 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:09c9c2c521bb04ec]…\npect vendor timing. Validate marker-bounded\nCoreMark with canonical CRCs and the existing formal/cosim gates. Judge\nthe proposal by median Gowin Fmax times iterations/cycle against 101.21;\na cycle reduction alone is insufficient, and acceptance requires more\nthan 4.6 percent improvement over that champion.\n\nNOTES: \n{'id': 'hyp-20261002-001-r3s0', 'category': 'micro_opt', 'title': 'Share all RV32M multiply results through one signed 33-bit product', 'outcome': 'regression', 'fitness': 133.12, 'fmax_mhz': 55.939, 'cycles': 4202272, 'lut4': 3323, 'ff': 970}\n{'id': 'hyp-20261002-002-r3s1', 'category': 'structural', 'title': 'Register fully bypassed operands before execute', 'outcome': 'improvement', 'fitness': 162.96, 'fmax_mhz': 68.482, 'cycles': 4202272, 'lut4': 3613, 'ff': 985}\n{'id': 'hyp-20261002-003-r3s2', 'category': 'predictor', 'title': 'Banked LUT-RAM direction predictor with folded PC indexing', 'outcome': 'regression', 'fitness': 125.61, 'fmax_mhz': 52.631, 'cycles': 4190183, 'lut4': 3113, 'ff': 842}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
