ed direct targets,\nparallel PC+4/target additions and unconditional aligned JAL prediction.\nKeep JALR sequential and all pipeline register boundaries unchanged.\n\nAt a valid legal aligned conditional branch's EX-to-EX/MEM acceptance,\ntrain the live indexed counter with residual = actual_taken XOR\naccepted_instruction[31]. Increment with saturation for residual one,\ndecrement with saturation for residual zero. Reuse the existing EX-to-IF\nupdate connection for this explicitly documented residual rather than\nadding a comparator or target-derived bias calculation. Narrow branch_index\nconsistently to four bits throughout IF, EX and top-level wiring. Train\nonce per EX advance and never during reset, bubbles, arithmetic occupancy\nor dmem holds. Use a simple resettable sixteen-element flop array, keeping\nthe current read/write edge semantics and no EX-outcome bypass into fetch.\nThis removes 224 counter state bits and greatly reduces asynchronous\nprediction/update selection and write-decoder fanout. It deliberately\nretains the two-bit hysteresis that a one-bit last-outcome table loses.\n\nReference replay of all 532,346 conditional branches in the canonical\nCoreMark program, including its untimed initialization/output, gives\n54,846 misses for the current 128-entry PC[8:2] bimodal table and 55,571\nfor this exact 16-entry PC[5:2] agree table, with both initialized to 01.\nThus the much smaller table adds only 725 idealized direction misses\nacross the whole program. Replay is architectural and omits wrong-path\nfetches and bus timing; obtain real marker-bounded cycles and Gowin\nmedian Fmax from an isolated RTL prototype before relying on these counts.\nThe gain should come principally from less predictor storage, muxing and\nrouting pressure, not from a claimed large branch-miss improvement.\n\nPreserve saved predicted_taken and instruction-derived direct_target,\ndirection-XOR EX correction, trap/link behavior and resolved RVFI next PC.\nAliasing changes guesses only: prediction remains qualified by valid\nBRANCH funct3 and aligned target, so other instructions cannot be skipped.\nKeep raw fetched instruction and register-file addresses independent of\nrecovery, full ID/EX clearing on invalid input or squash, and correction\npriority over younger imem/load-use stalls. Preserve registered execution\noperands, arithmetic, forwarding, memory handshakes, nret=1 IO, strict\nretirement order, canonical CRC checks and MMIO timing brackets.\n\nEstimate six percent higher fitness if the physical reduction raises\nFmax enough to offset the small accuracy cost. Vendor timing is decisive\nbecause the current worst path is outside the predictor; this is a low\nconfidence estimate until measured. Validate direct prediction and agree\ncounter saturation/reset/alias semantics, branches held under dmem stalls,\ncorrections under imem/load-use stalls, the existing formal/cosimulation\ngates, all canonical CRCs and the validation literal. Acceptance requires\nmedian Fmax times iterations/cycle more than 4.6 percent above 207.55.''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':6,'confidence':'low'},\n'changes':[\n {'file':'rtl/if_stage.sv','description':'''Replace the 128x2 bimodal flop table with a resettable 16x2 agree table\nindexed by PC[5:2]. XOR its MSB with the current B-immediate sign bit\nfor instruction-qualified conditional prediction; train saturated\ncounters from the EX residual. Preserve JAL, targets, fetch latency,\nmetadata, alignment qualification and PC stall/correction priorities.'''},\n {'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'''Narrow branch_index to four bits and select in.pc[5:2]. Send the\naccepted branch's actual_taken XOR in.instr[31] on the EX-to-IF\ntraining-outcome connection, documenting its new disagreement meaning.\nKeep the existing branch_update acceptance gate, architectural branch\ncomparison, direction-XOR recovery, operands, arithmetic and RVFI.'''},\n {'file':'rtl/core.sv','description':'''Narrow the internal branch-index wire consistently and document or\nrename the training-outcome wire as a disagreement residual. Preserve\nall stage boundaries, hazards, forwarding and the nret=1 top-level IO.'''},\n {'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Retain all invariant and regression checks. Adapt table/index and\ntraining-event expectations to 16 entries and residual outcomes. Cover\nbackward/forward cold bias, agreement/disagreement saturation, reset,\noppositely directed branches colliding at PC[5:2], simultaneous fetch\nand update to different entries, and a branch held behind dmem stalls.\nCheck recovery with imem/load-use interlocks, exact retired PC/next-PC\nsequence and order, traps, link/register values and no wrong-path stores.'''},\n]}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(h,sort_keys=False,width=88))\njsonschema.validate(h,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Refined hypothesis validates:',p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "mv: preserving permissions for ‘/srv/hwebench/tmp/6b356b5e/c42a2843/predictor_probe/branch_profile.bin’: Invalid argument\nmv: preserving permissions for ‘/srv/hwebench/tmp/6b356b5e/c42a2843/predictor_probe/coremark.dis’: Invalid argument\nRefined hypothesis validates: cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-003-r5s2.yaml\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
