{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_28","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'RTL_DIR=/srv/hwebench/tmp/6b356b5e/c42a2843/predictor_probe/recovery_control/rtl OBJ_DIR=/srv/hwebench/tmp/6b356b5e/c42a2843/predictor_probe/recovery_control/obj NRET=1 bash test/cosim/build.sh > /srv/hwebench/tmp/6b356b5e/c42a2843/predictor_probe/recovery_control/cosim-build.log 2>&1\n/srv/hwebench/tmp/6b356b5e/c42a2843/predictor_probe/recovery_control/obj/cosim_sim bench/programs/coremark.elf 10000000 --bench --istall --dstall > /srv/hwebench/tmp/6b356b5e/c42a2843/predictor_probe/recovery_control/bench.jsonl'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_29", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-003-r5s2.yaml')\nh={\n'id':'hyp-20261002-003-r5s2',\n'title':'Prediction-selected recovery without arithmetic-completion feedback',\n'category':'predictor',\n'motivation':'''The champion already eliminates direct-control bubbles with a 128-entry\nBHT and instruction-qualified JAL prediction, but its predictor recovery\nstill depends on two unnecessary late decisions. EX selects the recovery\naddress from actual_nonsequential even though a misprediction's corrected\ndirection is necessarily opposite the saved prediction. It also gates\nredirect and BHT training through ex_advance, whose \"'!busy term depends on\nmultiplier/divider completion even though a decoded branch or jump cannot\nbe an M-extension instruction. These connections enlarge recovery and\ninterlock timing cones without improving prediction accuracy. The recent\nbanked BHT proposals changed cycles by just 0.29 percent; target recovery\ncontrol instead of increasing direction-table complexity.'\"''',\n'hypothesis':'''Keep the existing 128-entry two-bit BHT, direct-JAL prediction, sequential\nJALR behavior and all pipeline boundaries. Restructure only the predictor's\nEX correction and training interface to remove arithmetic-completion\nfeedback and prepare correction addresses before actual branch resolution.\n\nRetain actual_nonsequential and saved predicted_taken. When their XOR is\none, the actual direction is opposite the accepted prediction, so select\nredirect_target from the saved prediction: predicted_taken ? (in.pc+4) :\n(in.ctrl.is_jump ? jump_target : in.direct_target). Compute this address\nindependently of branch_cond and actual_nonsequential. Direct predictions\nalready carry the same instruction-derived target used by resolution;\nJALR is never predicted and therefore still selects its computed target.\nA predicted-taken branch that exits recovers to PC+4. Preserve JALR bit-zero\nclearing, all illegal/misalignment gates, architectural PC+4 link results\nand execute_payload.pc_next selected from the actual resolved direction.\nThe new address is meaningful only when redirect is asserted.\n\nCreate a predictor-specific advancement condition in.valid && \"'!reset &&\n!stall, excluding ex_busy. Use it for redirect'\"'s direction-XOR correction\nand for the existing legal/aligned conditional branch_update event. Keep\nex_advance with \"'!busy unchanged for result forwarding, arithmetic transfer\nand every other data-path consumer. The safety argument is decoder-based:\na valid conditional branch or JAL/JALR never has an M-extension alu_op,\nand a MUL/DIV instruction always carries predicted_taken=0 and resolves\nactual_nonsequential=0. Thus arithmetic waits cannot generate a correction\nor BHT update, even though the predictor advancement term omits busy.\nOnly decoded legal conditional branches may train; retain the branch\nalignment check and current index/outcome. Document these exclusivity\nconditions and test them rather than changing arithmetic or hazard logic.\n\nLeave correction priority over younger imem/load-use stalls intact; defer\nboth recovery and training during an older dmem hold via !stall. Keep raw\nfetch bits and register-file addresses independent of recovery, full ID/EX\nclearing on invalid inputs and squash, saved prediction metadata, nret=1\nports, exact RVFI order, memory handshakes and all trap behavior. There is\nno added prediction state, pipeline stage, table-capacity change or new\nwrong-path architectural action.\n\nAn isolated prototype has 89.435 MHz option-0 Gowin Fmax versus the\nchampion'\"'s 83.021 MHz option-0 result, a 7.73 percent increase. Area is\n3,826 LUTs and 1,090 FFs versus 3,790 and 1,090, with two DSPs and the\nsame memories. Its worst option-0 arrival is 16.476 ns versus 17.339 ns.\nThis is preliminary timing evidence; median placement timing and stalled\nmarker-bounded CoreMark cycles remain decisive. Estimate an eight-percent\nfitness gain with unchanged cycles. Re-run all required formal/cosim gates,\ncanonical CRCs and validation literal, and directed correction/training\ntests involving arithmetic occupancy and bus/interlock stalls. Acceptance\nrequires more than 4.6 percent over 207.55.''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':8,'confidence':'medium'},\n'changes':[\n {'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'''Select redirect_target from the accepted predicted_taken bit and the\nopposite completed address, keeping actual direction out of its data\nmux. Gate redirect and conditional-BHT training with valid && \"'!reset &&\n!stall rather than the arithmetic-dependent ex_advance. Preserve\nex_advance for forwarding and arithmetic, all branch/jump/trap resolution,\narchitectural execute_payload.pc_next and current predictor indexing.'\"'''},\n {'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Keep all existing checks and add directed prediction-recovery coverage:\ntrained taken branches exiting to PC+4; not-taken predictions resolving\ntaken; aligned JALR correction; direct JAL; misaligned/illegal controls;\nwrong-path stores; correction overlapping imem/load-use stalls; and a\nbranch held behind older dmem stalls. Verify no redirect or BHT training\nthrough MUL/DIV waits and accepted responses, one training event per\nadvancing branch, exact retirement PC/next-PC continuity, order and links.'''},\n]}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(h,sort_keys=False,width=88))\njsonschema.validate(h,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Recovery hypothesis validates')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_29", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-003-r5s2.yaml')\nh={\n'id':'hyp-20261002-003-r5s2',\n'title':'Prediction-selected recovery without arithmetic-completion feedback',\n'category':'predictor',\n'motivation':'''The champion already eliminates direct-control bubbles with a 128-entry\nBHT and instruction-qualified JAL prediction, but its predictor recovery\nstill depends on two unnecessary late decisions. EX selects the recovery\naddress from actual_nonsequential even though a misprediction's corrected\ndirection is necessarily opposite the saved prediction. It also gates\nredirect and BHT training through ex_advance, whose \"'!busy term depends on\nmultiplier/divider completion even though a decoded branch or jump cannot\nbe an M-extension instruction. These connections enlarge recovery and\ninterlock timing cones without improving prediction accuracy. The recent\nbanked BHT proposals changed cycles by just 0.29 percent; target recovery\ncontrol instead of increasing direction-table complexity.'\"''',\n'hypothesis':'''Keep the existing 128-entry two-bit BHT, direct-JAL prediction, sequential\nJALR behavior and all pipeline boundaries. Restructure only the predictor's\nEX correction and training interface to remove arithmetic-completion\nfeedback and prepare correction addresses before actual branch resolution.\n\nRetain actual_nonsequential and saved predicted_taken. When their XOR is\none, the actual direction is opposite the accepted prediction, so select\nredirect_target from the saved prediction: predicted_taken ? (in.pc+4) :\n(in.ctrl.is_jump ? jump_target : in.direct_target). Compute this address\nindependently of branch_cond and actual_nonsequential. Direct predictions\nalready carry the same instruction-derived target used by resolution;\nJALR is never predicted