, \"fmax_mhz\": 93.05, \"levels\": 9, \"logic\": 3675, \"regs\": 1090, \"lutram\": 40, \"bsram\": 4, \"dsp\": 2, \"critical_paths\": [{\"from\": \"dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_id/reg_q.alu_b_11_s0\", \"slack_ns\": -5.747, \"arrival_ns\": 16.041, \"logic_cells\": 9, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_mem\", \"cpu/u_id\"]}, {\"from\": \"dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_id/reg_q.alu_b_19_s0\", \"slack_ns\": -5.745, \"arrival_ns\": 16.04, \"logic_cells\": 9, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_mem\", \"cpu/u_id\"]}, {\"from\": \"cpu/u_id/reg_q.alu_a_2_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_id/reg_q.alu_b_31_s0\", \"slack_ns\": -5.741, \"arrival_ns\": 16.035, \"logic_cells\": 37, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_id\"]}, {\"from\": \"cpu/u_id/reg_q.rs2_val_0_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_id/reg_q.ctrl.branch_op_0_s0\", \"slack_ns\": -5.741, \"arrival_ns\": 16.035, \"logic_cells\": 37, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_if\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_id\"]}, {\"from\": \"cpu/u_id/reg_q.ctrl.alu_op_0_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_if/counters_counters_RAMREG_0_G[7]_s0\", \"slack_ns\": -5.729, \"arrival_ns\": 16.024, \"logic_cells\": 8, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_if\"]}]}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_38", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-003-r5s2.yaml')\nh={\n'id':'hyp-20261002-003-r5s2',\n'title':'Localize prediction recovery squash to validity and control state',\n'category':'predictor',\n'motivation':'''The current predictor already avoids recurring direct-control bubbles,\nbut every EX misprediction still drives a whole-ID/EX zeroing mux. Its\nflush and invalid-fetch handling clear PC, instruction, target, operands,\nALU inputs and destination metadata as well as valid and control bits.\nPrediction recovery needs to invalidate the instruction and clear every\nside-effect control; clearing the inactive payload adds substantial\nfanout and input muxing to a timing-sensitive recovery path. Prior BHT\nbanking changed CoreMark cycles by only 0.29 percent. Reduce the physical\ncost of existing predictor recovery instead of adding table complexity.''',\n'hypothesis':'''Localize prediction recovery in ID/EX: keep the exact BHT/JAL guesses,\ndirection-XOR EX correction, resolved targets and pipeline boundaries,\nbut remove flush and fetch-validity gating from the data payload flops.\nSplit the current whole-struct ID/EX assignment into payload update and\ncontrol/valid update logic, retaining a single owner for each register bit.\n\nOn reset clear every field exactly as today. Outside reset, update PC,\ninstruction, immediate, rs1/rs2 values and addresses, alu_a/alu_b, rd,\npredicted_taken and direct_target whenever \"'!stall, using their existing\ncombinational sources. These data fields must not depend on flush or\nin.valid and may contain a wrong-path or unavailable fetch in a bubble.\nWhen stall is asserted, hold these payload fields even if flush requests\nan injected bubble. Independently, flush has priority over stall and\nclears the entire ctrl_t plus valid. Also clear ctrl_t and valid when\n!stall && !in.valid. Otherwise an unstalled valid input captures the\nexisting decoded control bundle and sets valid; a stall without flush\nholds both control and valid. This is precisely the existing architectural\nhold/bubble/advance behavior with a smaller recovery-driven register set.\n\nClearing valid alone is explicitly insufficient. Clear every ctrl_t bit,\nincluding reg_write, mem_read, mem_write, mem_to_reg, is_branch, is_jump,\nis_jalr, alu_op and is_illegal, exactly as the existing all-zero bubble.\nThe invalid instruction may retain data but must never launch arithmetic,\nforward, redirect, train the BHT, access dmem or retire. Retain EX'\"'s \"'!valid\nwhole-EX/MEM bubble insertion and all existing validity/completion gates.\nDo not modify memory, forwarding, arithmetic, hazards or decoder legality.\nAn invalid payload'\"'s preserved prediction bit cannot affect correction\nbecause ex_advance requires valid. Preserve ID/EX operand retention under\ndmem and M-extension holds, PC correction priority over younger imem and\nload-use stalls, nret=1 IO, RVFI order, trap rules and resolved pc_next.\n\nThe single predictor angle is recovery fanout: route a misprediction's\nsquash only to validity and decoded control state, allowing inactive\npayload storage to follow the ordinary stall clock-enable. No extra\nstage, table, speculation state or branch penalty is introduced. Keep\nthe existing predictor and EX implementation byte-for-byte.\n\nAn isolated RTL prototype gives option-0 Gowin Fmax 93.588 MHz versus\n83.021 MHz for the champion's option 0. Its worst arrival is 15.979 ns\nversus 17.339 ns. Area is 3,675 LUTs and 1,090 FFs versus 3,790 and\n1,090, with unchanged memories and two DSPs. Stalled canonical CoreMark\nfinishes in exactly the champion's 4,296,444 marker-bounded cycles,\nwith all five expected CRCs, the validation literal and no OOB access.\nMedian placement timing remains required before claiming a fitness gain.\nEstimate ten percent higher fitness from reduced recovery routing and\npayload input logic. Run unchanged formal/cosimulation gates and directed\nsquash/hold tests; acceptance requires more than 4.6 percent over 207.55.''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':10,'confidence':'medium'},\n'changes':[\n {'file':'rtl/id_stage.sv','description':'''Separate payload updates from control/valid updates in ID/EX.\nKeep global reset clearing every field. Payload fields capture existing\nsources on \"'!stall and hold on stall, independent of flush and in.valid.\nFlush or an unstalled invalid fetch clears all ctrl_t bits and valid;\notherwise preserve normal control capture and hold priorities. Keep\none procedural owner per bit and retain all architectural operand muxes.'\"'''},\n {'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Retain all invariant tests and add checks that every prediction squash\nand imem bubble clears valid and the entire control bundle even when\npayload bits are retained or capture unavailable/wrong-path data.\nExercise mispredicted branches followed by stores, loads, MUL/DIV,\nreserved encodings and JALR; correction with imem/load-use interlocks;\nand branches/arithmetic held behind older dmem stalls. Verify payload\nhold during stalls, no invalid arithmetic launch/forwarding/training/\nmemory/retirement, exact RVFI PC/next-PC sequence, order and trap behavior.'''},\n]}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(h,sort_keys=False,width=88))\njsonschema.validate(h,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Localized predictor recovery hypothesis validates')\nPY\npython3 -u - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport shutil,subprocess,json\nroot=Path('/srv/hwebench/tmp/6b356b5e/c42a2843/predictor_probe/recovery_squash')\nfw=root/'formal-framework'\nshutil.copytree('formal/riscv-formal',fw,ignore=shutil.ignore_patterns('.git','cores','__pycache__'),dirs_exist_ok=True)\nstaged=fw/'cores'/'probe';shutil.copytree(root/'rtl',staged,dirs_exist_ok=True)\nshutil.copyfile('formal/wrapper_si.sv',staged/'wrapper.sv')\ncfg=Path('formal/checks_si.cfg').read_text().split('[verilog-files]')[0]+'[verilog-files]\\\\n'\nfiles=sorted(p.name for p in staged.glob('*.sv'))\nfiles.remove('core_pkg.sv');files.remove('wrapper.sv')\nfor f in ['core_pkg.sv',*files,'wrapper.sv']:cfg+='@basedir@/cores/@core@/'+f+'\\\\n'\n(staged/'checks.cfg').write_text(cfg)\nr=subprocess.run(['python3','../../checks/genchecks.py'],cwd=staged,capture_output=True,text=True)\nprint('genchecks return:',r.returncode);print(r.stdout[-1000:]);print(r.stderr[-1000:]);\nif r.returncode:raise SystemExit(r.returncode)\nprint((staged/'checks'/'Makefile').read_text()[:3000])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_38", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-003-r5s2.yaml')\nh={\n'id':'hyp-20261002-003-r5s2',\n'title':'Localize prediction recovery squash to validity and control state',\n'category':'predictor',\n'motivation':'''The current predictor already avoids recurring direct-control bubbles,\nbut every EX misprediction still drives a whole-ID/EX zeroing mux. Its\nflush and invalid-fetch handling clear PC, instruction, target, operands,\nALU inputs and destination metadata as well as valid and control bits.\nPrediction recovery needs to invalidate the instruction and clear every\nside-effect control; clearing the inactive payload adds substantial\nfanout and input muxing to a timing-sensitive recovery path. Prior BHT\nbanking changed CoreMark cycles by only 0.29 percent. Reduce the physical\ncost of existing predictor recovery instead of adding table complexity.''',\n'hypothesis':'''Localize prediction recovery in ID/EX: keep the exact BHT/JAL guesses,\ndirection-XOR EX correction, resolved targets and pipeline boundaries,\nbut remove flush and fetch-validity gating from the data payload flops.\nSplit the current whole-struct ID/EX assignment into payload update and\ncontrol/valid update logic, retaining a single owner for each register bit.\n\nOn reset clear every field exactly as today. Outside reset, update PC,\ninstruction, immediate, rs1/rs2 values and addresses, alu_a/alu_b, rd,\npredicted_taken and direct_target whenever \"'!stall, using their existing\ncombinational sources. These data fields must not depend on flush or\nin.valid and may contain a wrong-path or unavailable fetch in a bubble.\nWhen stall is asserted, hold these payload fields even if flush requests\nan injected bubble. Independently, flush has priority over stall and\nclears the entire ctrl_t plus valid. Also clear ctrl_t and valid when\n!stall && !in.valid. Otherwise an unstalled valid input captures the\nexisting decoded control bundle and sets valid; a stall without flush\nholds both control and valid. This is precisely the existing architectural\nhold/bubble/advance behavior with a smaller recovery-driven register set.\n\nClearing valid alone is explicitly insufficient. Clear every ctrl_t bit,\nincluding reg_write, mem_read, mem_write, mem_to_reg, is_branch, is_jump,\nis_jalr, alu_op and is_illegal, exactly as the existing all-zero bubble.\nThe invalid instruction may retain data but must never launch arithmetic,\nforward, redirect, train the BHT, access dmem or retire. Retain EX'\"'s \"'!valid\nwhole-EX/MEM bubble insertion and all existing validity/completion gates.\nDo not modify memory, forwarding, arithmetic, hazards or decoder legality.\nAn invalid payload'\"'s preserved prediction bit cannot affect correction\nbecause ex_advance requires valid. Preserve ID/EX operand retention under\ndmem and M-extension holds, PC correction priority over younger imem and\nload-use stalls, nret=1 IO, RVFI order, trap rules and resolved pc_next.\n\nThe single predictor angle is recovery fanout: route a misprediction's\nsquash only to validity and decoded control state, allowing inactive\npayload storage to follow the ordinary stall clock-enable. No extra\nstage, table, speculation state or branch penalty is introduced. Keep\nthe existing predictor and EX implementation byte-for-byte.\n\nAn isolated RTL prototype gives option-0 Gowin Fmax 93.588 MHz versus\n83.021 MHz for the champion's option 0. Its worst arrival is 15.979 ns\nversus 17.339 ns. Area is 3,675 LUTs and 1,090 FFs versus 3,790 and\n1,090, with unchanged memories and two DSPs. Stalled canonical CoreMark\nfinishes in exactly the champion's 4,296,444 marker-bounded cycles,\nwith all five expected CRCs, the validation literal and no OOB access.\nMedian placement timing remains required before claiming a fitness gain.\nEstimate ten percent higher fitness from reduced recovery routing and\npayload input logic. Run unchanged formal/cosimulation gates and directed\nsquash/hold tests; acceptance requires more than 4.6 percent over 207.55.''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':10,'confidence':'medium'},\n'changes':[\n {'file':'rtl/id_stage.sv','description':'''Separate payload updates from control/valid updates in ID/EX.\nKeep global reset clearing every field. Payload fields capture existing\nsources on \"'!stall and hold on stall, independent of flush and in.valid.\nFlush or an unstalled invalid fetch clears all ctrl_t bits and valid;\notherwise preserve normal control capture and hold priorities. Keep\none procedural owner per bit and retain all architectural operand muxes.'\"'''},\n {'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Retain all invariant tests and add checks that every prediction squash\nand imem bubble clears valid and the entire control bundle even when\npayload bits are retained or capture unavailable/wrong-path data.\nExercise mispredicted branches followed by stores, loads, MUL/DIV,\nreserved encodings and JALR; correction with imem/load-use interlocks;\nand branches/arithmetic held behind older dmem stalls. Verify payload\nhold during stalls, no invalid arithmetic launch/forwarding/training/\nmemory/retirement, exact RVFI PC/next-PC sequence, order and trap behavior.'''},\n]}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(h,sort_keys=False,width=88))\njsonschema.validate(h,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Localized predictor recovery hypothesis validates')\nPY\npython3 -u - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport shutil,subprocess,json\nroot=Path('/srv/hwebench/tmp/6b356b5e/c42a2843/predictor_probe/recovery_squash')\nfw=root/'formal-framework'\nshutil.copytree('formal/riscv-formal',fw,ignore=shutil.ignore_patterns('.git','cores','__pycache__'),dirs_exist_ok=True)\nstaged=fw/'cores'/'probe';shutil.copytree(root/'rtl',staged,dirs_exist_ok=True)\nshutil.copyfile('formal/wrapper_si.sv',staged/'wrapper.sv')\ncfg=Path('formal/checks_si.cfg').read_text().split('[verilog-files]')[0]+'[verilog-files]\\\\n'\nfiles=sorted(p.name for p in staged.glob('*.sv'))\nfiles.remove('core_pkg.sv');files.remove('wrapper.sv')\nfor f in ['core_pkg.sv',*files,'wrapper.sv']:cfg+='@basedir@/cores/@core@/'+f+'\\\\n'\n(staged/'checks.cfg').write_text(cfg)\nr=subprocess.run(['python3','../../checks/genchecks.py'],cwd=staged,capture_output=True,text=True)\nprint('genchecks return:',r.returncode);print(r.stdout[-1000:]);print(r.stderr[-1000:]);\nif r.returncode:raise SystemExit(r.returncode)\nprint((staged/'checks'/'Makefile').read_text()[:3000])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "Localized predictor recovery hypothesis validates\ngenchecks return: 0\nReading checks.cfg.\nCreating checks directory.\nGenerated 53 checks.\n\n\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"<stdin>\", line 16, in <module>\n  File \"/opt/hwe-python/cpython-3.13.12-linux-x86_64-gnu/lib/python3.13/pathlib/_local.py\", line 546, in read_text\n    return PathBase.read_text(self, encoding, errors, newline)\n           ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/opt/hwe-python/cpython-3.13.12-linux-x86_64-gnu/lib/python3.13/pathlib/_abc.py\", line 632, in read_text\n    with self.open(mode='r', encoding=encoding, errors=errors, newline=newline) as f:\n         ~~~~~~~~~^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/opt/hwe-python/cpython-3.13.12-linux-x86_64-gnu/lib/python3.13/pathlib/_local.py\", line 537, in open\n    return io.open(self, mode, buffering, encoding, errors, newline)\n           ~~~~~~~^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\nFileNotFoundError: [Errno 2] No such file or directory: '/srv/hwebench/tmp/6b356b5e/c42a2843/predictor_probe/recovery_squash/formal-framework/cores/probe/checks/Makefile'\n", "exit_code": 1, "status": "failed"}}
