{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_2", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"git status --short; rg -n '\\\"category\\\":\\\\s*\\\"predictor\\\"|branch.predict|BHT|gshare|return.address|return stack|RAS|BTB' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "4:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261002-003-r1s2\", \"title\": \"Small tagged target predictor eliminates recurrent control-flow bubbles\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The baseline always fetches pc+4 and redirects in EX for every taken\\nconditional branch, JAL, or JALR. Since IF/ID is combinational rather\\nthan a separate register, each redirect discards one younger instruction\\nand inserts a bubble. CoreMark repeatedly executes loops and stable\\ndirect jumps, so many of these bubbles should be predictable. The sole\\nrecorded experiment has 4,491,485 measured cycles and 5.442 MHz median\\nFmax. Its critical path runs through forwarding and the combinational\\narithmetic unit, so this proposal targets iterations per cycle while\\nkeeping predictor logic small enough to avoid reducing Fmax. There are\\nno recorded predictor experiments or LESSONS.md takeaways in this fixture.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The baseline always fetches pc+4 and redirects in EX for every taken\\nconditional branch, JAL, or JALR. Since IF/ID is combinational rather\\nthan a separate register, each redirect discards one younger instruction\\nand inserts a bubble. CoreMark repeatedly executes loops and stable\\ndirect jumps, so many of these bubbles should be predictable. The sole\\nrecorded experiment has 4,491,485 measured cycles and 5.442 MHz median\\nFmax. Its critical path runs through forwarding and the combinational\\narithmetic unit, so this proposal targets iterations per cycle while\\nkeeping predictor logic small enough to avoid reducing Fmax. There are\\nno recorded predictor experiments or LESSONS.md takeaways in this fixture.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a 64-entry direct-mapped branch target buffer with an integrated\\ntwo-bit saturating direction counter. Index with fetch PC[7:2]; retain\\nthe full PC[31:8] tag, a word-aligned 30-bit target, a conditional versus\\nunconditional type bit, and a valid bit. A matching unconditional entry\\npredicts its cached target; a conditional entry predicts that target\\nwhen the counter MSB is set. A miss or not-ta\n…[70437 of 73509 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:bb66921f0f9de6b1]…\nement\", \"fitness\": 218.36, \"delta_pct\": 5.21, \"vs_baseline\": 1701.65, \"fmax_mhz\": 93.817, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4296444, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 3675, \"ff\": 1090, \"seeds\": [90.815, 93.817, 93.817], \"perturbations\": [[0, 90.815, 10], [1, 93.817, 13], [2, 93.817, 13]], \"lutram\": 40, \"bsram\": 4, \"dsp\": 2, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_id/reg_q.alu_a_30_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_id/reg_q.alu_b_7_s0\", \"slack_ns\": -6.011, \"arrival_ns\": 16.306, \"logic_cells\": 10, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_id\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 10, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-02T19:10:16.352646Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 5, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-10-02 hyp-20261002-003-r5s2 (improvement, +5.21%): Keeping full reset but limiting ID/EX flush/invalid-fetch clearing to ctrl_t, valid and predicted_taken while preserving payload stall holds reduces recovery muxing and fanout, improving Fmax and LUT use with unchanged CoreMark cycles.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'for p in /AGENTS.md /srv/AGENTS.md /srv/hwebench/AGENTS.md /srv/hwebench/clones/AGENTS.md /srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6_1-sol_xhigh-v2-rep6/AGENTS.md /srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6_1-sol_xhigh-v2-rep6/cores/AGENTS.md /srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6_1-sol_xhigh-v2-rep6/cores/bench/AGENTS.md AGENTS.md; do if [ -f \"$p\" ]; then cat \"$p\"; fi; done; cat cores/bench/LESSONS.md; cat schemas/hypothesis.schema.json'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_3", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'for p in /AGENTS.md /srv/AGENTS.md /srv/hwebench/AGENTS.md /srv/hwebench/clones/AGENTS.md /srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6_1-sol_xhigh-v2-rep6/AGENTS.md /srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6_1-sol_xhigh-v2-rep6/cores/AGENTS.md /srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6_1-sol_xhigh-v2-rep6/cores/bench/AGENTS.md AGENTS.md; do if [ -f \"$p\" ]; then cat \"$p\"; fi; done; cat cores/bench/LESSONS.md; cat schemas/hypothesis.schema.json'", "aggregated_output": "- 2026-10-02 hyp-20261002-002-r1s1 (improvement, +735.07%): Moving combinational DIV/REM (`/` and `%`) out of the shared ALU into a registered iterative divider removes their timing cost from ordinary instructions, letting Fmax gains outweigh CoreMark's added divide stalls.\n- 2026-10-02 hyp-20261002-002-r2s1 (regression, +7.45%): Registering elastic IF/ID removes redirect-to-decode feedback, but the added taken-branch refill cycle raised CoreMark cycles 6.45%, limiting a 14.39% Fmax gain to 7.45% fitness.\n- 2026-10-02 hyp-20261002-003-r2s2 (improvement, +13.63%): Instruction-qualified BHT/JAL prediction removes recurring CoreMark control bubbles, while saved direct targets enable direction-XOR recovery and full ID/EX control clearing keeps correction out of decode/register-file read paths.\n- 2026-10-02 hyp-20261002-001-r3s0 (regression, +15.76%): Opcode-selected sign-extension bits on one signed 33-by-33 product and a shared high-half case arm cut Gowin DSP usage from six to two and shorten the multiplier/result-mux path without changing CoreMark cycles.\n- 2026-10-02 hyp-20261002-002-r3s1 (improvement, +41.70%): Capturing bypass-resolved rs1/rs2 and final alu_a/alu_b in ID/EX removes the shared register-file/forwarding timing prefix from both multiplier and branch-recovery paths without adding a pipeline stage.\n- 2026-10-02 hyp-20261002-003-r3s2 (regression, +9.23%): Resetting validity bits instead of two-bit BHT payloads makes banked asynchronous-read arrays LUT-RAM eligible without adding fetch latency, but the unchanged ALU/forwarding critical path limits gains compared with operand-path retiming.\n- 2026-10-02 hyp-20261002-001-r4s0 (regression, +14.05%): A balanced tree of two-bit equality/less-than leaves fits four-input LUTs and shortens the EX branch comparator carry-chain path without changing CoreMark cycles, shifting the timing limit to ALU-result-to-ID forwarding.\n- 2026-10-02 hyp-20261002-002-r4s1 (improvement, +27.36%): Routing MUL/MULH/MULHU/MULHSU through a single registered response breaks the comb\n…[1366 of 4438 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:86037fb02cdcff43]…\nnLength\": 5},\n    \"category\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"micro_opt\",\"structural\",\"extension\",\"predictor\",\"memory\"]},\n    \"motivation\":  {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 20},\n    \"hypothesis\":  {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 20},\n    \"expected_impact\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"required\": [\"fitness_delta_pct\",\"confidence\"],\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"fitness_delta_pct\": {\"type\": \"integer\"},\n        \"confidence\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"low\",\"medium\",\"high\"]}\n      }\n    },\n    \"changes\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\", \"minItems\": 1,\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"required\": [\"file\",\"description\"],\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"file\":        {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"description\": \"Must be under rtl/ (any extension) or be a test/test_*.py cocotb suite. Anything else is rejected by the runtime sandbox check.\",\n            \"pattern\": \"^(rtl/[^.].*|test/test_[^/]+\\\\.py)$\"\n          },\n          \"description\": {\"type\": \"string\"}\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
