{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_44","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor l in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n d=json.loads(l)\n if d['id']=='hyp-20261002-001-r4s0':\n  print(d['hypothesis']['hypothesis']);print({k:d[k] for k in ('fitness','fmax_mhz','cycles')})\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_44","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor l in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n d=json.loads(l)\n if d['id']=='hyp-20261002-001-r4s0':\n  print(d['hypothesis']['hypothesis']);print({k:d[k] for k in ('fitness','fmax_mhz','cycles')})\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"Replace the EX branch unit's wide relational operators with an explicitly\nbalanced comparison tree suited to four-input FPGA LUTs. Preserve the\npipeline boundaries, predictor, exact branch outcomes and all instruction\nlatencies. This is a local Boolean implementation change to comparison,\nintended to raise Fmax while preserving CoreMark iterations per cycle.\n\nCompute equality and unsigned less-than for sixteen independent two-bit\nslices of the registered rs1/rs2 operands. Each leaf has four operand\ninputs. Combine adjacent low/high groups in four balanced levels using\neq = eq_high & eq_low and\nlt = lt_high | (eq_high & lt_low).\nReproduce the measured prototype with packed 31-bit eq/lt node vectors:\nleaves occupy indices 15+i for operand slice [2*i +: 2], i=0..15;\ninternal node n=0..14 combines high child 2*n+2 and low child 2*n+1.\nNode zero is the root. This layout keeps the most significant operand\nslices on each group's high child.\nThe root supplies whole-word equality and unsigned less-than. Derive\nsigned less-than as (rs1[31] ^ rs2[31]) ? rs1[31] : unsigned_less.\nUse these shared facts for BEQ/BNE, BLT/BGE and BLTU/BGEU, complementing\nonly the matching legal predicate; retain false for unsupported branch\nfunct3 values. Express the tree with static generate indices or explicit\nlevels so synthesis sees bounded local comparisons rather than a new\n32-bit ripple comparator. Do not replace comparison with a full-width\nsubtractor whose carry propagation recreates the long path.\n\nKeep target alignment faults, branch training on actual acceptance,\ndirection-XOR correction, EX/MEM and ID/EX hold/flush priorities,\nbypass producer validity, divider protocol and RVFI metadata intact.\nPreserve nret=1, decoder default-illegal behavior and all correctness\nchecks. Validate all six branch conditions with equality, differing\nsigns and differences at every bit position, including misaligned\ntaken targets and independent instruction/data bus stalls. Run the\nunchanged formal and stalled CoreMark gates and inspect vendor timing\nto confirm the comparator/recovery path actually becomes shorter.\nExpected gain is 14 percent in fitness, supported by the local prototype\nrather than an extrapolation from the previous champion's circuit.\nThe prototype's new limiting paths cross ALU-result-to-ID forwarding;\nleave that separate opportunity for a later hypothesis. Full pipeline\nriscv-formal remains an implementation gate; the local SAT proof covers\ncomparator equivalence and does not replace that gate. Acceptance\nrequires fitness above 170.46, accounting for the 4.6 percent margin.\n\n{'fitness': 185.85, 'fmax_mhz': 78.099, 'cycles': 4202272}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_45","type":"agent_message","text":"The smaller tables and delayed feedback also fall below the champion. An earlier balanced comparator improved recovery timing, but it was tested before the registered multiplier removed another timing limit. I’ll check that approach on the current core, with prediction polarity folded into the comparison operation."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_46","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport shutil\nfor name in ('r8s2_tree','r8s2_predicate_tree'):\n root=Path('cores/bench/generated')/name;rtl=root/'rtl';rtl.mkdir(parents=True,exist_ok=True)\n for p in Path('cores/bench/rtl').glob('*.sv'):shutil.copy2(p,rtl/p.name)\n p=rtl/'ex_stage.sv';s=p.read_text()\n start=s.index('  always_comb begin\\\\n    case (in.ctrl.branch_op)')\n end=s.index('    branch_taken  =',start)\n block='''  logic [30:0] cmp_eq, cmp_lt;\n  logic signed_less;\n  for (genvar i = 0; i < 16; i++) begin: cmp_leaf\n    assign cmp_eq[15+i] = (rs1[2*i +: 2] == rs2[2*i +: 2]);\n    assign cmp_lt[15+i] = (rs1[2*i +: 2] < rs2[2*i +: 2]);\n  end\n  for (genvar i = 0; i < 15; i++) begin: cmp_node\n    assign cmp_eq[i] = cmp_eq[2*i+2] & cmp_eq[2*i+1];\n    assign cmp_lt[i] = cmp_lt[2*i+2] | (cmp_eq[2*i+2] & cmp_lt[2*i+1]);\n  end\n  assign signed_less = (rs1[31] \"'^ rs2[31]) ? rs1[31] : cmp_lt[0];\n  always_comb begin\n    case (in.ctrl.branch_op)\n      BR_BEQ:  branch_cond = cmp_eq[0];\n      BR_BNE:  branch_cond = !cmp_eq[0];\n      BR_BLT:  branch_cond = signed_less;\n      BR_BGE:  branch_cond = !signed_less;\n      BR_BLTU: branch_cond = cmp_lt[0];\n      BR_BGEU: branch_cond = !cmp_lt[0];\n      default: branch_cond = 1'\"'b0;\n    endcase\n'''\n s=s[:start]+block+s[end:]\n if name=='r8s2_predicate_tree':\n  s=s.replace('case (in.ctrl.branch_op)','case (in.prediction_cmp_op)')\n  s=s.replace('branch_cond =','branch_error =')\n  s=s.replace('logic        branch_cond;', 'logic        branch_cond;\\\\n  logic        branch_error;')\n  s=s.replace('    branch_taken  =', '    branch_cond = branch_error \"'^ in.predicted_taken;'\"\\\\n    branch_taken  =')\n  s=s.replace('assign redirect = ex_advance && (actual_nonsequential \"'^ in.predicted_taken);'\"', '''assign redirect = ex_advance\n                    && ((in.ctrl.is_branch && \"'!in.ctrl.is_illegal\n                         && branch_target[1:0] == 2'\"'b00)\n                        ? branch_error\n                        : (actual_nonsequential \"'^ in.predicted_taken));'\"''')\n  pp=rtl/'core_pkg.sv';sp=pp.read_text()\n  anchor='''    logic        predicted_taken;\n    logic [31:0] direct_target;\n    logic        valid;\n  } id_ex_t;'''\n  sp=sp.replace(anchor, '''    logic        predicted_taken;\n    logic [2:0]  prediction_cmp_op;\n    logic [31:0] direct_target;\n    logic        valid;\n  } id_ex_t;''');pp.write_text(sp)\n  pp=rtl/'id_stage.sv';sp=pp.read_text()\n  sp=sp.replace(\\\"reg_q.predicted_taken <= 1'b0;\\\", \\\"reg_q.predicted_taken <= 1'b0;\\\\n        reg_q.prediction_cmp_op <= '0;\\\")\n  sp=sp.replace('reg_q.predicted_taken <= in.predicted_taken;', \\\"reg_q.predicted_taken <= in.predicted_taken;\\\\n        reg_q.prediction_cmp_op <= dec_branch_op \"'^ {2'\"'b0, in.predicted_taken};\\\")\n  pp.write_text(sp)\n p.write_text(s)\nprint('Prepared comparator recovery probes')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
