{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_60", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-003-r8s2.yaml'", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20261002-003-r8s2\ntitle: \"Isolate branch prediction recovery from EX operand admission\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The champion scores 218.36 iterations/sec at 93.817 MHz with 4,296,444\n  marker-bounded CoreMark cycles. Predictor banking and folded indexing\n  saved only 0.29 percent of cycles, while one-bit agree prediction and\n  removing redirect from stall enables regressed fitness. The latest\n  vendor path still crosses registered EX rs2, recovery-related EX logic,\n  ID operand selection and an ID ALU-input register. EX currently shares\n  conditional-branch misalignment and jump misalignment in ctrl_with_trap,\n  then uses that bundle to qualify every ordinary bypass and arithmetic\n  launch. A conditional branch never writes a register, so its comparison\n  need not influence whether a younger instruction receives an EX result.\nhypothesis: |\n  Isolate predictor resolution and its conditional-target trap decision\n  from EX producer qualification, preserving the current 128x2 BHT,\n  predictions, direction-XOR correction, targets and pipeline boundaries.\n  The single angle is shortening the branch-recovery timing cone: a\n  conditional comparator must govern correction, training outcome and the\n  retiring branch's trap, but must not govern EX bypass admission or the\n  acceptance of an unrelated arithmetic producer.\n\n  In EX derive separate legal producer predicates directly from registered\n  ID/EX controls. An ordinary producer is permitted only when reg_write,\n  !is_illegal, !is_branch and !mem_read hold, its rd is nonzero, EX advances,\n  and either it is not a jump or its resolved jump target is aligned.\n  Use the existing jump-target misalignment check, including JALR bit-zero\n  clearing, to suppress a trapping jump's link bypass. Do not use the\n  combined misalign_fault or ctrl_with_trap.is_illegal in this predicate.\n  Keep the exact data/rd mux and EX-over-MEM forwarding priority unchanged.\n\n  Arithmetic launches similarly require valid, decoded multiply/divide,\n  reg_write, !is_illegal, !is_br\n…[2278 of 5350 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:f0bff9b677425242]…\nitness_delta_pct: 8\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Separate registered-control EX producer and arithmetic-launch\n      qualification from conditional-branch recovery/trap logic. Preserve\n      jump-alignment suppression of link bypass, saved-response completion\n      checks, bypass data and rd selection, branch comparison and final\n      trap-adjusted execute payload. Express legal aligned branch and jump\n      next-PC selection as parallel cases without a shared conditional\n      misalignment dependency; retain predictions and EX acceptance gates.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Retain existing assertions and add directed prediction corrections\n      beside dependent ALU operations, taken versus not-taken misaligned\n      branches, misaligned JAL/JALR link suppression, aligned link bypass,\n      arithmetic response holds and imem/dmem stalls. Check exact RVFI\n      operands, PCs, next PCs, trap/results/order and accepted memory effects.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
