0', 'to': 'cpu/u_id/reg_q.alu_b_7_s0', 'slack_ns': -6.011, 'arrival_ns': 16.306, 'logic_cells': 10, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_id']}\nhyp-20261002-001-r6s0 Factor AND OR XOR into one four-input-LUT ALU result family {'from': 'cpu/u_id/reg_q.rs2_val_0_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_if/counters_counters_RAMREG_0_G[67]_s0', 'slack_ns': -6.018, 'arrival_ns': 16.313, 'logic_cells': 37, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'c\n…[1238 of 4310 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:e53f3b90138404e4]…\nfrom': 'cpu/u_id/reg_q.rs2_val_0_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_id/reg_q.alu_b_2_s0', 'slack_ns': -7.016, 'arrival_ns': 17.311, 'logic_cells': 38, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_id']}\nhyp-20261002-001-r8s0 Match forwarding destinations in parallel using one held M tag {'from': 'dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s', 'to': 'cpu/u_id/reg_q.alu_b_22_s0', 'slack_ns': -6.637, 'arrival_ns': 16.931, 'logic_cells': 10, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_mem', 'cpu/u_id']}\nhyp-20261002-002-r8s1 Resolve control-flow recovery from registered EX/MEM transactions {'from': 'cpu/u_id/reg_q.alu_a_23_s0', 'to': 'dmem_2_dmem_2_0_0_s', 'slack_ns': -6.284, 'arrival_ns': 16.579, 'logic_cells': 10, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex']}\nhyp-20261002-003-r8s2 Register lookahead direction lookup without adding a fetch stage {'from': 'cpu/u_id/reg_q.rs2_val_0_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_ex/u_div/state_q_0_s1', 'slack_ns': -7.89, 'arrival_ns': 18.185, 'logic_cells': 38, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_mul', 'cpu/u_ex/u_div']}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_19", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 -B - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-003-r9s2.yaml')\nd={\n'id':'hyp-20261002-003-r9s2',\n 'title':'Fold saved prediction into a balanced branch-miss comparator',\n 'category':'predictor',\n 'motivation':'''The champion already predicts direct JAL and conditional branches. A canonical reference profile finds only 13,735 returns in 2,922,015 timed instructions, so perfect return prediction could remove at most 0.32 percent of the champion's 4,296,444 cycles. Previous folded indexing saved only 0.29 percent of cycles, while agree tables and registered direction lookup reduced Fmax. Recent worst paths repeatedly traverse a 37-38-cell EX operand-to-prediction-recovery feedback cone. An earlier balanced comparator shortened that cone before the multiplier was registered; revisit it as a prediction-relative recovery circuit on the current champion, with the saved direction folded into registered comparison polarity.''',\n 'hypothesis':'''Keep the current 128-entry two-bit BHT, direct JAL prediction, fetch topology and one-cycle EX recovery. Replace generic branch-condition-then-direction-XOR recovery with one balanced, prediction-relative branch check. In ID, compute and register branch_miss_invert = decoded branch_op[0] XOR the accepted predicted_taken bit. This folds BEQ/BNE or LT/GE complement and prediction direction before the operand comparison, rather than placing both decisions after it. Capture and hold this bit with its instruction; clear it on control squash and invalid fetch exactly as predicted_taken.\n\nIn EX, construct equality and less-than from sixteen two-bit operand leaves and a balanced reduction tree. Each leaf produces equality and unsigned less-than of its two bits. Combine high and low groups with EQ = EQ_hi AND EQ_lo and LT = LT_hi OR (EQ_hi AND LT_lo), using four reduction levels. For signed BLT/BGE, invert the sign bit of both operands in the highest leaf; other bits and unsigned BLTU/BGEU use ordinary ordering. Select root EQ for BEQ/BNE and root LT for the other legal branches using registered branch controls. Actual branch_cond is this base relation XOR branch_op[0]; branch direction miss is the same relation XOR the registered branch_miss_invert. Share the comparator rather than duplicating a carry-chain comparison for training or architectural outcome. Use portable RTL, with no vendor primitive or syn_keep forcing.\n\nGate the conditional correction with the instruction's legal branch classification and direct-target alignment, independently of operand-dependent trap qualification. For an aligned legal branch, redirect exactly when the prediction-relative direction check says miss. For a trapped or unaligned branch, actual flow remains sequential and correction equals saved predicted_taken, preserving recovery even for an inconsistent synthetic prediction. Non-branch correction uses the legal aligned jump decision XOR predicted_taken, independent of conditional branch operands. Qualify all corrections with the unchanged valid EX acceptance event. Do not defer correction to MEM or add another pipeline stage.\n\nCompute architectural branch outcome, misalignment traps, resolved pc_next and BHT training from the actual relation. Preserve all illegal/default decoder checks, link write suppression, independently resolved JALR, once-per-acceptance BHT saturation updates and current target selection. Keep all arithmetic, bypass selection, regfile, hazard priorities, payload stall enables and memory handshakes unchanged. This is one predictor-recovery redesign; no return stack, target cache, global history, direction-table resizing or unrelated datapath optimization.\n\nExpect approximately six percent higher fitness from shortening the comparator/recovery cone while preserving CoreMark instruction count, prediction decisions and cycle count. Confidence is low because the ordinary ALU-to-ID feedback can remain the timing limit. At unchanged 4,296,444 cycles, acceptance requires median vendor Fmax above 98.133 MHz and fitness above 228.40456 iter/sec. Verify the actual median Fmax times marker-bounded iterations/cycle, rather than extrapolating from logic depth. Directed tests must cover all six comparisons with both saved directions, signed/unsigned boundaries, equal operands, low-bit-only differences, misaligned targets, reset, stalls and wrong-path stores. Require unchanged nret=1 IO, exact RVFI operands/PC/trap/order and all existing formal/cosim and canonical CRC/UART/MMIO gates.''',\n 'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':6,'confidence':'low'},\n 'changes':[\n {'file':'rtl/core_pkg.sv','description':'Add one branch_miss_invert bit to id_ex_t; retain all architectural operands, direct targets and downstream RVFI fields.'},\n {'file':'rtl/id_stage.sv','description':'Register decoded branch polarity XOR accepted prediction direction before EX comparison. Hold it with ID/EX and clear it with control/valid/prediction squash; preserve all operand and payload enables.'},\n {'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'Share a balanced two-bit-leaf equality/less-than tree between actual branch outcome and prediction-relative miss. Use the saved polarity for branch recovery, factor alignment/legal classification before miss gating, and retain EX acceptance, traps, architectural PC and training semantics.'},\n {'file':'test/test_ex_stage.py','description':'Update ID/EX packing and test all six legal branch relations against both prediction directions, signed/unsigned corner cases, each operand-bit position, target alignment, jumps and holds. Preserve existing arithmetic and trap checks.'},\n {'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'Update ID/EX metadata layout and add prediction-relative recovery cases with independent bus stalls and competing writes. Retain exact retirement, link, operand, trap, order, payload-hold and wrong-path-memory assertions; confirm unchanged warmed-branch cycle behavior.'}\n ]}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=80))\nimport json,jsonschema\njsonschema.validate(d,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Revised hypothesis is schema valid.')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
