{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_56","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python3 -B - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-003-r9s2.yaml')\nd=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text());d['title']='Pipeline training into a compact banked bimodal predictor'\nd['motivation']+=' Isolated prototypes found that banking alone reduced area by 152 LUTs and 128 flip-flops but reached only 89.252 MHz, and posting training into the original flop table reached only 84.355 MHz. The proposed combination targets both predictor routing/state pressure and the combinational training prefix; neither isolated optimization is claimed to beat the champion.'\nd['hypothesis']=d['hypothesis'].replace('between the existing EX acceptance interface and the unchanged BHT update logic','between the existing EX acceptance interface and a compact banked BHT update port').replace('retain the BHT\\\\'s current reset to weakly not taken','retain the BHT\\\\'s logical reset to weakly not taken').replace('existing 128-entry two-bit table','128-entry two-bit table')\nd['hypothesis']=d['hypothesis'].replace('No table banking, folded index, alternative encoding, outcome-to-fetch bypass or registered fetch lookup.','No folded index, alternative counter encoding, outcome-to-fetch bypass or registered fetch lookup.')\ninsert='''\n\nImplement the BHT as eight explicitly generated banks of sixteen two-bit counter payloads. Select bank with index[6:4] and row with index[3:0], retaining PC[8:2] for both fetch and training. Each bank has a 16-bit resettable valid vector; its counter payload array has no reset so Gowin can infer asynchronous-read, synchronous-write LUT RAM. An invalid fetch or update row behaves as 2'b01. The first queued taken update therefore writes 2'b10, and a not-taken update writes 2'b00. Read fetch and training rows independently. Select completed bank counters for fetch, parallel with the existing target additions. Payload writes are unconditional on saturation whenever \"'!reset && train_valid_q selects the bank; compute next_counter combinationally from the current valid-qualified row and write even when the saturated value is unchanged. Reset and update validity in a separate always_ff block. Preserve bank/row shape and this memory inference pattern; do not replace it with vendor primitives or reset counter arrays.\n'\"'''\nd['hypothesis']=d['hypothesis'].replace('\\\\n\\\\nFetch keeps',insert+'\\\\n\\\\nFetch keeps')\nd['changes'][0]['description']='Register accepted EX branch events and apply each prior transaction once through the update port of eight 16-row LUT-RAM counter banks. Reset only pending validity and per-bank valid bits; invalid counters logically equal 01. Preserve PC[8:2], exact live two-bit saturation, dual fetch/update row reads, ordinary IF prediction and all PC priorities.'\nd['changes'][1]['description']+=' Cover invalid uninitialized payload masking, every bank/row, reset and first-update behavior, simultaneous fetch/update on different rows and banks, and same-row old-data behavior.'\nd['expected_impact']={'fitness_delta_pct':6,'confidence':'low'}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=80));jsonschema.validate(d,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nassert d['id']=='hyp-20261002-003-r9s2' and d['category']=='predictor'\nprint('Final combined predictor hypothesis written and schema validated.')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
