{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_10", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nrows=[json.loads(line) for line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines()]\nfor r in rows:\n print(r['id'], r.get('category'),r.get('title'), '|', r.get('fitness'),r.get('fmax_mhz'),r.get('cycles'),r.get('lut4'))\n print('critical:',r.get('critical_path'))\n if r.get('category')=='micro_opt' and not r['id'].startswith('baseline'):\n  h=r.get('hypothesis',{})\n  print('proposal:', h.get('hypothesis') if isinstance(h,dict) else h)\n  print('notes:',r.get('implementation_notes',''))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "baseline-bench-2e8305b micro_opt Baseline retest for cores/bench | 12.12 5.442 4491485 12312\ncritical: {'from': 'cpu/u_mem/reg_q.rd_3_s0', 'to': 'dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s', 'slack_ns': -189.542, 'arrival_ns': 199.837, 'logic_cells': 156, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_fwd', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex']}\nhyp-20261002-001-r1s0 micro_opt Share a width-tapered combinational divider across RV32M operations | 8.95 4.021 4491485 4611\ncritical: {'from': 'cpu/u_id/reg_q.rs2_addr_0_s0', 'to': 'dmem_1_dmem_1_0_0_s', 'slack_ns': -248.428, 'arrival_ns': 258.722, 'logic_cells': 375, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_fwd', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex']}\nproposal: Replace only the real DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU datapath with one combinational\nunsigned restoring divider that produces quotient and remainder together.\nKeep the existing pipeline, forwarding and bus-handshake behavior, with\nno extra cycles for any instruction. For signed operations, convert both\noperands to unsigned 32-bit magnitudes before the divider, then negate the\nquotient when operand signs differ and negate the remainder only when the\ndividend is negative. Unsigned operations use the original operand bits.\n\nMake the 32 unrolled restoring stages explicitly width-tapered. At stage\nk=1..32, append dividend bit 32-k to the previous remainder to form a\nk-bit trial remainder. Subtract divisor[k-1:0] once using a k+1-bit\nzero-extended subtraction. Accept its low k bits and set quotient bit\n32-k only when the subtraction has no borrow and every divisor bit above\nk-1 is zero; otherwise retain the trial remainder and emit quotient zero.\nAt k=32 the upper-divisor predicate is constant true. Use the subtraction's\nborrow bit instead of a separate magnitude comparator, and use static\ngenerate widths so early stages contain only the necessary carry logic.\nThe final stage supplies both results; do not infer another '%' circuit.\n\nPreserve division-by-zero results explicitly (quotient 0xffffffff,\nremainder original dividend) and signed INT_MIN/-1 results (quotient\n\n…[36992 of 40064 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:42b6e431ab2c12f3]…\nely 98.133 MHz median Fmax\nat that cycle count. Run all three canonical Gowin placement options and\nthe unchanged formal, stalled RVFI cosimulation, real arithmetic and\ncanonical CoreMark CRC/UART/MMIO/bracket/bounded-memory gates. Prototype\ntiming is preliminary and does not replace those implementation gates.\n\nnotes: \nhyp-20261002-002-r9s1 structural Decouple predicted fetch with an independently written circular instruction queue | 225.27 92.585 4110006 3851\ncritical: {'from': 'cpu/u_id/reg_q.alu_a_2_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_id/reg_q.alu_b_29_s0', 'slack_ns': -5.914, 'arrival_ns': 16.208, 'logic_cells': 36, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_id']}\nhyp-20261002-003-r9s2 predictor Four-bank bimodal predictor with registered training transactions | 190.67 81.919 4296444 3470\ncritical: {'from': 'cpu/u_id/reg_q.ctrl.alu_op_0_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_id/reg_q.rs2_val_17_s0', 'slack_ns': -7.277, 'arrival_ns': 17.572, 'logic_cells': 11, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_fwd', 'cpu/u_id']}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
