{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_43", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n 'reuse|architectural operand|duplicate.*register' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl --only-matching | tail -20\"", "aggregated_output": "3:duplicate memory side effects while\\nolder instructions drain during divider occupancy.\\n\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 50, \"confidence\": \"high\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/div_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a shared unsigned-magnitude radix-2 iterative divider with registered\\nrequest operands, signedness/result-selection metadata, 33-bit partial\\nremainder, quotient, divisor, and bounded iteration counter. Provide\\nrequest acceptance and a held result handshake; implement all RV32M\\nquotient/remainder sign rules, divide-by-zero, overflow, and reset.\\nKeep each arithmetic step bounded to one subtract/compare and mux.\\nUnder ALTOPS, produce the original operation-specific add/sub XOR\\nstand-ins through a short transaction using the same external control.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Remove real combinational DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU arithmetic from the ALU;\\nretain all base integer operations and all four multiplication results.\\nPreserve the exact RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS formulas, including division and\\nremainder, and use deterministic inactive outputs for real divider\\nopcodes because their results now come from the registered div_unit.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Instantiate div_unit and add EX issue/busy/result-transfer control.\\nCapture forwarded operands once on an accepted valid divide, retain\\nits original instruction and RVFI operand values, bubble EX/MEM while\\nwaiting, and publish the registered result exactly once when MEM can\\naccept it. Preserve single-cycle non-divide execution; ALTOPS divides\\nuse the same interlock with a shortened arithmetic transaction.\\nSuppress side effects from invalid bubbles and handle reset and dmem\\nbackpressure without reissuing or dropping an in-flight divide.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a distinct EX-busy interlock that holds PC and ID/EX for a divide\\nwithout holding older MEM/WB work. Preserve load-use and redirect\\nbehavior, with dmem backpressure taking precedence over divider issue\\nand EX/MEM\n…[37875 of 40947 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:e1df49e8c25bb702]…\nlization used by EX that excludes duplicate\\nADD/SUB/SLT/SLTU implementations, since their architectural results come\\nfrom registered carry preparation. Preserve all other operations, the\\nexact ALTOPS stand-ins and inactive real M outputs; ensure synthesis\\ncannot retain another full-width arithmetic path in the shared result.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_ex_stage.py\", \"description\": \"Update packed ID/EX layouts and operand stimulus to supply correctly\\nprepared p/g/s with each instruction. Retain all existing assertions.\\nCheck carry crossing every prefix boundary, overflow and signedness,\\nall branch conditions, JALR low-bit clearing/alignment traps and valid\\nbubbles, without substituting weaker arithmetic or trap expectations.\\nExercise every registered class across valid instructions, bubbles,\\nsquashes and arithmetic response holds; verify class and result ownership.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Update packed bundle layouts and check preparation register\n31:architectural operand\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
