{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_10", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n d=json.loads(line)\n print(d['id'], d['category'], d.get('outcome'), d.get('fitness'), d.get('fmax_mhz'), d.get('cycles'), '\\\\n ', d['title'])\n if d['category']=='micro_opt':\n  h=d.get('hypothesis',{})\n  if isinstance(h, dict): print(' ', h.get('hypothesis',''))\n  print(' PATH',d.get('critical_path'))\n  print(' NOTES',d.get('implementation_notes','')[:6000])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "baseline-bench-2e8305b micro_opt improvement 12.12 5.442 4491485 \n  Baseline retest for cores/bench\n  \n PATH {'from': 'cpu/u_mem/reg_q.rd_3_s0', 'to': 'dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s', 'slack_ns': -189.542, 'arrival_ns': 199.837, 'logic_cells': 156, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_fwd', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex']}\n NOTES \nhyp-20261002-001-r1s0 micro_opt regression 8.95 4.021 4491485 \n  Share a width-tapered combinational divider across RV32M operations\n  Replace only the real DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU datapath with one combinational\nunsigned restoring divider that produces quotient and remainder together.\nKeep the existing pipeline, forwarding and bus-handshake behavior, with\nno extra cycles for any instruction. For signed operations, convert both\noperands to unsigned 32-bit magnitudes before the divider, then negate the\nquotient when operand signs differ and negate the remainder only when the\ndividend is negative. Unsigned operations use the original operand bits.\n\nMake the 32 unrolled restoring stages explicitly width-tapered. At stage\nk=1..32, append dividend bit 32-k to the previous remainder to form a\nk-bit trial remainder. Subtract divisor[k-1:0] once using a k+1-bit\nzero-extended subtraction. Accept its low k bits and set quotient bit\n32-k only when the subtraction has no borrow and every divisor bit above\nk-1 is zero; otherwise retain the trial remainder and emit quotient zero.\nAt k=32 the upper-divisor predicate is constant true. Use the subtraction's\nborrow bit instead of a separate magnitude comparator, and use static\ngenerate widths so early stages contain only the necessary carry logic.\nThe final stage supplies both results; do not infer another '%' circuit.\n\nPreserve division-by-zero results explicitly (quotient 0xffffffff,\nremainder original dividend) and signed INT_MIN/-1 results (quotient\n0x80000000, remainder zero). Keep the RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS substitutions\nexactly as they are and exclude the real divider from that build. Keep\nmultiply and all RV32I datapaths unchanged. The expected gain comes fro\n…[41831 of 44903 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:1bc0a56abffd3a57]…\nps and side-effect suppression, reset and\nsquash priorities, memory acceptance, predictor training and consecutive\nRVFI order. Run unchanged formal, real arithmetic and stalled ISS cosim\ngates. Require canonical CoreMark CRCs, its validation literal, bounded\nmemory and original MMIO timing brackets. At the expected unchanged\n4,296,444 measured cycles, acceptance requires median Gowin Fmax above\nabout 98.133 MHz and fitness above 228.405 iter/sec. Measure all three\ncanonical placement options and actual cycles before claiming a gain.\n\n PATH {'from': 'cpu/u_id/reg_q.alu_a_0_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_id/reg_q.rs2_val_17_s0', 'slack_ns': -5.997, 'arrival_ns': 16.291, 'logic_cells': 25, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_id']}\n NOTES \nhyp-20261003-002-r11s1 structural regression 123.55 54.25 4390778 \n  Separate operand-candidate registers from bypass-source selection\nhyp-20261003-003-r11s2 predictor regression 210.39 90.089 4282066 \n  Resolve return bubbles with a small EX-trained return stack\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
