{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_13", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d['id'] in ['hyp-20261002-001-r6s0','hyp-20261003-002-r10s1','hyp-20261002-001-r8s0','hyp-20261002-003-r5s2']:\n  print(d['id'],d['title'])\n  print(d.get('hypothesis',{}).get('hypothesis',''))\n  print(d.get('implementation_notes',''))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261002-003-r5s2 Local prediction squash clears control while freeing payload registers\nLocalize prediction recovery in ID/EX: keep the exact BHT/JAL guesses,\ndirection-XOR EX correction, resolved targets and pipeline boundaries,\nbut remove flush and fetch-validity gating from the data payload flops.\nSplit the current whole-struct ID/EX assignment into payload update and\ncontrol/valid/prediction update logic, retaining a single owner for each register bit.\n\nOn reset clear every field exactly as today. Outside reset, update PC,\ninstruction, immediate, rs1/rs2 values and addresses, alu_a/alu_b, rd and direct_target whenever !stall, using their existing\ncombinational sources. These data fields must not depend on flush or\nin.valid and may contain a wrong-path or unavailable fetch in a bubble.\nWhen stall is asserted, hold these payload fields even if flush requests\nan injected bubble. Independently, flush has priority over stall and\nclears the entire ctrl_t plus valid and predicted_taken. Also clear ctrl_t, valid and predicted_taken when\n!stall && !in.valid. Otherwise an unstalled valid input captures the\nexisting decoded control bundle and predicted_taken, and sets valid; a\nstall without flush holds control, valid and predicted_taken. This is precisely the existing architectural\nhold/bubble/advance behavior with a smaller recovery-driven register set.\n\nClearing valid alone is explicitly insufficient. Clear every ctrl_t bit,\nincluding reg_write, mem_read, mem_write, mem_to_reg, is_branch, is_jump,\nis_jalr, alu_op and is_illegal, exactly as the existing all-zero bubble.\nThe invalid instruction may retain data but must never launch arithmetic,\nforward, redirect, train the BHT, access dmem or retire. Retain EX's !valid\nwhole-EX/MEM bubble insertion and all existing validity/completion gates.\nDo not modify memory, forwarding, arithmetic, hazards or decoder legality.\nA bubble must clear predicted_taken as part of prediction control, keeping\ninactive speculation out of the next EX correction cone; ex_advance still\nrequ\n…[14724 of 17796 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:35ddcc145ae62c85]…\ntic, access memory or retire. Preserve\nfull reset, payload/control squash split, decoder default-illegal\nvalidation, EBREAK-only SYSTEM legality, aligned memory masks, every\nexisting trap and monotonically consecutive channel-zero RVFI orders.\nMaintain nret=1 and all top-level ports and benchmark/evaluator contracts.\n\nPredict eight percent fitness improvement with low confidence, from\nshorter ordinary arithmetic/branch feedback at unchanged CoreMark\ncycles. This is a prediction, not an accepted measured result. At\n4,296,444 cycles, acceptance requires median Gowin Fmax above 98.133 MHz\nand fitness above 228.405 iterations/sec. Register and prefix routing\ncosts, shifter/result-selection delay, multiplier control and the extra\nbitwise preparation after forwarding can erase the gain. Require actual\nmedian vendor timing and marker-bounded cycles; area or a shorter logic\npath alone is insufficient. Run unchanged formal, real arithmetic,\nRVFI cosimulation and canonical stalled CoreMark CRC/UART/OOB/marker gates.\n\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
