/reg_q.alu_a_26_s0\n          through: clock_ibuf > cpu/u_ex > cpu/u_id\n  full report: /srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6_1-sol_xhigh-v2-rep6/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20261003-001-r13s0-hypgen/cores/bench/generated/timing/gowin_p1/impl/pnr/core_bench.tr\nplace_option 2: Fmax 89.12 MHz, 13 logic levels; logic 3728, registers 1103, LUT-RAM 40, BSRAM 4, DSP 2\n  path 1: 16.515 ns, 38 cells, cpu/u_id/reg_q.rs2_val_0_s0 -> cpu/u_id/reg_q.alu_a_18_s0\n          through: clock_ibuf > cpu/u_ex > cpu/u_id\n  path 2: 16.514 ns, 38 cells, cpu/u_id/reg_q.rs2_val_0_s0 -> cpu/u_id/reg_q.alu_b_21_s0\n          through: clock_ibuf > cpu/u_ex > cpu/u_id\n  path 3: 16.51 ns, 23 cells, cpu/u_id/reg_q.alu_b_10_s0 -> cpu/u_id/reg_q.alu_a_24_s0\n          through: clock_ibuf > cpu/u_ex/u_alu > cpu/u_ex > cpu/u_id\n  path 4: 16.507 ns, 38 cells, cpu/u_id/reg_q.rs2_val_0_s0 -> cpu/u_id/reg_q.alu_b_28_s0\n          through: clock_ibuf > cpu/u_ex > cpu/u_id\n  path 5: 16.505 ns, 38 cells, cpu/u_id/reg_q.rs2_val_0_s0 -> cpu/u_id/reg_q.alu_a_26_s0\n          through: clock_ibuf > cpu/u_ex > cpu/u_id\n  full report: /srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6_1-sol_xhigh-v2-rep6/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20261003-001-r13s0-hypgen/cores/bench/generated/timing/gowin_p2/impl/pnr/core_bench.tr\nscore Fmax (median): 89.12 MHz\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_51", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-001-r13s0.yaml')\nd=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\nd['title']='Register ALU result and M-family predecode at ID/EX'\nd['motivation']='''The champion scores 218.36 iter/sec at 93.817 MHz with 4,296,444\nmarker-bounded CoreMark cycles. Its ALU/EX-to-ID feedback path remains\ncritical. A local eleven-bit RV32I result-predecode prototype passed\nexisting pipeline/ID and real/ALTOPS EX tests and reduced LUTs from\n3,675 to 3,630, but median Gowin Fmax fell to 89.754 MHz. Its worst\nmedian-placement path begins at registered alu_op through M-family\nrecognition, EX forwarding eligibility and younger ID operands. Finish\nthe same control-predecode transformation by registering both M-family\nbits rather than leaving those binary classifications in EX. Earlier\nM tag recoding, broad operand crossbars and full result registering\nfailed; preserve current operation tags, data routing and latency.\n'''\nd['hypothesis']='''Move ALU operation predecode to the existing ID/EX edge. Register one\nthirteen-bit instruction-owned control field: bits 0..10 select ADD,\nSUB, AND, OR, XOR, SLT, SLTU, SLL, SRL, SRA and LUI, respectively;\nbit 11 identifies MUL/MULH/MULHU/MULHSU and bit 12 identifies\nDIV/DIVU/REM/REMU. Each validated operation activates exactly one bit.\nKeep the five-bit alu_op and all existing ctrl_t fields and encodings.\nThis is one local operation-control predecode optimization, with no\nnew stage, execution bubble, dependency interlock or prediction change.\n\nDerive the field in ID from the unchanged decoder's dec_alu_op, using\nexplicit exact matches. Match all four existing tags for each M family;\nnever infer a family from a coarse bit that also accepts undefined tags.\nAdd alu_result_sel[12:0] to id_ex_t only. Capture it on the same accepted\nvalid edge as ctrl_decoded. Reset, flush or unstalled invalid fetch must\nclear the entire field; an ordinary hold retains it. Apply precisely\nthe existing control reset/flush/hold priorities, including flush over\nhold and older dmem/M ownership precedence. Illegal decoder defaults\nretain their existing behavior and never gain side effects. Prove the\nfield agrees with the owning instruction's binary operation whenever\nID/EX is valid, and remains one-hot-or-zero across reset and squash.\n\nIn EX drive is_multiply and is_divide directly from registered bits 11\nand 12. All original valid/reset/stall, legal-write, accepted launch,\nsaved-payload-valid, held-result and trap checks remain in force.\nReplace only the ordinary ALU result-selection decode with bits 0..10:\ncompute the same eleven RV32I candidates with the current arithmetic,\ncomparison, shift and LUI expressions and widths; mask each candidate\nby its registered select and use a balanced OR reduction. Do not put\nanother binary-opcode RV32I result mux after it. Preserve standalone\nalu ports and binary behavior for its existing unit suite, using a\nlocal predecoded implementation or constant-specialized wrapper in\nalu.sv. EX must synthesize without the legacy RV32I result decoder or\nthe four-way multiply/divide classifiers.\n\nKeep alu_op for requests to the unchanged multiplier and divider and\nfor every exact RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS stand-in. A real M operation has all\nRV32I result-select bits zero and still obtains its result exclusively\nthrough the existing registered response. The ALTOPS implementation\nmust retain all eight exact formulas and operand routing, including\ncorner-case operands. Keep all arithmetic datapaths, M latency,\nlaunch-once metadata, response acceptance, EX/MEM and MEM/WB ownership,\nshared bypass data/destination buses and forwarding priority intact.\nDo not add carry preparation, a comparator tree, shifter sharing,\nextra result crossbar candidates, tag recoding or memory formatting.\n\nPreserve same-cycle branch correction/training, targets/link writes,\nbranch/jump and memory alignment traps, x0, accepted load forwarding,\nfull control/valid squash, resolved payload holds, memory handshake,\nnret=1 ports, architectural RVFI fields and consecutive retirement\norder. Inactive bundles cannot forward, launch, redirect, access memory\nor retire. Only permitted bench RTL and unit tests may change.\n\nThe earlier eleven-bit prototype is a measured regression, not evidence\nof an improvement. The final thirteen-bit version addresses its exposed\nM classification path; its gain must be established independently.\nPredict eight percent greater fitness with low confidence. Additional\nselect registers/fanout and unchanged carry, branch and accepted-load\npaths can erase the benefit. Expected canonical CoreMark cycles remain\nexactly 4,296,444. Acceptance requires actual fitness above 228.40456\niter/sec, approximately 98.133 MHz median Fmax at that cycle count.\nRun all three scored Gowin options and actual marker-bounded CoreMark;\na shorter source expression or lower LUT count is insufficient.\n\nValidate symbolic selection equivalence and operation-control ownership,\nall real/ALTOPS unit tests, unchanged formal and stalled ISS cosimulation,\nand canonical CoreMark CRCs, validation literal, bounded memory and\noriginal MMIO timing brackets. Directed checks must cover every defined\noperation and unused tag, shifts, carry/sign extremes, rapid ordinary/M\ntransitions, M response holds, independent bus stalls, load forwarding,\nx0, flush-over-hold, reset and wrong-path stores/M instructions.\n'''\nd['changes'][0]['description']='''Add the thirteen-bit registered operation-predecode field to id_ex_t\nonly: eleven RV32I result bits and one bit for each M family. Preserve\nctrl_t, all operation tags, original operands, downstream bundles,\ntop-level IO and nret.\n'''\nd['changes'][1]['description']='''Decode exact RV32I operations and MUL/DIV families from dec_alu_op.\nCapture the one-hot-or-zero field on valid admission with the existing\ncontrol reset, flush, invalid-fetch and hold priorities. Preserve all\noperand muxes, final ALU inputs, decoder legality and architectural data.\n'''\nd['changes'][3]['description']='''Use registered bits 11/12 for is_multiply/is_divide and bits 0..10\nfor ordinary ALU result selection. Keep binary alu_op for unchanged\nM requests and ALTOPS. Preserve every launch/transfer/trap/producer\nqualification, shared bypass bus, link result, recovery/training event,\nmetadata record and sequential ownership rule.\n'''\nd['changes'][5]['description']='''Update packed ID/EX layout and assert all thirteen predecode bits\nagainst every operation tag. Check one-hot-or-zero, reset, flush over\nhold, invalid admission and stable ownership during stalls. Preserve\nevery existing operand and control assertion.\n'''\nd['changes'][6]['description']='''Update packed stimulus with the exact thirteen-bit field. Keep every\narithmetic launch, held response, metadata, destination and bypass\nassertion. Cover ordinary/M family transitions, undefined tags,\ninvalid/illegal instructions and reset cancellation in real and ALTOPS.\n'''\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=78))\njsonschema.validate(d,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Updated thirteen-bit hypothesis; schema valid')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
