/reg_q.alu_a_14_s0 -> cpu/u_id/reg_q.alu_b_27_s0\n          through: clock_ibuf > cpu/u_ex/u_alu > cpu/u_ex > cpu/u_id\n  full report: /srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6_1-sol_xhigh-v2-rep6/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20261003-001-r13s0-hypgen/cores/bench/generated/timing/gowin_p1/impl/pnr/core_bench.tr\nplace_option 2: Fmax 88.182 MHz, 11 logic levels; logic 3642, registers 1090, LUT-RAM 40, BSRAM 4, DSP 2\n  path 1: 16.635 ns, 11 cells, cpu/u_id/reg_q.alu_a_8_s0 -> dmem_1_dmem_1_0_0_s\n          through: clock_ibuf > cpu/u_ex/u_alu > cpu/u_id > cpu/u_ex\n  path 2: 16.627 ns, 11 cells, cpu/u_id/reg_q.alu_a_4_s0 -> dmem_3_dmem_3_0_0_s\n          through: clock_ibuf > cpu/u_ex/u_alu > cpu/u_ex\n  path 3: 16.624 ns, 9 cells, cpu/u_id/reg_q.rs1_val_10_s0 -> cpu/u_if/counters_counters_RAMREG_0_G[109]_s0\n          through: clock_ibuf > cpu/u_ex > cpu/u_if\n  path 4: 16.624 ns, 9 cells, cpu/u_id/reg_q.rs1_val_10_s0 -> cpu/u_if/counters_counters_RAMREG_0_G[108]_s0\n          through: clock_ibuf > cpu/u_ex > cpu/u_if\n  path 5: 16.618 ns, 11 cells, cpu/u_id/reg_q.alu_a_14_s0 -> cpu/u_id/reg_q.alu_b_27_s0\n          through: clock_ibuf > cpu/u_ex/u_alu > cpu/u_ex > cpu/u_id\n  full report: /srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6_1-sol_xhigh-v2-rep6/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20261003-001-r13s0-hypgen/cores/bench/generated/timing/gowin_p2/impl/pnr/core_bench.tr\nscore Fmax (median): 88.182 MHz\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_56", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-001-r13s0.yaml')\nd={\n'id':'hyp-20261003-001-r13s0',\n'title':'Shorten branch recovery with a dedicated LUT4 comparison tree',\n'category':'micro_opt',\n'motivation':'''The champion scores 218.36 iter/sec at median 93.817 MHz and\n4,296,444 marker-bounded CoreMark cycles. Its ordinary ALU feedback\ncompetes with recurring 37-38-cell paths from registered branch operands\nthrough comparison, redirect or predictor training into IF/ID controls.\nThe round-4 dedicated branch tree improved Fmax 14 percent relative to\nits then-current parent, but lost to that round's registered multiplier\nand was not retained. The current champion has registered multiply\nresponses, making a dedicated branch-only comparator worth reevaluating.\nLocal result-predecode and shared ALU/branch-comparator probes failed;\nexclude their changes and preserve the current data/control boundaries.\n''',\n'hypothesis':'''Replace only EX's conditional-branch comparison network with a\nbalanced equality/unsigned-less tree suited to the FPGA's four-input\nLUTs. Keep ALU SLT/SLTU, add/subtract, shifts, result selection,\noperand registers, multiplier/divider and every pipeline boundary\nunchanged. Do not share this tree with the ALU or add operation-class\nregisters. This is one local Boolean branch-comparator optimization,\nwith identical branch outcomes, training events and instruction latency.\n\nUse sixteen independent two-bit slices of the existing registered\narchitectural rs1 and rs2. For slice i, form equality and unsigned\nless-than from rs1[2*i +: 2] and rs2[2*i +: 2]. Each leaf depends on\nonly four data inputs. Combine adjacent higher/lower groups with\n  eq = eq_high & eq_low;\n  lt = lt_high | (eq_high & lt_low).\nUse four balanced merge levels instead of a full-width ripple comparator\nor subtractor. A concrete implementation uses packed 31-bit eq/lt\nvectors: leaves occupy 15+i; internal node n combines higher child\n2*n+2 and lower child 2*n+1; node zero is the whole-word root. Compute\nleaves first and internal nodes from n=14 down to zero in one complete\nalways_comb block, or use separately sized level vectors. Avoid an\nunpacked feedback interpretation or an unbounded priority loop.\n\nRoot equality supplies BEQ and complemented BNE. Root unsigned less\nsupplies BLTU and complemented BGEU. Signed less is\n(rs1[31] \"'^ rs2[31]) ? rs1[31] : unsigned_less; use it for BLT and\ncomplemented BGE. Keep false for branch funct3 2/3 and retain the\nvalidated decoder'\"'s default-illegal behavior. Branch_taken must still\nbe qualified by is_branch; unsupported or invalid instructions cannot\nredirect or train. Do not put a 32-bit relational operator or full\nsubtractor back into this branch cone. Preserve the independent ALU\ncomparisons exactly as they are, including ALTOPS routing.\n\nKeep alignment traps and redirect suppression, actual architectural\nnext-PC, direction-XOR correction and sequential correction targets,\nsame-cycle correction priority, once-per-accepted branch training,\noriginal BHT policy, dmem hold precedence, arithmetic busy ownership,\nload-use bubble, payload holds and complete control/valid squash.\nRetain all launch-once and held-result M behavior, shared forwarding\neligibility/data/destinations, memory requests, x0, nret=1 core IO,\nRVFI metadata and consecutive retirement order. Modify only permitted\nbench RTL and unit tests.\n\nPredict six percent higher fitness with low confidence. Removing the\nserial branch comparison chain can shorten several control consumers,\nbut unchanged ALU and accepted-load paths can still set Fmax and the\ntree can increase routing pressure. Historical gains on the earlier\nparent do not establish a gain on this champion. Require unchanged\n4,296,444 canonical CoreMark cycles, exact branch/prediction traces and\nactual median Gowin Fmax above about 98.133 MHz, giving fitness above\n228.40456 iter/sec to clear the 4.6 percent acceptance margin. Evaluate\nall three scored placement options, not only the best placement.\n\nProve the six branch predicates and default-false cases equivalent to\nthe original comparisons for every 32-bit operand pair and funct3.\nRetain all existing assertions and add directed equal values, opposite\nsigns, sign boundaries, each possible highest differing bit, all six\nconditions and reserved functions. Exercise misaligned taken versus\nuntaken targets, independent instruction/data stalls, held branches,\ncorrection coinciding with unavailable fetch and wrong-path stores/M\ninstructions. Check accepted training occurs once, exact RVFI source\nvalues and next PCs, trap/write suppression and consecutive orders.\nRun unchanged formal and stalled ISS cosimulation, real/ALTOPS arithmetic\nchecks, canonical CoreMark CRCs, validation literal, bounded memory and\noriginal start/stop MMIO brackets before accepting a measured gain.\n''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':6,'confidence':'low'},\n'changes':[\n{'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'''Implement the dedicated two-bit-leaf balanced equality/unsigned-less\nbranch tree, derive signed ordering from operand signs and choose the\nsix branch predicates from shared roots. Preserve default false,\nall ALU/M datapaths, trap/redirect/training qualification, forwarding,\nmetadata and sequential ownership. Add no state or pipeline stage.\n'''},\n{'file':'test/test_ex_stage.py','description':'''Retain every existing arithmetic acceptance, saved-metadata, response\nhold and bypass assertion. Add direct checks of all branch predicates,\nreserved branch functions, equality/sign/differing-bit boundaries,\naligned and misaligned targets, valid/illegal controls and dmem holds.\nProve local comparator equivalence without replacing formal gates.\n'''},\n{'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Retain every existing exact RVFI, operand-capture, memory-effect,\ntrap, retirement-order and progression assertion. Add all six branch\nconditions with differing-bit/sign cases, held and corrected branches,\nindependent bus stalls, wrong-path stores/M operations and once-only\ntraining. Verify unchanged branch correction/dependency latency and\ncanonical marker-bounded CoreMark cycles.\n'''}]}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=78))\njsonschema.validate(d,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Final-angle hypothesis written; schema valid')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
