usive\nprefix pairs (G,P) in three static parallel levels at distances 1, 2\nand 4. A higher group H composed with a lower group L has\n  G = G_H | (P_H & G_L);\n  P = P_H & P_L.\nAt each level, nodes whose index is below the distance pass through;\nother nodes combine with the corresponding node from the PREVIOUS\nlevel. Never read a partially updated level or create a recursive\nfull-width priority chain. After the final level, carry into group zero\nis zero and carry into group j>0 is prefix_G[j-1].\n\nCompute each four-bit output slice as the low four bits of an explicitly\nsized local a_j+b_j+carry_j addition. This leaves only short native\ncarry chains within groups and a three-level inter-group prefix instead\nof a 32-bit serial carry recurrence. Express all group boundaries and\nprefix distances with static generate indices or fixed-width vectors,\nusing portable combinational SV accepted by Gowin, Verilator and Yosys.\nKeep the implementation local to alu.sv, avoiding source-list edits.\nDo not implement two speculative whole-word carry-select sums, a dense\n32-node bit prefix, or an operand-dependent early-exit path. Do not force\nLUT boundaries with syn_keep attributes. Confirm synthesis retains the\nintended bounded group structure rather than reconstructing a long\nword-wide adder or introducing latches.\n\nRoute only ALU_ADD through this result. Preserve SUB, signed/unsigned\nSLT, all bitwise and shift expressions, LUI, the ALU port contract and\ndefault-zero behavior exactly. Preserve every RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS\noperation-specific formula unchanged and keep the real registered\nM datapaths and their inactive ALU outputs unchanged. Do not alter the\nseparate PC increment, JALR target adder, branch comparator, predictor,\nMEM extraction, result/operand muxes or forwarding qualification.\n\nThe new result must equal (a+b) modulo 2\"'^32 for EVERY operand pair,\nincluding overflow; no dependence on opcode history, memory layout or\nbenchmark data is permitted. Loads, stores, ADD/ADDI and AUIPC retain\ntheir existing effective-address/result semantics. Preserve nret=1\nand exact core IO, decoder default-illegal validation, EBREAK-only\nSYSTEM legality, all alignment traps and side-effect suppression,\nM launch-once/held-response ownership, reset/flush/hold priorities,\nmemory handshakes, branch recovery/training and strict RVFI order.\n\nPredict eight percent higher fitness with low confidence. This final\nadder is unmeasured. Its extra P/G logic and local sum routing can erase\nthe carry-depth gain, and unchanged branch, shifter or accepted-load\npaths can remain limiting. Failed local predecode/comparator prototypes\nare negative evidence, not a claimed improvement for this different\ncircuit. Expected canonical CoreMark cycles remain exactly 4,296,444;\nacceptance requires actual fitness above 228.40456 iter/sec, about\n98.133 MHz median Gowin Fmax at that cycle count. Measure all three\nscored vendor placement options and actual marker-bounded cycles.\n\nProve combinational equivalence to the original addition for symbolic\n32-bit a and b. Keep all existing unit assertions and add carry chains\ncrossing each four-bit boundary, generate/propagate/kill combinations,\nall-ones wraparound, alternating-bit patterns, sign extremes and random\npairs. Exercise dependent ADD/ADDI/AUIPC and memory-address consumers\nwith operands from EX, accepted MEM loads and write-first WB/RF under\nindependent bus stalls. Run unchanged formal, real/ALTOPS arithmetic\nand stalled ISS cosimulation gates; require canonical CoreMark CRCs,\nvalidation literal, bounded memory and original start/stop MMIO brackets.\n'\"''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':8,'confidence':'low'},\n'changes':[\n{'file':'rtl/alu.sv','description':'''Implement ALU_ADD using eight four-bit P/G groups, three inclusive\nprefix levels at distances 1/2/4 and short local sum slices driven by\nthe resolved group carries. Use explicit intermediate widths and\nstatic dependencies. Preserve all other operations, exact ALTOPS\nformulas, default-zero behavior and existing module ports.\n'''},\n{'file':'test/test_alu.py','description':'''Retain every existing real/ALTOPS assertion. Add exact ADD vectors\ncovering every group boundary, long propagate chains, carry kill and\ngenerate cases, overflow, alternating bits and random pairs. Prove\nsymbolic equality to the original modulo-32-bit addition; this local\nproof supplements rather than replaces the unchanged formal gates.\n'''},\n{'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Retain every existing exact RVFI, trap, memory-effect, operand-hold\nand order assertion. Add dependent ADD/ADDI/AUIPC, carry-boundary\nloads/stores and forwarded address operands under independent bus\nstalls. Verify unchanged instruction/dependency latency, accepted\nmemory effects and canonical marker-bounded CoreMark cycles.\n'''}]}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=78))\njsonschema.validate(d,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nassert d['id']=='hyp-20261003-001-r13s0' and d['category']=='micro_opt'\nassert type(d['expected_impact']['fitness_delta_pct']) is int\nprint('Final hypothesis schema validation: PASS')\nroot=Path('cores/bench'); bak=root/'generated/r13-backup'\nfor f in bak.rglob('*'):\n if f.is_file(): (root/f.relative_to(bak)).write_bytes(f.read_bytes())\nprint('Restored all exploratory RTL and test changes')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "Final hypothesis schema validation: PASS\nRestored all exploratory RTL and test changes\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
