{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_20", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n d=json.loads(line)\n h=d.get('hypothesis')\n h=h.get('hypothesis','') if isinstance(h,dict) else str(h)\n if any(s in h.lower() for s in ['carry-select','one-hot alu','onehot','result selection','shifter']):\n  print(d['id'],d.get('title'))\n  for paragraph in h.split('\\\\n\\\\n'):\n   if any(s in paragraph.lower() for s in ['carry-select','one-hot alu','onehot','shifter']): print(paragraph)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261002-002-r5s1 Complete pipelined multiplies in MEM instead of blocking EX\nhyp-20261002-001-r6s0 Factor AND OR XOR into one four-input-LUT ALU result family\nhyp-20261002-001-r7s0 Align M operation codes to shorten EX class selection\nKeep decoder opcode/funct validation and default-illegal behavior unchanged; its existing symbolic ALU constants now produce the new tags. Keep every other consumer symbolic, including ordinary ALU dispatch, exact ALTOPS formulas, multiplier signedness/high-half selection and divider operation selection. The natural low bits also expose DIV/REM signedness and remainder selection to synthesis through the existing constant comparisons, without changing their arithmetic or request/response protocols. Do not introduce new class registers, alter instruction encodings, widen ctrl_t, change pipeline boundaries, or combine this with result-crossbar, shifter, comparator or prediction changes.\nhyp-20261002-001-r8s0 Match forwarding destinations in parallel using one held M tag\nExpect eight percent higher fitness from Fmax, with low confidence\nbecause branch recovery and accepted-load forwarding remain competing\npaths. An initial prototype comparing all three destinations separately\nreached only 90.203 MHz and increased LUTs to 3,881. It is not an accepted\nresult. The proposed refinement instead uses the single held M tag to\nremove duplicate M comparisons and timed saved-destination selection;\nthis refinement remains unmeasured and requires full evaluation.\nRequire unchanged 4,296,444 canonical measured cycles; acceptance\nneeds more than 228.40456 iter/sec, or approximately 98.133 MHz median\nFmax at that cycle count. Measure all three canonical Gowin placement\noptions and inspect the destination-match path. Local comparator,\nshifter, metadata-sharing and wider one-hot selection probes did not\nestablish a gain on this champion; do not include those changes.\nhyp-20261003-002-r10s1 Retiming carry preparation and execution classes across ID/EX\nThe structural benefit is moving initial bit carr\n…[3272 of 6344 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:1d8bf8a15ed8d6e8]…\nnd Yosys.\nKeep the implementation local to alu.sv, avoiding source-list edits.\nDo not implement two speculative whole-word carry-select sums, a dense\n32-node bit prefix, or an operand-dependent early-exit path. Do not force\nLUT boundaries with syn_keep attributes. Confirm synthesis retains the\nintended bounded group structure rather than reconstructing a long\nword-wide adder or introducing latches.\nPredict eight percent higher fitness with low confidence. This final\nadder is unmeasured. Its extra P/G logic and local sum routing can erase\nthe carry-depth gain, and unchanged branch, shifter or accepted-load\npaths can remain limiting. Failed local predecode/comparator prototypes\nare negative evidence, not a claimed improvement for this different\ncircuit. Expected canonical CoreMark cycles remain exactly 4,296,444;\nacceptance requires actual fitness above 228.40456 iter/sec, about\n98.133 MHz median Gowin Fmax at that cycle count. Measure all three\nscored vendor placement options and actual marker-bounded cycles.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
