 their timing cost from ordinary instructions, letting Fmax gains outweigh CoreMark's added divide stalls.\n- 2026-10-02 hyp-20261002-002-r2s1 (regression, +7.45%): Registering elastic IF/ID removes redirect-to-decode feedback, but the added taken-branch refill cycle raised CoreMark cycles 6.45%, limiting a 14.39% Fmax gain to 7.45% fitness.\n- 2026-10-02 hyp-20261002-003-r2s2 (improvement, +13.63%): Instruction-qualified BHT/JAL prediction removes recurring CoreMark control bubbles, while saved direct targets enable direction-XOR \n…[474995 of 478067 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:932d5d580cb91b24]…\n.29, \"delta_pct\": -16.06, \"vs_baseline\": 1412.29, \"fmax_mhz\": 79.787, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4353135, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 3074, \"ff\": 834, \"seeds\": [81.089, 79.787, 79.787], \"perturbations\": [[0, 81.089, 10], [1, 79.787, 11], [2, 79.787, 11]], \"lutram\": 40, \"bsram\": 4, \"dsp\": 2, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_id/reg_q.ctrl.alu_op_4_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_id/reg_q.rs1_val_20_s0\", \"slack_ns\": -7.332, \"arrival_ns\": 17.626, \"logic_cells\": 10, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_mul\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_fwd\", \"cpu/u_id\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 10, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-03T02:16:47.056959Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 14, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-10-03 hyp-20261003-003-r14s2 (regression, -16.06%): Deleting the 128-entry BHT for static backward-taken prediction saves 256 FFs but leaves `alu_op`-to-MUL/forwarding-to-ID operand feedback critical, so median Fmax fell from 93.817 to 79.787 MHz while CoreMark cycles rose only 1.32%.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
