ed divide. Completed arithmetic responses use the saved\nlaunch destination and metadata. A load has no EX value. A busy,\ninvalid, trapped or stalled instruction is never an eligible producer.\nMEM is eligible only for its actual accepted architectural result,\nincluding the existing sign/zero-extended load extraction; EX wins\nover MEM and MEM wins over the existing write-first register-file read.\n\nUse these early selects directly in balanced mask-and-OR datapaths,\nrather than encoding a selection and rebuilding nested priority muxes.\nForm rs1_val and rs2_val from the independent candidates for branches,\nJALR, \n…[14034 of 17106 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:b15348528bd16afc]…\nl dependency and redundant completion gates\nthat the preliminary probe retained. Those preliminary checks do not\nestablish a fitness gain or replace validation of this final circuit.\nPredict eight percent higher fitness with low confidence; ordinary ALU\nand accepted-load forwarding remain competing timing limits.\n\nPreserve nret=1 and all core ports, default-illegal validated decoding,\nEBREAK-only SYSTEM legality, exact real RV32M and ALTOPS arithmetic,\narchitectural operands, traps and side-effect suppression, reset and\nsquash priorities, memory acceptance, predictor training and consecutive\nRVFI order. Run unchanged formal, real arithmetic and stalled ISS cosim\ngates. Require canonical CoreMark CRCs, its validation literal, bounded\nmemory and original MMIO timing brackets. At the expected unchanged\n4,296,444 measured cycles, acceptance requires median Gowin Fmax above\nabout 98.133 MHz and fitness above 228.405 iter/sec. Measure all three\ncanonical placement options and actual cycles before claiming a gain.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
