{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_38", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-002-r10s1.yaml')\nh=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\nh['title']='Retiming carry preparation and execution classes across ID/EX'\ns=h['hypothesis']\ns=s.replace('EX consumes only these registered p/g/s values to produce the arithmetic\\\\nsum, carry-out and comparison results. Use an explicit balanced prefix\\\\ncarry network over registered p/g, with bounded fanout and a topology\\\\nchosen for LUT4s; do not reintroduce a serial 32-bit ripple recurrence.', '''Register execution classes on the same boundary as preparation. Derive\nis_multiply, is_divide, use_prepared_arithmetic, arithmetic_compare and\nsigned_compare from validated decoder outputs in ID. Carry these with\nctrl_t, clear them on every squash/bubble and hold them with the owning\ninstruction. Use registered multiply/divide classes for busy, launch,\nresponse and bypass routing, and the prepared/compare classes for result\nselection. Do not repeatedly decode five-bit alu_op in the EX-to-ID\nfeedback path. Retain exact alu_op for the M unit request and nonarithmetic\nALU. This is necessary control retiming for the new arithmetic boundary;\nr7s1's class retiming alone regressed and is not evidence of a gain here.\n\nEX consumes registered p/g/s to produce sum, carry-out and comparisons.\nUse a sparse balanced carry structure: eight four-bit groups with local\ngroup generate/propagate, a balanced group prefix and bounded local carry\nreconstruction. Avoid a dense all-bit prefix with long global wiring and\navoid a serial 32-bit ripple recurrence. Use registered class bits for\nthe final arithmetic-versus-other and comparison-versus-sum muxes.''')\ns=s.replace('This final bitwise\\\\npreparation differs from it and must be evaluated on its own merits.\\\\nUse a hierarchical or sparse balanced prefix if a dense prefix creates\\\\nexcessive routing; this is a mapping choice within the single retimed\\\\narithmetic structure, not another architectural hypothesis.', '''A second prototype registered bitwise p/g and used a dense five-level\nprefix, but retained repeated alu_op class decoding. It passed stalled\nRVFI comparison for selftest and all three random programs (115, 11,037,\n11,094 and 12,059 retirements), and canonical CoreMark CRC/UART/OOB/marker\nchecks at exactly 4,296,444 cycles. Placement option zero reached only\n74.857 MHz, with 3,824 logic cells and 1,123 registers. Its worst path was\n18.653 ns through 13 cells from ID/EX alu_op to a preparation register,\nvia EX result selection and forwarding. It is a measured regression.\nThe final proposal explicitly differs by registering execution classes\nand using the sparse group carry structure; neither its timing nor its\nfitness has been measured. Do not reproduce either failed prototype or\nclaim their correctness checks establish the final implementation.''')\nh['hypothesis']=s\nh['changes'][0]['description']+='Add the five validated execution-class bits to ctrl_t, keeping full\\\\ncontrol reset/clear and instruction ownership. Preserve decoder-facing\\\\noperation encodings and all downstream architectural metadata.\\\\n'\nh['changes'][1]['description']+='Register validated M/prepared/compare classes in ctrl_decoded and clear\\\\nthem with all other controls on squash or unavailable-fetch bubbles.\\\\n'\nh['changes'][2]['description']=h['changes'][2]['description'].replace('prefix structure','sparse eight-group prefix structure')+'Use registered execution classes throughout EX busy, M launch/transfer,\\\\nbypass and prepared-result selection instead of repeated alu_op matching.\\\\nKeep alu_op for exact arithmetic requests. Do not retain the failed dense\\\\nprefix prototype or its five-bit opcode-to-preparation feedback cone.\\\\n'\nh['changes'][4]['description']+='Exercise every registered class across valid instructions, bubbles,\\\\nsquashes and arithmetic response holds; verify class and result ownership.\\\\n'\nh['changes'][5]['description']+='Update ctrl_t widths as well as the new arithmetic payload layout and\\\\ncheck execution classes clear on bubbles and hold across backpressure.\\\\n'\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(h,sort_keys=False,width=90))\njsonschema.validate(h,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nassert h['id']=='hyp-20261003-002-r10s1' and h['category']=='structural'\nassert type(h['expected_impact']['fitness_delta_pct']) is int\nassert -50<=h['expected_impact']['fitness_delta_pct']<=50\nprint('Final hypothesis schema-valid:',p)\nprint('Only target-relative allowed change paths:',*[c['file'] for c in h['changes']],sep='\\\\n')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
