"title\": \"Instruction-qualified direction prediction with short recovery control\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The divider champion scores 101.21 at 45.46 MHz, with a 27.6 ns worst\\npath crossing ID, EX, IF, the hazard unit, and ID again. Fetch currently\\nchooses pc+4 for every instruction. Every taken branch or jump discards\\none younger instruction, and EX redirect also masks the entire fetched\\\n…[10297 of 13369 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:0203ab888bd0aca9]…\nRegister memory lane formatting at the existing EX/MEM boundary\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"Accepted-load forwarding from MEM into ID remains a competing timing\\nlimit: r8s0 and r10s1 reported critical u_mem-to-u_id paths. Currently\\nMEM decodes access width and effective-address alignment before granting\\nbypass eligibility, and also formats the timed memory write outputs.\\nEarlier wider operand crossbars and ID arithmetic preparation reg [... omitted end of long line]\n36:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261003-002-r12s1\", \"title\": \"Register execution results before operand forwarding\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The champion reaches 218.36 iter/sec at 93.817 MHz and 4,296,444\\nmarker-bounded CoreMark cycles. Successful structural changes isolated\\ndivision, registered resolved operands, and registered multiplication.\\nThe remaining recurring path crosses EX arithmetic and acceptance\\nqualification into the next ID operand registers. r6s1 widened the\\nunregistered cro [... omitted end of long line]\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
