rather than freezing an already completed memory request or\nreplaying an older retirement. Clear reg_write, mem_read, mem_write, and\nredirect controls in these bubbles as well as valid, because the current\nmemory and forwarding logic consumes control bits without validity gates.\nAn older dmem stall still holds EX/MEM and\ntakes precedence over divider issue and result transfer. Latch forwarded\noperands at accepted launch so draining WB cannot change an active divide.\nRetain an unconsumed registered result until EX/MEM can accept it, transfer\nit exactly once with the original instruction's RVFI metadata, then resume\nthe pipeline. Preserve the existing EX/MEM and MEM/WB forwarding priority;\n\n…[25139 of 28211 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:be091f1c7d81205c]…\n is unavailable in both EX and the\nnew result stage and becomes available only on accepted MEM completion,\nso its immediately dependent consumer gains two interlock cycles total.\nMatch both raw encoded source fields to preserve the existing exact\nRVFI operand convention, including fields unused by execution. Never\nlet an older MEM/RF value override a younger unavailable writer.\n\nRegister branch condition, resolved next-PC, final alignment/trap\ncontrols, prediction correction and training metadata with the result\ntransaction. Apply a correction exactly once from the new stage on\ntransfer, when older MEM is not stalled. Kill the younger current EX\ninstruction and ID admission, including \n  path: {'from': 'dmem_3_dmem_3_0_0_s', 'to': 'cpu/u_id/reg_q.rs2_val_16_s0', 'slack_ns': -5.209, 'arrival_ns': 15.504, 'logic_cells': 8, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_mem', 'cpu/u_id']}\nhyp-20261003-003-r12s2 predictor Forward fetched counter state to remove the BHT training read fitness= 203.56 fmax= 87.46 cycles= 4296444\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
