{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_13", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d.get('id') in ('hyp-20261002-002-r9s1','hyp-20261003-002-r10s1'):\n  h=d.get('hypothesis',{})\n  print(d['id'],d['title'])\n  print(h.get('hypothesis',h) if isinstance(h,dict) else h)\n  print('result:',{k:d.get(k) for k in ('fitness','fmax_mhz','cycles','lut4','ff','critical_path','implementation_notes')})\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261002-002-r9s1 Decouple predicted fetch with an independently written circular instruction queue\nReplace the live combinational IF/ID interface with a strict, two-entry\ncircular FIFO of accepted predicted fetch transactions. Each entry owns its PC,\ninstruction, predicted_taken and direct_target. Keep the existing\ninstruction-qualified 128-entry two-bit BHT, direct-JAL prediction,\nindexing, initialization and once-per-accepted-EX training. Prediction\nand next-PC calculation occur when a fetch is enqueued, never when its\ninstruction is dequeued. This is one structural change to frontend\nbuffering and pipeline elasticity; it adds no cache or new predictor.\n\nUse two stationary payload slots and one-bit registered head/tail\npointers. Write only the tail slot on a fetch-space/ready opportunity;\ndequeue advances the head pointer rather than copying a wide tail\npayload into a head register. A registered-head-selected mux exposes\nthe stored instruction. Separate payload writes from occupancy and\ncorrection control. Payload opportunity enables depend on imemReady,\nregistered capacity and raw issue-hold reasons, never on redirect or\nbranch operand comparison. Reset payloads fully, but let an inactive\nslot capture harmless data on a correction edge; occupancy/pointers\nflush and PC redirect, so that data is never admitted or retired.\nCorrection only co