{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_47", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d.get('id')=='hyp-20261002-002-r8s1': print(d['hypothesis']['hypothesis'])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "Move control-flow correction and branch-predictor training from advancing\nEX to acceptance of the existing EX/MEM transaction in MEM. EX still\ncomputes conditional-branch direction, JAL/JALR destinations, alignment\nfaults and architectural next-PC, but registers the correction-needed bit,\ncorrection target, branch update enable/index and actual outcome alongside\nthat instruction in EX/MEM. Fetch, decode squash and BHT writes consume\nonly these registered records. This is one structural change to the\ncontrol-transfer resolution boundary, not a new predictor or another\nmultiply pipeline. Retain the present two-bit direction predictor, its\nindexing and reset state, direct-JAL prediction, fetch topology, ordinary\nALU latency, existing operand forwarding, and blocking RV32M units.\n\nA valid accepted EX/MEM control transfer emits its recovery and training\nevent exactly once. Use MEM acceptance, not merely occupancy; an older\ndmem hold cannot replay an event or let it overtake an older transaction.\nCompute the saved mismatch with the current direction-XOR policy: actual\nnonsequential execution is legal, aligned taken branch or legal aligned\njump; a mismatch also restores sequential execution after a misaligned\npredicted target. Carry the correct architectural pc_next and final trap\ncontrols for RVFI independently of whether a redirect is necessary.\nPredictor training uses the current counter at the saved branch index,\npreserving saturation and updating only a legal aligned conditional branch.\n\nOn registered MEM correction, redirect PC and squash both younger slots:\nthe current ID/EX instruction and the raw fetched instruction. Suppress\nthat younger EX instruction's EX/MEM advance, bypass write enable,\nmultiplier/divider request, saved arithmetic payload capture, and any\nbranch record. Insert an invalid EX/MEM bubble with every side-effect\ncontrol cleared. Clear ID/EX controls, valid and prediction state; preserve\nthe champion's payload-hold/reset policy. Correction overrides load-use,\nimem unavailability and younger EX o\n…[1495 of 4567 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:3e2eb462c3a0a546]…\n\nload extraction, memory masks, trap-qualified writes, retirement order,\ndefault-illegal decoding, EBREAK-only SYSTEM legality, nret=1 and all IO.\n\nPredict a 12 percent fitness improvement with medium confidence: removing\nthe repeated branch-to-recovery-to-operand path should allow an appreciable\nFmax gain while only incorrect predictions pay the extra cycle. This is\nunmeasured. For example, at a three percent cycle increase, acceptance\nneeds more than approximately 101.1 MHz; 110 MHz at that cycle count would\nyield roughly 248.6 iterations/sec. The ordinary ALU-to-ID feedback may\nbecome the new limit, and delayed predictor updates or physical placement\nmay consume the gain. Evaluate final median Gowin Fmax and actual bracketed\ncycles against the 228.405 iterations/sec acceptance threshold. Run the\nunchanged formal and RVFI cosimulation gates, real arithmetic suites, and\nstalled canonical CoreMark CRC, UART, marker and OOB validation. No wrapper,\nbenchmark, evaluator, contract file or other core is changed.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_48", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport shutil\nbase=Path('/srv/hwebench/tmp/6b356b5e/1b6202c7')\nfor depth in (2,4):\n root=base/('fetch_registered_recovery'+str(depth))\n shutil.copytree(base/'fetch_circular4/rtl',root/'rtl',dirs_exist_ok=True)\n p=root/'rtl/if_stage.sv';s=p.read_text()\n if depth==2:\n  s=s.replace('slots_q [0:3]','slots_q [0:1]').replace('logic [1:0] read_q, write_q','logic [0:0] read_q, write_q').replace('logic [2:0] count_q','logic [1:0] count_q').replace(\\\"count_q < 3'd4\\\", \\\"count_q < 2'd2\\\").replace('i<4','i<2').replace(\\\"write_q + 2'd1\\\", \\\"write_q + 1'd1\\\").replace(\\\"read_q + 2'd1\\\", \\\"read_q + 1'd1\\\").replace(\\\"count_q + 3'd1\\\", \\\"count_q + 2'd1\\\").replace(\\\"count_q - 3'd1\\\", \\\"count_q - 2'd1\\\")\n p.write_text(s)\n p=root/'rtl/core_pkg.sv';s=p.read_text().replace('  // MEM/WB register payload', '  // MEM/WB register payload',1)\n s=s.replace('    logic        branch_taken;','    logic        correction_needed;\\\\n    logic        train_branch;\\\\n    logic        branch_taken;',1);p.write_text(s)\n p=root/'rtl/core.sv';s=p.read_text()\n s=s.replace('  logic        redirect;','  logic        ex_redirect_unused, ex_branch_update_unused, ex_branch_outcome_unused;\\\\n  logic [31:0] ex_redirect_target_unused;\\\\n  logic [6:0] ex_branch_index_unused;\\\\n  logic        redirect;',1)\n block=s.split('  ex_stage u_ex (',1)[1].split('  );',1)[0]\n new=block.replace('.reset           (reset),','.reset           (reset),\\\\n    .squash          (redirect),').replace('.redirect        (redirect)', '.redirect        (ex_redirect_unused)').replace('.redirect_target (redirect_target)', '.redirect_target (ex_redirect_target_unused)').replace('.branch_update   (branch_update)', '.branch_update   (ex_branch_update_unused)').replace('.branch_index    (branch_index)', '.branch_index    (ex_branch_