e measured 4,061,023 cycles, acceptance requires median Gowin Fmax\n  above 92.756 MHz; at the old two-entry cycle count it requires 93.875 MHz.\n  These are thresholds, not timing measurements. Require measured fitness above\n  228.405 iter/sec using canonical marker-bounded cycles and median vendor\n  Fmax. Run unchanged formal, real RV32M arithmetic, RVFI cosimulation and\n  CoreMark CRC/UART/OOB/marker checks; no evaluator or contract edits.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 8\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Add the dedicated registered issue head and four-slot stationary\n      backing ring, prediction metadata ownership, exact head/count/pointer\n      updates, direct registered head refill and simultaneous promotion/\n      enqueue. Separate ready-qualified fetch from issue holds and logical\n      correction from payload opportunities. Preserve BHT behavior and\n      reset; make fetch-PC advance correspond to accepted queue insertion.\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: |\n      Apply imemReady only to new fetch acceptance, and use buffered head\n      validity for ID admission. Expose raw issue holds independent of\n      redirect for queue payload movement. Preserve load-use bubbles,\n      arithmetic ownership, dmem precedence and correction squash priority.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
