{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_58","type":"agent_message","text":"Registering recovery removes the branch-to-fetch critical path, but those prototypes still fall short on timing. I’m setting aside the queue proposal and testing a different structural angle: a banked, replicated LUT-RAM register file, with per-register validity bits preserving zero reads after reset. This keeps the current pipeline latency and forwarding behavior."}}
