{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_65", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d.get('id') in ('hyp-20261003-001-r11s0','hyp-20261003-001-r10s0'):\n  print(d['id'],d['title'],d.get('fitness'))\n  print(d.get('hypothesis',{}))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261003-001-r10s0 Fuse immediate selection into the ID ALU-B forwarding mux 183.32\n{'motivation': \"The champion's limiting path runs from registered EX ALU operands through\\nthe ALU and forwarding back to the ID/EX ALU inputs. ID currently resolves\\na three-source rs2_value, forces x0, then selects immediate versus that\\nresult for alu_b. This serial selection adds another mux to a timed\\nrecurrence. Previous opcode recoding, predictor updates and the six-source\\ndirect EX result crossbar all regressed; the latter increased LUTs to\\n3,887. A smaller change confined to final ALU-B selection can remove one\\nserial mux while retaining the shared EX bypass and producer qualification.\\nA local experiment fusing both ALU-A and ALU-B selection passed the\\nexisting ID/pipeline suites but reached only 92.375 MHz median, below the\\n93.817 MHz champion. The proposed narrower ALU-B-only circuit avoids the\\nadditional AUIPC/ALU-A crossbar and its routing pressure.\\n\", 'hypothesis': 'Replace only the combinational source selection feeding reg_q.alu_b with\\na four-candidate mutually exclusive masked-OR mux. Derive its scalar\\nselects in parallel from dec_alu_src, fwd_rs2_sel and the raw rs2 address:\\n  immediate = dec_alu_src;\\n  ex = !dec_alu_src && rs2_addr != 0 && fwd_rs2_sel == 1;\\n  mem = !dec_alu_src && rs2_addr != 0 && fwd_rs2_sel == 2;\\n  rf = !dec_alu_src && rs2_addr != 0\\n       && fwd_rs2_sel != 1 && fwd_rs2_sel != 2.\\nCompute alu_b_value as the bitwise OR of imm masked by immediate,\\nfwd_ex_data masked by ex, fwd_mem_data masked by mem, and rs2_data masked\\nby rf. Capture this value into the existing ID/EX alu_b register on its\\nunchanged payload clock enable. Express the four masks directly so the\\nsource-mode gate can merge into source selection; do not select rs2_value\\nand then put a second full-width immediate mux after it.\\n\\nLeave rs2_value and its architectural rs2_val capture exactly unchanged\\nfor stores, branches, divider operands and RVFI. Leave ALU-A, AUIPC,\\nrs1_value, EX bypass data/destination/e\n…[9251 of 12323 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:b94251323ceeee6f]…\ntional branches\\nnever write registers. Symbolically compare original and factored\\nwrite/launch gates with arbitrary branch/jump alignment predicates.\\n'}, {'file': 'test/test_ex_stage.py', 'description': 'Retain every existing result, metadata, response-hold, x0, illegal\\nproducer, reset and bypass assertion. Check all eight legal M control\\nbundles, exact saved-control equivalence and the saved.valid ownership\\nimplication through launch, wait, held response, transfer and reset.\\nExercise both families, changing current inputs and dmem holds, and\\nrequire identical captured destinations, operands and acceptance.\\n'}, {'file': 'test/test_pipeline.py', 'description': 'Retain all existing tests and exact RVFI assertions. Cover illegal\\nencodings, taken/untaken misaligned branches, misaligned JAL/JALR,\\nM operations beside redirects and memory stalls, same-destination\\nproducers, x0, wrong-path suppression and reset cancellation. Require\\nidentical traps, operands, results, PCs/order and memory effects.\\n'}]}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
