{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_69","type":"agent_message","text":"The LUT-RAM register file preserves correctness and cycle count, but its timing is lower too. I’m checking one final frontend design: a two-entry fall-through queue that issues a ready fetch directly when empty. It retains stall buffering and avoids the mandatory refill cycle of the earlier registered queues."}}
