\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_id/reg_q.alu_a_20_s0\", \"slack_ns\": -8.801, \"arrival_ns\": 19.095, \"logic_cells\": 17, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_div\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_fwd\", \"cpu/u_id\"]}}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_79", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\nh={\n'id':'hyp-20261003-002-r13s1',\n'title':'Retime branch comparison leaves across the operand register boundary',\n'category':'structural',\n'motivation':'''The champion scores 218.36 iter/sec at 93.817 MHz and 4,296,444 timed CoreMark cycles. Prior structural successes registered resolved operands and isolated multiplication/division. r12s1 registered every execution result, increased cycles 19.71 percent and regressed fitness; r11s1 moved operand selection into EX and regressed sharply. r10s1's preparation of all add/sub/compare operations made accepted-load-to-preparation timing critical. These outcomes argue for a narrow register-boundary change that preserves ordinary arithmetic and instruction latency.\n\nConditional branches still compare registered 32-bit operands with native relational operators. Several recent reports expose 38-cell paths from rs2 through EX branch comparison into recovery, predictor updates and ID control. The earlier r4s0 balanced comparator gained 14.05 percent over its then-champion without changing cycles, but left the comparison entirely after the operand registers. This proposal instead moves only the two-bit comparison leaves before that existing boundary; it does not retime general arithmetic or add a stage.''',\n'hypothesis':'''Partition conditional-branch comparison across the existing ID/EX operand boundary. ID continues to resolve both architectural operands with current advancing-EX, completing-MEM and write-first-RF priority. For each of sixteen two-bit slices, compute unsigned equality and less-than from those exact resolved values and register the two one-bit flags alongside the original rs1_val/rs2_val. Each leaf depends on just four operand bits and fits a LUT4 truth table. Keep all original operand and ALU-input registers; never reconstruct architectural operands from comparison flags.\n\nEX combines the registered leaves in a balanced four-level tree. A node spanning a more-significant group H and less-significant group L produces equal = equal_H AND equal_L and less = less_H OR (equal_H AND less_L). Compose contiguous bit groups in their original significance order. The root gives full unsigned less-than and equality. Signed less-than uses registered operand signs: if signs differ, use rs1's sign; otherwise use unsigned less-than. BEQ/BNE use equality/inverse, BLT/BGE use signed less-than/inverse, and BLTU/BGEU use unsigned less-than/inverse. No 32-bit branch subtractor or relational operator should remain in the core's branch-resolution cone. Leave ALU SLT/SLTU and ADD/SUB/address/JALR arithmetic unchanged.\n\nThis is one structural retiming of conditional-branch execution across an existing register boundary. There is no new pipeline stage, instruction buffer, cache, predictor policy, register-file change or additional execution bubble. Fetch prediction, direct targets, EX correction latency and once-per-accepted-EX BHT training stay as in the champion. The balanced combine alone is not the hypothesis: the important boundary is the newly registered, bit-local comparison information.\n\nCapture comparison leaves with exactly the same payload reset, advance and hold enable as their owning resolved operands. Full reset clears the new fields. On load-use, arithmetic occupancy or dmem holds, retain the instruction's leaves together with its operand values. Flush/invalid admission keeps the existing full ctrl/valid/prediction squash; stale leaves in an invalid payload cannot cause a branch, redirect, predictor update or side effect. A dependent branch after a load must capture the accepted sign/zero-extended MEM load value, not its address or an unaccepted bus word. Back-to-back branches and same-destination writers must use their own freshest operand pair; x0 leaves reflect hardwired zero.\n\nPreserve actual_nonsequential and direction-XOR recovery, saved direct targets, all six branch encodings, taken-target alignment traps, untaken misaligned-target behavior, JAL/JALR link and alignment semantics and complete RVFI operand/PC/trap reporting. Keep nret=1 and the exact top-level ports, decoder default-illegal validated matching and EBREAK-only SYSTEM legality. Keep all real RV32M and RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS arithmetic, launch-once/held-response ownership, memory alignment/masks/handshakes, architectural reset, side-effect-free bubbles and strictly consecutive channel-zero retirement orders.\n\nPredict eight percent higher fitness with low confidence, at unchanged canonical CoreMark cycles. The likely gain is removing the long post-register branch carry chain and the resulting recovery/control timing recurrence. The risk is moving one additional leaf LUT after ID forwarding: accepted-load or ALU-result-to-leaf capture can become critical, and the added 32 flops/tree routing can erase the improvement. Unlike r10s1, no propagate/generate preparation is added to ordinary arithmetic, and unlike r12s1, no dependency or correction cycle is added. This is a prediction, not a claim of measured improvement.\n\nRequire the unchanged formal and stalled RVFI/cosimulation gates and canonical CoreMark CRC/UART/OOB/MMIO-marker checks. Verify the leaf/tree comparison against native signed/unsigned comparison for arbitrary operands, in addition to directed operand-boundary tests. At 4,296,444 timed cycles, acceptance requires median Gowin Fmax above 98.133 MHz and fitness above 228.405 iter/sec. Measure actual cycles and all three vendor placement options; fewer comparator cells alone cannot establish success.''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':8,'confidence':'low'},\n'changes':[\n{'file':'rtl/core_pkg.sv','description':'Add sixteen equality and sixteen unsigned-less-than flags to the ID/EX payload. Retain original resolved operands, final ALU inputs, controls, prediction metadata and all downstream architectural meanings. No IO or retirement-width change.'},\n{'file':'rtl/id_stage.sv','description':'Compute two-bit equality/less-than leaves from the exact bypass-resolved rs1_value/rs2_value pair and capture them with the owning operands under existing full reset, payload advance and hold rules. Preserve forwarding selection and control-only squash; add no arithmetic carry preparation or operand-selection stage.'},\n{'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'Replace native full-width conditional-branch comparison with a balanced ordered reduction of registered leaves, followed by sign correction from registered source signs and funct3 selection. Preserve original ALU/M execution, branch/jump legality and alignment traps, recovery/training acceptance, bypass eligibility and architectural/RVFI payloads.'},\n{'file':'test/test_id_stage.py','description':'Extend bundle layouts and retain every existing assertion. Check leaf capture against resolved operands for EX/MEM/RF selection, x0, source aliasing, accepted byte/halfword loads, reset, holds and squash. Verify that flags belong to the same operand pair across changing bypass candidates.'},\n{'file':'test/test_ex_stage.py','description':'Adapt branch stimuli and bundle layouts to include matching comparison leaves. Retain all existing ALU/link/store/trap/RVFI assertions. Exhaustively verify two-bit leaves and symbolically verify balanced unsigned/signed comparison for arbitrary 32-bit operands; cover sign boundaries, equality, each bit significance and all six branch conditions.'},\n{'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'Extend packed layouts without weakening metadata, reset, hold, control-squash, RVFI/order or memory checks. Exercise ALU-to-branch, accepted-load-to-branch, back-to-back branches, duplicate destination writers, x0, signed/unsigned boundary comparisons, prediction corrections and alignment traps under independent bus stalls. Require unchanged instruction scheduling and canonical CoreMark cycles.'}\n]}\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-002-r13s1.yaml')\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(h,sort_keys=False,width=90,allow_unicode=True))\njsonschema.validate(yaml.safe_load(p.read_text()),json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Rewritten final structural hypothesis; schema validation passed.')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
