{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_9", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n 'WB|write.first|register.file|commit|retire|reg_file' cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py cores/bench/test/test_reg_file.py cores/bench/test/test_id_stage.py CLAUDE.md\"", "aggregated_output": "CLAUDE.md:11:| 1 | Top module `core` exposes an RVFI port set selected by `cores/<target>/core.yaml`'s `nret` field (default 2). **nret=1**: only `io_rvfi_*_0` ports exist; the single retirement always lands on channel 0. **nret=2**: both `io_rvfi_*_0` and `io_rvfi_*_1` exist; channel 0 carries the older of two simultaneous retirements, channel 1 the younger; single-retire cycles MUST place the retirement on channel 0 with `io_rvfi_valid_1 = 0`; all channel-1 ports MUST be driven (no X/Z, tie unused fields to `'0`). | cocotb smoke test, `riscv-formal` wrapper (`wrapper.sv` for nret=2, `wrapper_si.sv` for nret=1) |\nCLAUDE.md:14:| 4 | `rvfi_order` strictly monotonic +1 per retirement across both channels combined (no gaps, no duplicates). When both channels retire in the same cycle, channel-0 order = N and channel-1 order = N+1.                                       | `riscv-formal unique` check                  |\nCLAUDE.md:81:- Change `core`'s top-level IO shape relative to the `nret` value declared in `core.yaml` — specifically: the imem/dmem port set, and the RVFI port set (only `_0` fields for `nret: 1`; both `_0` and `_1` for `nret: 2` with channel-0-older convention and the single-retire-on-channel-0 rule).\nCLAUDE.md:95:Cores declare their retirement width in `cores/<TARGET>/core.yaml`\nCLAUDE.md:105:  single-retire pipeline.\nCLAUDE.md:137:but whose channel 1 silently never retires would also vacuous-pass\nCLAUDE.md:157:  2. cosim against `test/cosim/reference.py` (each retired MUL/DIV/REM\ncores/bench/test/test_reg_file.py:1:\"\"\"Unit tests for rtl/reg_file.sv. Covers x0 hardwiring, write-first\ncores/bench/test/test_reg_file.py:70:async def write_first_by