{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_7", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n '\\\"category\\\":\\\\s*\\\"structural\\\"|r12s1|r14s1|r3s1|r2s1|r4s1' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "3:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261002-002-r1s1\", \"title\": \"Move division out of the single-cycle execute path\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The only recorded bench experiment is the baseline: 5.442 MHz with a\\n199.837 ns worst path spanning forwarding, EX, and the combinational ALU\\nthrough 156 cells. There are no previous structural attempts or recorded\\nlessons. The ALU implements signed and unsigned divide and remainder with\\ncombinational / and % operators. These unrolled arithmetic networks remain\\nin the timed result-selection cone even when an ordinary RV32I instruction\\nexecutes. Moving this rare, deep operation behind registers offers much\\nmore timing headroom than improving an individual forwarding mux.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The only recorded bench experiment is the baseline: 5.442 MHz with a\\n199.837 ns worst path spanning forwarding, EX, and the combinational ALU\\nthrough 156 cells. There are no previous structural attempts or recorded\\nlessons. The ALU implements signed and unsigned divide and remainder with\\ncombinational / and % operators. These unrolled arithmetic networks remain\\nin the timed result-selection cone even when an ordinary RV32I instruction\\nexecutes. Moving this rare, deep operation behind registers offers much\\nmore timing headroom than improving an individual forwarding mux.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace all four combinational DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU paths with one shared,\\nblocking, iterative divider connected to EX. Keep RV32I execution and\\nmultiplication on their existing single-cycle paths. The divider captures\\nthe fully forwarded operands and operation exactly once, converts signed\\noperands to unsigned magnitudes, and performs one radix-2 restoring\\ndivision step per cycle using a registered partial remainder, quotient,\\ndivisor, and a bounded counter. Share the magnitude datapath between signed\\nand unsigned operations and between quotient and remainder; register sign\\ncorrection before presenting the result. A normal division takes about\\n34-35 cycles including prepara\n…[193012 of 196084 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:17dcd3d6f99ae699]…\ningle-channel wrapper/config. The initial run had 52 passes and pc_fwd_ch0 failed: its trace showed a nonempty queue returning zero PC/instruction because Yosys treated the struct array as one packed word. First fix changed to a vector array sized by $bits(if_id_t), but that frontend rejects $bits(type) with a syntax error. Second fix uses the preserved bundle's explicit 98-bit width; a direct Yosys frontend/proc/check run now recognizes the slots as memory and reports zero problems. The final full run passed, including pc_fwd_ch0 and reg_ch0. No wrapper, config or check has been edited.\\n\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-03T02:32:04.839627Z\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 14, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-10-03 hyp-20261003-002-r14s1 (regression, +1.58%): A four-entry circular fetch queue with empty fall-through overlaps fetch with ID holds and avoids correction-refill bubbles, but frontend elasticity must preserve decode/operand timing: 7.05% fewer CoreMark cycles were mostly offset by median Fmax falling from 93.817 to 88.583 MHz.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
