{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_9", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d.get('category') == 'structural':\n  print(json.dumps({k:d.get(k) for k in ('id','title','outcome','fitness','delta_pct','fmax_mhz','cycles','critical_path')},indent=2))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "{\n  \"id\": \"hyp-20261002-002-r1s1\",\n  \"title\": \"Move division out of the single-cycle execute path\",\n  \"outcome\": \"improvement\",\n  \"fitness\": 101.21,\n  \"delta_pct\": 735.07,\n  \"fmax_mhz\": 45.46,\n  \"cycles\": 4491817,\n  \"critical_path\": {\n    \"from\": \"cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s0\",\n    \"to\": \"cpu/u_id/id_ex_w.rs2_val_9_s1\",\n    \"slack_ns\": -17.306,\n    \"arrival_ns\": 27.6,\n    \"logic_cells\": 47,\n    \"modules\": [\n      \"clock_ibuf\",\n      \"cpu/u_id\",\n      \"cpu/u_ex\",\n      \"cpu/u_if\",\n      \"cpu/u_hazard\",\n      \"cpu/u_id\"\n    ]\n  }\n}\n{\n  \"id\": \"hyp-20261002-002-r2s1\",\n  \"title\": \"Register the fetch-to-decode boundary to break redirect feedback\",\n  \"outcome\": \"regression\",\n  \"fitness\": 108.75,\n  \"delta_pct\": 7.45,\n  \"fmax_mhz\": 52.0,\n  \"cycles\": 4781572,\n  \"critical_path\": {\n    \"from\": \"cpu/u_mem/reg_q.rd_3_s0\",\n    \"to\": \"dmem_1_dmem_1_0_0_s\",\n    \"slack_ns\": -14.261,\n    \"arrival_ns\": 24.556,\n    \"logic_cells\": 14,\n    \"modules\": [\n      \"clock_ibuf\",\n      \"cpu/u_fwd\",\n      \"cpu/u_ex\",\n      \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\",\n      \"cpu/u_ex\"\n    ]\n  }\n}\n{\n  \"id\": \"hyp-20261002-002-r3s1\",\n  \"title\": \"Register fully bypassed operands before execute\",\n  \"outcome\": \"improvement\",\n  \"fitness\": 162.96,\n  \"delta_pct\": 41.7,\n  \"fmax_mhz\": 68.482,\n  \"cycles\": 4202272,\n  \"critical_path\": {\n    \"from\": \"cpu/u_id/reg_q.rs2_val_0_s0\",\n    \"to\": \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu/mult_5_s1\",\n    \"slack_ns\": -10.709,\n    \"arrival_ns\": 20.783,\n    \"logic_cells\": 39,\n    \"modules\": [\n      \"clock_ibuf\",\n      \"cpu/u_ex\",\n      \"cpu/u_id\"\n    ]\n  }\n}\n{\n  \"id\": \"hyp-20261002-002-r4s1\",\n  \"title\": \"Register multiply completion outside the ordinary EX bypass path\",\n  \"outcome\": \"improvement\",\n  \"fitness\": 207.55,\n  \"delta_pct\": 27.36,\n  \"fmax_mhz\": 89.174,\n  \"cycles\": 4296444,\n  \"critical_path\": {\n    \"from\": \"cpu/u_id/reg_q.ctrl.alu_op_4_s0\",\n    \"to\": \"cpu/u_id/reg_q.alu_a_5_s0\",\n    \"slack_ns\": -7.045,\n    \"arrival_ns\": 17.339,\n    \"logic_cells\": 11,\n    \"modules\": [\n      \"clock_ibuf\",\n      \"cpu/u_ex/u_mul\",\n      \"cpu/u_ex\",\n      \"cpu/u_fwd\",\n      \"cpu/u_id\"\n    \n…[3987 of 7059 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:62e86f8c0c546744]…\n\n}\n{\n  \"id\": \"hyp-20261003-002-r13s1\",\n  \"title\": \"Retime branch comparison leaves across the operand register boundary\",\n  \"outcome\": \"regression\",\n  \"fitness\": 181.87,\n  \"delta_pct\": -16.71,\n  \"fmax_mhz\": 78.139,\n  \"cycles\": 4296444,\n  \"critical_path\": {\n    \"from\": \"cpu/u_id/reg_q.ctrl.alu_op_1_s0\",\n    \"to\": \"cpu/u_id/reg_q.rs2_val_9_s0\",\n    \"slack_ns\": -7.431,\n    \"arrival_ns\": 17.725,\n    \"logic_cells\": 14,\n    \"modules\": [\n      \"clock_ibuf\",\n      \"cpu/u_ex\",\n      \"cpu/u_fwd\",\n      \"cpu/u_id\"\n    ]\n  }\n}\n{\n  \"id\": \"hyp-20261003-002-r14s1\",\n  \"title\": \"Hide fetch stalls with a fall-through instruction queue\",\n  \"outcome\": \"regression\",\n  \"fitness\": 221.81,\n  \"delta_pct\": 1.58,\n  \"fmax_mhz\": 88.583,\n  \"cycles\": 3993687,\n  \"critical_path\": {\n    \"from\": \"cpu/u_id/reg_q.rs2_val_0_s0\",\n    \"to\": \"cpu/u_id/reg_q.ctrl.reg_write_s0\",\n    \"slack_ns\": -8.659,\n    \"arrival_ns\": 18.953,\n    \"logic_cells\": 38,\n    \"modules\": [\n      \"clock_ibuf\",\n      \"cpu/u_ex\",\n      \"cpu/u_if\",\n      \"cpu/u_id\"\n    ]\n  }\n}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nwanted={'hyp-20261003-002-r12s1','hyp-20261002-002-r9s1','hyp-20261002-002-r7s1','hyp-20261002-002-r8s1','hyp-20261003-002-r10s1','hyp-20261003-002-r11s1'}\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d.get('id') in wanted:\n  print(d['id'],d['title'])\n  h=d.get('hypothesis')\n  print(h.get('hypothesis') if isinstance(h,dict) else h)\n  print('IMPLEMENTATION NOTES',d.get('implementation_notes'))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_10", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nwanted={'hyp-20261003-002-r12s1','hyp-20261002-002-r9s1','hyp-20261002-002-r7s1','hyp-20261002-002-r8s1','hyp-20261003-002-r10s1','hyp-20261003-002-r11s1'}\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d.get('id') in wanted:\n  print(d['id'],d['title'])\n  h=d.get('hypothesis')\n  print(h.get('hypothesis') if isinstance(h,dict) else h)\n  print('IMPLEMENTATION NOTES',d.get('implementation_notes'))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261002-002-r7s1 Pipeline full-width multiply completion with registered execution classes\nBuild a pipelined multiply completion lane whose register holds the full 64-bit architectural product, not the already selected 32-bit low/high result. Capture the product and high-half selection metadata on the same edge that an accepted EX multiply places its original instruction in EX/MEM. MEM owns the matching response, selects low or high product bits there, and uses that single selected architectural value for both completing-MEM forwarding and MEM/WB capture. Remove multiply from blocking EX occupancy and from the current EX bypass. This is one structural change to M-extension issue/completion ownership; preserve the ordinary RV32I pipeline, predictor, fetch topology and blocking divider.\n\nUnlike r5s1, move low/high product selection after the product register. Preserve the shared signed 33-by-33 multiplication and explicit 66-bit intermediate: sign-extend a only for MULH/MULHSU, sign-extend b only for MULH, and retain product[63:0]. MUL reads [31:0]; MULH/MULHU/MULHSU read [63:32]. Register the selection with the accepted transaction. Do not infer separate signed/unsigned multipliers or route a combinational product into younger operand capture. Upper intermediate bits 65:64 are redundant sign extension.\n\nRegister explicit is_multiply and is_divide bits in ID/EX from the validated decoder outputs. Use these bits consistently for EX occupancy, request launch, response routing, producer eligibility and dependency interlocks instead of comparing alu_op throughout the EX-to-ID control recurrence. Retain alu_op only where the arithmetic unit needs the exact operation. The class bits are part of instruction ownership and must clear with the entire control bundle on every bubble/squash and hold with operands during stalls. Derive them only from legal decoder results; preserve default-illegal decoding and every reserved-encoding trap. This predecoded scheduling is required in the final proposal; the partial full-produc\n…[29216 of 32288 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:4eb6ae4fdff72c4b]…\ny\nyounger arithmetic ownership. Retain all real and ALTOPS formulas.\nReset every new ownership bit, and clear all side-effect controls in\ninvalid transactions. Preserve complete architectural reset, decoder\ndefault-illegal validation, EBREAK-only SYSTEM legality, alignment\ntraps, byte masks, nret=1 and the exact single-channel IO/RVFI contract.\n\nPredict twelve percent fitness improvement with low confidence. The\ncritical test is whether isolating EX arithmetic from ID forwarding\nraises median Gowin Fmax enough to pay for measured dependency and\ncorrection bubbles. At a hypothetical 20 percent cycle increase,\nacceptance requires Fmax above approximately 117.76 MHz; this is a\nbreak-even calculation, not a timing measurement. Run the unchanged\nformal/cosimulation gates and canonical CRC/UART/OOB/marker checks,\nthen compare actual CoreMark cycles times median Gowin Fmax against\nthe 228.405 iter/sec acceptance floor. Do not infer success from\nfewer logic levels or a single placement result.\n\nIMPLEMENTATION NOTES \n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"agent_message","text":"The history shows two useful limits: a result stage raised Fmax but added 19.7% to CoreMark cycles, while fetch buffering cut cycles by 7.05% but lost much of that gain to timing. I’m looking for a structural change that shortens the dependency path with a smaller throughput cost."}}
