{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_3", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"cat schemas/hypothesis.schema.json cores/bench/LESSONS.md && rg -n 'predictor|hyp-20261002-003-r8s2|hyp-20261002-001-r9s0|hyp-20261002-003-r9s2' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"required\": [\"id\",\"title\",\"category\",\"motivation\",\"hypothesis\",\"expected_impact\",\"changes\"],\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"id\":       {\"type\": \"string\", \"pattern\": \"^hyp-[0-9]{8}-[0-9]{3}(-r[0-9]+s[0-9]+)?$\"},\n    \"title\":    {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 5},\n    \"category\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"micro_opt\",\"structural\",\"extension\",\"predictor\",\"memory\"]},\n    \"motivation\":  {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 20},\n    \"hypothesis\":  {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 20},\n    \"expected_impact\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"required\": [\"fitness_delta_pct\",\"confidence\"],\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"fitness_delta_pct\": {\"type\": \"integer\"},\n        \"confidence\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"low\",\"medium\",\"high\"]}\n      }\n    },\n    \"changes\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\", \"minItems\": 1,\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"required\": [\"file\",\"description\"],\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"file\":        {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"description\": \"Must be under rtl/ (any extension) or be a test/test_*.py cocotb suite. Anything else is rejected by the runtime sandbox check.\",\n            \"pattern\": \"^(rtl/[^.].*|test/test_[^/]+\\\\.py)$\"\n          },\n          \"description\": {\"type\": \"string\"}\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n- 2026-10-02 hyp-20261002-002-r1s1 (improvement, +735.07%): Moving combinational DIV/REM (`/` and `%`) out of the shared ALU into a registered iterative divider removes their timing cost from ordinary instructions, letting Fmax gains outweigh CoreMark's added divide stalls.\n- 2026-10-02 hyp-20261002-002-r2s1 (regression, +7.45%): Registering elastic IF/ID removes redirect-to-decode feedback, but the added taken-branch refill cycle raised CoreMark cycles 6.45%, limiting a 14.39% Fmax gain to 7.45% fitness.\n- 2026-10-02 hyp-20261002-003-r2s2 (improvement, +13.63%): Instruction-qualified BHT/JAL prediction removes recurring CoreMark control bubbles, while saved direct targets enable direction-XOR \n…[237314 of 240386 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:197f0e4db39479dc]…\ndelta_pct\": -12.68, \"vs_baseline\": 1473.18, \"fmax_mhz\": 81.919, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4296444, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 3470, \"ff\": 971, \"seeds\": [81.45, 81.919, 81.919], \"perturbations\": [[0, 81.45, 11], [1, 81.919, 11], [2, 81.919, 11]], \"lutram\": 56, \"bsram\": 4, \"dsp\": 2, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_id/reg_q.ctrl.alu_op_0_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_id/reg_q.rs2_val_17_s0\", \"slack_ns\": -7.277, \"arrival_ns\": 17.572, \"logic_cells\": 11, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_fwd\", \"cpu/u_id\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 11, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-02T22:18:40.749604Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 9, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-10-03 hyp-20261002-003-r9s2 (regression, -12.68%): Registering BHT training with four 32-row validity-reset LUT-RAM banks shifts the timing limit to ID/EX ALU control through EX forwarding into ID operands, so area savings alone cannot prevent Fmax falling from 93.817 to 81.919 MHz at unchanged CoreMark cycles.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
