{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_9", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nids={'hyp-20261002-001-r4s0','hyp-20261002-002-r8s1','hyp-20261002-001-r9s0','hyp-20261002-003-r5s2'}\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d['id'] in ids:\n  h=d['hypothesis'] if isinstance(d['hypothesis'],dict) else d\n  print(d['id'],d['title'])\n  print('critical:',d.get('critical_path'))\n  print('proposal:',h.get('hypothesis',''))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261002-001-r4s0 Balance branch comparison logic to shorten EX recovery\ncritical: {'from': 'cpu/u_id/reg_q.alu_b_0_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu/mul_ss_63_s0', 'slack_ns': -7.483, 'arrival_ns': 17.557, 'logic_cells': 39, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_id']}\nproposal: Replace the EX branch unit's wide relational operators with an explicitly\nbalanced comparison tree suited to four-input FPGA LUTs. Preserve the\npipeline boundaries, predictor, exact branch outcomes and all instruction\nlatencies. This is a local Boolean implementation change to comparison,\nintended to raise Fmax while preserving CoreMark iterations per cycle.\n\nCompute equality and unsigned less-than for sixteen independent two-bit\nslices of the registered rs1/rs2 operands. Each leaf has four operand\ninputs. Combine adjacent low/high groups in four balanced levels using\neq = eq_high & eq_low and\nlt = lt_high | (eq_high & lt_low).\nReproduce the measured prototype with packed 31-bit eq/lt node vectors:\nleaves occupy indices 15+i for operand slice [2*i +: 2], i=0..15;\ninternal node n=0..14 combines high child 2*n+2 and low child 2*n+1.\nNode zero is the root. This layout keeps the most significant operand\nslices on each group's high child.\nThe root supplies whole-word equality and unsigned less-than. Derive\nsigned less-than as (rs1[31] ^ rs2[31]) ? rs1[31] : unsigned_less.\nUse these shared facts for BEQ/BNE, BLT/BGE and BLTU/BGEU, complementing\nonly the matching legal predicate; retain false for unsupported branch\nfunct3 values. Express the tree with static generate indices or explicit\nlevels so synthesis sees bounded local comparisons rather than a new\n32-bit ripple comparator. Do not replace comparison with a full-width\nsubtractor whose carry propagation recreates the long path.\n\nKeep target alignment faults, branch training on actual acceptance,\ndirection-XOR correction, EX/MEM and ID/EX hold/flush priorities,\nbypass producer validity, divider protocol and RVFI metadata intact.\nPreserve nret=1, decoder default-illegal b\n…[11912 of 14984 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:0acc311afe67e337]…\nation, architectural operand\ncapture, trap-qualified side effects, memory handshakes, consecutive RVFI\norder and all hard invariants. Prove each local transition matches the\noriginal saturating update for all four states and both outcomes, then\ncheck table hold, reset, aliasing and accepted-event behavior in fetch and\npipeline tests. Retain every existing test assertion.\n\nExpect eight percent greater fitness through lower logic and routing cost,\nwith low confidence because ALU and load forwarding remain competing\nlimits. Require unchanged 4,296,444 canonical marker-bounded cycles and\nexact prediction traces for identical branch events. Acceptance requires\nmore than 228.40456 iterations/sec, approximately 98.133 MHz median Fmax\nat that cycle count. Run all three canonical Gowin placement options and\nthe unchanged formal, stalled RVFI cosimulation, real arithmetic and\ncanonical CoreMark CRC/UART/MMIO/bracket/bounded-memory gates. Prototype\ntiming is preliminary and does not replace those implementation gates.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
