{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_3", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n '\\\"category\\\"\\\\s*:\\\\s*\\\"predictor\\\"|hyp-20261002-003-r[234679]s2|hyp-20261003-003-r10s2' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "4:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261002-003-r1s2\", \"title\": \"Small tagged target predictor eliminates recurrent control-flow bubbles\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The baseline always fetches pc+4 and redirects in EX for every taken\\nconditional branch, JAL, or JALR. Since IF/ID is combinational rather\\nthan a separate register, each redirect discards one younger instruction\\nand inserts a bubble. CoreMark repeatedly executes loops and stable\\ndirect jumps, so many of these bubbles should be predictable. The sole\\nrecorded experiment has 4,491,485 measured cycles and 5.442 MHz median\\nFmax. Its critical path runs through forwarding and the combinational\\narithmetic unit, so this proposal targets iterations per cycle while\\nkeeping predictor logic small enough to avoid reducing Fmax. There are\\nno recorded predictor experiments or LESSONS.md takeaways in this fixture.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The baseline always fetches pc+4 and redirects in EX for every taken\\nconditional branch, JAL, or JALR. Since IF/ID is combinational rather\\nthan a separate register, each redirect discards one younger instruction\\nand inserts a bubble. CoreMark repeatedly executes loops and stable\\ndirect jumps, so many of these bubbles should be predictable. The sole\\nrecorded experiment has 4,491,485 measured cycles and 5.442 MHz median\\nFmax. Its critical path runs through forwarding and the combinational\\narithmetic unit, so this proposal targets iterations per cycle while\\nkeeping predictor logic small enough to avoid reducing Fmax. There are\\nno recorded predictor experiments or LESSONS.md takeaways in this fixture.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a 64-entry direct-mapped branch target buffer with an integrated\\ntwo-bit saturating direction counter. Index with fetch PC[7:2]; retain\\nthe full PC[31:8] tag, a word-aligned 30-bit target, a conditional versus\\nunconditional type bit, and a valid bit. A matching unconditional entry\\npredicts its cached target; a conditional entry predicts that target\\nwhen the counter MSB is set. A miss or not-ta\n…[99219 of 102291 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:f4cbfa9fa6dc56bb]…\nycle.\\nExercise recovery with imem stalls, after older dmem holds, around\\nload-use bubbles and adjacent blocking M instructions. Retain exact\\nRVFI PC, next-PC, result, trap and order checks and wrong-path store\\nsuppression; verify no extra recovery cycle or repeated training.\\n\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 209.66, \"delta_pct\": -3.98, \"vs_baseline\": 1629.87, \"fmax_mhz\": 90.078, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4296444, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 3740, \"ff\": 1092, \"seeds\": [83.653, 90.078, 90.078], \"perturbations\": [[0, 83.653, 13], [1, 90.078, 10], [2, 90.078, 10]], \"lutram\": 40, \"bsram\": 4, \"dsp\": 2, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_id/reg_q.rs2_val_0_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_if/counters_counters_RAMREG_1_G[43]_s0\", \"slack_ns\": -6.954, \"arrival_ns\": 17.248, \"logic_cells\": 38, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_if\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 13, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-02T23:24:18.328789Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 10}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
