{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_4", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d.get('category')=='predictor' or d.get('id')=='hyp-20261002-003-r5s2':\n  print(json.dumps({k:d.get(k) for k in ['id','title','outcome','fitness','delta_pct','fmax_mhz','cycles','lut4','ff','critical_path']}, indent=2))\n  print('HYPOTHESIS:', d.get('hypothesis',{}).get('hypothesis',''))\n  print('NOTES:',d.get('implementation_notes',''))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "{\n  \"id\": \"hyp-20261002-003-r1s2\",\n  \"title\": \"Small tagged target predictor eliminates recurrent control-flow bubbles\",\n  \"outcome\": \"regression\",\n  \"fitness\": 13.02,\n  \"delta_pct\": 7.43,\n  \"fmax_mhz\": 5.467,\n  \"cycles\": 4197517,\n  \"lut4\": 12795,\n  \"ff\": 685,\n  \"critical_path\": {\n    \"from\": \"cpu/u_mem/reg_q.rd_1_s0\",\n    \"to\": \"dmem_1_dmem_1_0_0_s\",\n    \"slack_ns\": -187.719,\n    \"arrival_ns\": 198.013,\n    \"logic_cells\": 148,\n    \"modules\": [\n      \"clock_ibuf\",\n      \"cpu/u_rf\",\n      \"cpu/u_ex\",\n      \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\",\n      \"cpu/u_ex\"\n    ]\n  }\n}\nHYPOTHESIS: Add a 64-entry direct-mapped branch target buffer with an integrated\ntwo-bit saturating direction counter. Index with fetch PC[7:2]; retain\nthe full PC[31:8] tag, a word-aligned 30-bit target, a conditional versus\nunconditional type bit, and a valid bit. A matching unconditional entry\npredicts its cached target; a conditional entry predicts that target\nwhen the counter MSB is set. A miss or not-taken prediction chooses pc+4.\nInclude JAL and JALR in the same predictor, using the last resolved\ntarget for JALR, without adding a return stack or global history.\n\nCarry the exact predicted next PC alongside each accepted instruction\nthrough IF/ID and ID/EX. In EX compute the architectural next PC using\nthe existing forwarded operands, branch comparison, JALR bit-zero\nclearing, and misalignment/trap rules. Redirect and flush only when a\nvalid instruction advances out of EX and its actual next PC differs\nfrom its saved prediction. Check this equality for every instruction,\nincluding non-control and trapped instructions, so stale entries cannot\nsilently skip architectural instructions. RVFI pc_wdata always reports\nthe resolved next PC, never the prediction. Correctly predicted taken\ncontrol flow captures the target instruction normally without a bubble.\n\nTrain once per valid EX advance, never during dmem holds or bubbles.\nAllocate only decoded legal control-flow instructions with aligned\ntargets; initialize conditional counters to weakly taken or weakly\nnot-taken a\n…[46963 of 50035 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:82890301dbafe9c1]…\nrict RVFI order, all legality/alignment traps, operand\nforwarding and retention, memory handshakes and real/ALTOPS M arithmetic.\nChange only predictor state, metadata, target verification and its wiring.\n\nForecast six percent higher fitness with low confidence: removed return\nbubbles must outweigh the added top-read and JALR-target-check timing cost.\nThis is an unmeasured hypothesis, not a claimed benchmark improvement.\nAcceptance requires median Gowin Fmax_Hz times ten divided by marker-\nbounded CoreMark cycles greater than 228.40456 iterations/second. Validate\nempty/full stacks, overflow/underflow, nested calls using x1 and x5,\nconsecutive calls/returns, altered link-register values, illegal/misaligned\nJALR, reset, every bus/interlock hold and wrong-path calls/returns. Require\nexact RVFI PC/next-PC/results/traps/order and absence of wrong-path stores,\nunchanged formal/cosim gates, all five canonical CoreMark CRCs, validation\nliteral, bounded accesses and MMIO timing brackets before scoring timing.\n\nNOTES: \n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
