n actual acceptance,\ndirection-XOR correction, EX/MEM and ID/EX hold/flush priorities,\nbypass producer validity, divider protocol and RVFI metadata intact.\nPreserve nret=1, decoder default-illegal behavior and all correctness\nchecks. Validate all six branch conditions with equality, differing\nsigns and differences at every bit position, including misaligned\ntaken targets and independent instruction/data bus stalls. Run the\nunchanged formal and stalled CoreMark gates and inspect vendor timing\nto confirm the comparator/recovery path actually becomes shorter.\nExpected gain is 14 percent in fitness, supported by the local prototype\nrather than an extrapolation from the previous champion's circuit.\nThe prototype's new limiting paths cross ALU-result-to-ID forwarding;\nleave that separate opportunity for a later hypothesis. Full pipeline\nriscv-formal remains an implementation gate; the local SAT proof covers\ncomparator equivalence and does not replace that gate. Acceptance\nrequires fitness above 170.46, accounting for the 4.6 percent margin.\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
